d institutions reported a net income of $71. Updates on FDIC policy changes and upcoming conferences can be found in the FDIC's regular news updates, which include announcements, speeches, testimonies, and details on conferences and events."}, {"knowledge": [{"content": "EVENT / February 25, 2025\nFDIC-Insured Institutions Reported Return on Assets of 1.11 Percent and Net Inc\u2026", "wikipage": "AML Topic 21"}, {"content": "EVENT / September 05, 2024\nFDIC-Insured Institutions Reported Net Income of $71.5 Billion", "wikipage": "AML Topic 21"}, {"content": "The FDIC publishes regular updates on news and activities. Keep up with FDIC announcements, read speeches and testimony on the latest banking issues, learn about policy changes for banks, and get the details on upcoming conferences and events.", "wikipage": "AML Topic 21"}], "long_answer": "FDIC-insured institutions reported a return on assets of 1.11 percent on February 25, 2025.\n\nFDIC-insured institutions reported a net income of $71.5 billion on September 05, 2024.\n\nUpdates on FDIC policy changes and upcoming conferences can be found in the FDIC's regular news updates, which include announcements, speeches, testimonies, and details on conferences and events."}], "sample_id": "aml-topic-21-3", "question": "What is the return on assets reported by FDIC-insured institutions for February 25, 2025?", "docs": [{"id": "doc-aml-topic-21-3-1", "title": "AML Topic 21 Part 1", "text": "state banking performance data. Browse our extensive research tools and reports.\nMore FDIC Analysis\nCenter for Financial Research\nConsumer Research\nFDIC National Survey of Unbanked and Underbanked Households\nQuarterly Banking Profile\nFDIC Academic Challenge\nFDIC Banking Issues in Focus\nAnnual Risk Review\nEVENT / February 25, 2025\nFDIC-Insured Institutions Reported Return on Assets of 1.11 Percent and Net Inc\u2026\nEVENT / December 12, 2024\nFDIC-Insured Institutions Reported Net Income of $65.4 Billio", "score": 0.9, "summar