e found in their regular news updates, which include announcements, speeches, and testimonies on the latest banking issues. To stay informed about upcoming FDIC conferences and events, one can check the FDIC's announcements and news updates that provide details on such activities."}, {"knowledge": [{"content": "Quarterly Banking Profile\nFDIC-Insured Institutions Reported Return on Assets of 1.11 Percent and Net Inc\u2026", "wikipage": "AML Topic 22"}, {"content": "The FDIC publishes regular updates on news and activities. Keep up with FDIC announcements, read speeches and testimony on the latest banking issues, learn about policy changes for banks...", "wikipage": "AML Topic 22"}, {"content": "The FDIC publishes regular updates on news and activities. Keep up with FDIC announcements... and get the details on upcoming conferences and events.", "wikipage": "AML Topic 22"}], "long_answer": "The FDIC provides data on the performance of FDIC-insured institutions in its Quarterly Banking Profile, including metrics like net income and return on assets.\n\nUpdates on FDIC policy changes for banks can be found in their regular news updates, which include announcements, speeches, and testimonies on the latest banking issues.\n\nTo stay informed about upcoming FDIC conferences and events, one can check the FDIC's announcements and news updates that provide details on such activities."}], "sample_id": "aml-topic-22-3", "question": "What type of data does the FDIC provide in its Quarterly Banking Profile?", "docs": [{"id": "doc-aml-topic-22-3-1", "title": "AML Topic 22 Part 1", "text": "les, working papers, and state banking performance data. Browse our extensive research tools and reports.\nMore FDIC Analysis\nCenter for Financial Research\nConsumer Research\nFDIC National Survey of Unbanked and Underbanked Households\nQuarterly Banking Profile\nFDIC Academic Challenge\nFDIC Banking Issues in Focus\nAnnual Risk Review\nEVENT / February 25, 2025\nFDIC-Insured Institutions Repor