 "annotations": [{"knowledge": [], "long_answer": "The FDIC provides a wealth of resources for consumers, bankers, analysts, and other stakeholders, including financial education materials, data tools, documentation of laws and regulations, and information on important initiatives. The FDIC offers a Consumer Resource Center and a Banker Resource Center to assist these groups with relevant information and resources. The FDIC offers a Community Banking Research Program, which is part of its broader research initiatives."}, {"knowledge": [{"content": "The FDIC provides a wealth of resources for consumers, bankers, analysts, and other stakeholders. Browse our collection of financial education materials, data tools, documentation of laws and regulations, information on important initiatives, and more.", "wikipage": "AML Topic 23"}, {"content": "Additional FDIC Resources Consumer Resource Center Banker Resource Center", "wikipage": "AML Topic 23"}, {"content": "Community Banking Research Program", "wikipage": "AML Topic 23"}], "long_answer": "The FDIC provides a wealth of resources for consumers, bankers, analysts, and other stakeholders, including financial education materials, data tools, documentation of laws and regulations, and information on important initiatives.\n\nThe FDIC offers a Consumer Resource Center and a Banker Resource Center to assist these groups with relevant information and resources.\n\nThe FDIC offers a Community Banking Research Program, which is part of its broader research initiatives."}], "sample_id": "aml-topic-23-2", "question": "What resources does the FDIC offer to bankers and other stakeholders?", "docs": [{"id": "doc-aml-topic-23-2-1", "title": "AML Topic 23 Part 1", "text": "Bank, Des Plaines, Ill. Assumes All Deposits of Pulaski Savings\u2026\nPODCASTS / January 06, 2025\nSmall Business Lending\nResources\nToggle submenu\nResources\nThe FDIC provides a wealth of resources for consumers, bankers, analysts, and other stakeholders. Browse our collection of financial education materials, data tools, documentation of laws and regulations, information on important initiatives, and more.\nAdditional FDIC Resources\nConsumer Resource Center\nBanker Resource Center\nDeposit Insurance\nSupe", "score": 0.9, "summary": "Bank, Des Plaines, Ill. Assumes All Deposits of Pulaski Savings\u2026 PODCASTS / January 06, 2025 Small Business Lending Resources Toggle submenu Resources...", "extraction": "The FDIC provides a wealth of resources for consumers, bankers, analysts, and other stakeholders. Browse our collection of financial education materials, data tools, documentation of laws and regulations, information on important initiatives, and more."}], "answer": "The FDIC provides a wealth of resources for consumers, bankers, analysts, and other stakeholders, including financial education materials, data tools, documentation of laws and regulations, and information on important initiatives. The FDIC offers a Consumer Resource Center and a Banker Resource Center to assist these groups with relevant information and resources. The FDIC offers a Community Banking Research Program, which is part of its broader research initiatives.", "output": "Answer: The FDIC provides a wealth of resources for consumers, bankers, analysts, and other stakeholders [1].", "intermediate": ["[Retrieval]", "Answer: The FDIC provides a wealth of resources for consumers, bankers, analysts, and other stakeholders."]}, {"qa_pairs": [{"context": "No context provided", "question": "What type of research tools and reports does the FDIC provide for analyzing banking performance?", "short_answers": ["state banking performance data", "Quarterly Banking Profile", "Annual Risk Review"], "wikipage": null}, {"context": "No context provided", "question": "How does the FDIC disseminate news and updates about banking issues and policy changes?", "short_answers": ["regular announcements", "speeches and testimonies", "policy changes for banks"], "wikipage": null}, {"context": "No context provided", "question": "What kind of financial performance data does the FDIC report for insured institutions?", "short_answers": ["return on assets", "net income", "FDIC-insured institutions"], "wikipage": null}], "wikipages": [{"title": "AML Topic 23", "url": "https://www.fdic.gov/accessibility"}], "annotations": [{"knowledge": [], "long_answer": "The FDIC provides an array of research tools and reports including state banking performance data, the FDIC National Survey of Unbanked and Underbanked Households, the Quarterly Banking Profile, and the Annual Risk Review. The FDIC disseminates news and updates through regular announcements, speeches, testimonies, policy changes for banks, and details on upcoming conferences and events. The FDIC reports financial performance data such as the return on assets and net income of FDIC-insured institutions."}, {"knowledge": [{"content": "and state banking performance data. Browse our extensive research tools and reports. More FDIC Analysis Center for Financial Research Consumer Research FDIC National Survey of Unbanked and Underbanked Households Quarterly Banking Profile FDIC Academic Challenge FDIC Banking Issues in Focus Annual Risk Review", "wikipage": "AML Topic 23"}, {"content": "The FDIC publishes regular updates on news and activities. Keep up with FDIC announcements, read speeches and testimony on the latest banking issues, learn about policy changes for banks, and get the details on upcoming conferences and events. Find More FDIC News Press Releases Financial Institution Letters Conferences & Events", "wikipage": "AML Topic 23"}, {"content": "EVENT / February 25, 2025 FDIC-Insured Institutions Reported Return on Assets of 1.11 Percent and Net Inc\u2026 EVENT / December 12, 2024 FDIC-Insured Institutions Reported Net Income of $65.4 Billion EVENT / September 05, 2024 FDIC-Insured Institutions Reported Net Income of $71.5 Billion", "wikipage": "AML Topic 23"}], "long_answer": "The FDIC provides an array of research tools and reports including state banking performance data, the FDIC National Survey of Unbanked and Underbanked Households, the Quarterly Banking Profile, and the Annual Risk Review.\n\nThe FDIC disseminates news and updates through regular announcements, speeches, testimonies, policy changes for banks, and details on upcoming conferences and events. They also provide press releases, financial institution letters, and media campaigns.\n\nThe FDIC reports financial performance data such as the return on assets and net income of FDIC-insured institutions. For example, they reported a return on assets of 1.11 percent and net incomes of $65.4 billion and $71.5 billion in different periods."}], "sample_id": "aml-topic-23-3", "question": "What type of research tools and reports does the FDIC provide for analyzing banking performance?", "docs": [{"id": "doc-aml-topic-23-3-1", "title": "AML Topic 23 Part 1", "text": "and state banking performance data. Browse our extensive research tools and reports.\nMore FDIC Analysis\nCenter for Financial Research\nConsumer Research\nFDIC National Survey of Unbanked and Underbanked Households\nQuarterly Banking Profile\nFDIC Academic Challenge\nFDIC Banking Issues in Focus\nAnnual Risk Review\nEVENT / February 25, 2025\nFDIC-Insured Institutions Reported Return on Assets of 1.11 Percent and Net Inc\u2026\nEVENT / December 12, 2024\nFDIC-Insured Institutions Reported Net Income of $65.4 Bi", "score": 0.9, "summary": "and state banking performance data. Browse our extensive research tools and reports. More FDIC Analysis Center for Financial Research Consumer Researc...", "extraction": "and state banking performance data. Browse our extensive research tools and reports. More FDIC Analysis Center for Financial Research Consumer Research FDIC National Survey of Unbanked and Underbanked Households Quarterly Banking Profile FDIC Academic Challenge FDIC Banking Issues in Focus Annual Risk Review"}], "answer": "The FDIC provides an array of research tools and reports including state banking performance data, the FDIC National Survey of Unbanked and Underbanked Households, the Quarterly Banking Profile, and the Annual Risk Review. The FDIC disseminates news and updates through regular announcements, speeches, testimonies, policy changes for banks, and details on upcoming conferences and events. The FDIC reports financial performance data such as the return on assets and net income of FDIC-insured institutions.", "output": "Answer: The FDIC provides a variety of research tools and reports for analyzing banking performance, including the Quarterly Banking Profile, the FDIC National Survey of Unbanked and Underbanked Households, the FDIC Banking Issues in Focus, and the FDIC-Insured Institutions Report [1].", "intermediate": ["[Retrieval]", "Answer: The FDIC provides a variety of research tools and reports for analyzing banking performance, including the Quarterly Banking Profile, the FDIC National Survey of Unbanked and Underbanked Households, the FDIC Banking Issues in Focus, and the FDIC-Insured Institutions Report."]}, {"qa_pairs": [{"context": "No context provided", "question": "What types of resources does the FDIC provide for stakeholders such as bankers and consumers?", "short_answers": ["Financial education materials", "Data tools", "Laws and regulations documentation"], "wikipage": null}, {"context": "No context provided", "question": "Where can bankers find FDIC resources specifically tailored for them?", "short_answers": ["Banker Resource Center"], "wikipage": null}, {"context": "No context provided", "question": "What kind of research programs does the FDIC offer for community banking?", "short_answers": ["Community Banking Research Program"], "wikipage": null}], "wikipages": [{"title": "AML Topic 24", "url": "https://www.fdic.gov/open-government"}], "annotations": [{"knowledge": [], "long_answer": "The FDIC provides a variety of resources for stakeholders, including financial education materials, data tools, documentation of laws and regulations, information on important initiatives, and more. Bankers can find resources specifically tailored for them at the Banker Resource Center provided by the FDIC. The FDIC offers a Community Banking Research Program among its various resources."}, {"knowledge": [{"content": "The FDIC provides a wealth of resources for consumers, bankers, analysts, and other stakeholders. Browse our collection of financial education materials, data tools, documentation of laws and regulations, information on important initiatives, and more.", "wikipage": "AML Topic 24"}, {"content": "Additional FDIC Resources Consumer Resource Center Banker Resource Center", "wikipage": "AML Topic 24"}, {"content": "Community Banking Research Program", "wikipage": "AML Topic 24"}], "long_answer": "The FDIC provides a variety of resources for stakeholders, including financial education materials, data tools, documentation of laws and regulations, information on important initiatives, and more.\n\nBankers can find resources specifically tailored for them at the Banker Resource Center provided by the FDIC.\n\nThe FDIC offers a Community Banking Research Program among its various resources."}], "sample_id": "aml-topic-24-2", "question": "What types of resources does the FDIC provide for stakeholders such as bankers and consumers?", "docs": [{"id": "doc-aml-topic-24-2-1", "title": "AML Topic 24 Part 1", "text": "ines, Ill. Assumes All Deposits of Pulaski Savings\u2026\nPODCASTS / January 06, 2025\nSmall Business Lending\nResources\nToggle submenu\nResources\nThe FDIC provides a wealth of resources for consumers, bankers, analysts, and other stakeholders. Browse our collection of financial education materials, data tools, documentation of laws and regulations, information on important initiatives, and more.\nAdditional FDIC Resources\nConsumer Resource Center\nBanker Resource Center\nDeposit Insurance\nSupervision & Exa", "score": 0.9, "summary": "ines, Ill. Assumes All Deposits of Pulaski Savings\u2026 PODCASTS / January 06, 2025 Small Business Lending Resources Toggle submenu Resources The FDIC pro...", "extraction": "The FDIC provides a wealth of resources for consumers, bankers, analysts, and other stakeholders. Browse our collection of financial education materials, data tools, documentation of laws and regulations, information on important initiatives, and more."}], "answer": "The FDIC provides a variety of resources for stakeholders, including financial education materials, data tools, documentation of laws and regulations, information on important initiatives, and more. Bankers can find resources specifically tailored for them at the Banker Resource Center provided by the FDIC. The FDIC offers a Community Banking Research Program among its various resources.", "output": "Answer: The FDIC provides a wealth of resources for consumers, bankers, analysts, and other stakeholders [1].", "intermediate": ["[Retrieval]", "Answer: The FDIC provides a wealth of resources for consumers, bankers, analysts, and other stakeholders."]}, {"qa_pairs": [{"context": "No context provided", "question": "What resources does the FDIC provide for researching banking performance data?", "short_answers": ["Research tools and reports", "Quarterly Banking Profile", "Annual Risk Review"], "wikipage": null}, {"context": "No context provided", "question": "What recent events has the FDIC reported regarding the financial performance of insured institutions?", "short_answers": ["Return on assets of 1.11%", "Net income of $65.4 billion", "Net income of $71.5 billion"], "wikipage": null}, {"context": "No context provided", "question": "How does the FDIC keep the public informed about its activities and policy changes?", "short_answers": ["Regular updates", "Policy changes", "Conferences and events"], "wikipage": null}], "wikipages": [{"title": "AML Topic 24", "url": "https://www.fdic.gov/open-government"}], "annotations": [{"knowledge": [], "long_answer": "The FDIC offers extensive research tools and reports, including the Center for Financial Research, Consumer Research, the FDIC National Survey of Unbanked and Underbanked Households, the Quarterly Banking Profile, the FDIC Academic Challenge, FDIC Banking Issues in Focus, and the Annual Risk Review. Recent events reported by the FDIC include FDIC-insured institutions reporting a return on assets of 1. The FDIC keeps the public informed through regular updates on news and activities, including announcements, speeches, testimony on banking issues, policy changes for banks, and details on upcoming conferences and events."}, {"knowledge": [{"content": "nking performance data. Browse our extensive research tools and reports. More FDIC Analysis Center for Financial Research Consumer Research FDIC National Survey of Unbanked and Underbanked Households Quarterly Banking Profile FDIC Academic Challenge FDIC Banking Issues in Focus Annual Risk Review", "wikipage": "AML Topic 24"}, {"content": "EVENT / February 25, 2025 FDIC-Insured Institutions Reported Return on Assets of 1.11 Percent and Net Inc\u2026 EVENT / December 12, 2024 FDIC-Insured Institutions Reported Net Income of $65.4 Billion EVENT / September 05, 2024 FDIC-Insured Institutions Reported Net Income of $71.5 Billion", "wikipage": "AML Topic 24"}, {"content": "The FDIC publishes regular updates on news and activities. Keep up with FDIC announcements, read speeches and testimony on the latest banking issues, learn about policy changes for banks, and get the details on upcoming conferences and events.", "wikipage": "AML Topic 24"}], "long_answer": "The FDIC offers extensive research tools and reports, including the Center for Financial Research, Consumer Research, the FDIC National Survey of Unbanked and Underbanked Households, the Quarterly Banking Profile, the FDIC Academic Challenge, FDIC Banking Issues in Focus, and the Annual Risk Review.\n\nRecent events reported by the FDIC include FDIC-insured institutions reporting a return on assets of 1.11 percent on February 25, 2025, a net income of $65.4 billion on December 12, 2024, and a net income of $71.5 billion on September 5, 2024.\n\nThe FDIC keeps the public informed through regular updates on news and activities, including announcements, speeches, testimony on banking issues, policy changes for banks, and details on upcoming conferences and events."}], "sample_id": "aml-topic-24-3", "question": "What resources does the FDIC provide for researching banking performance data?", "docs": [{"id": "doc-aml-topic-24-3-1", "title": "AML Topic 24 Part 1", "text": "nking performance data. Browse our extensive research tools and reports.\nMore FDIC Analysis\nCenter for Financial Research\nConsumer Research\nFDIC National Survey of Unbanked and Underbanked Households\nQuarterly Banking Profile\nFDIC Academic Challenge\nFDIC Banking Issues in Focus\nAnnual Risk Review\nEVENT / February 25, 2025\nFDIC-Insured Institutions Reported Return on Assets of 1.11 Percent and Net Inc\u2026\nEVENT / December 12, 2024\nFDIC-Insured Institutions Reported Net Income of $65.4 Billion\nEVENT", "score": 0.9, "summary": "nking performance data. Browse our extensive research tools and reports. More FDIC Analysis Center for Financial Research Consumer Research FDIC Natio...", "extraction": "nking performance data. Browse our extensive research tools and reports. More FDIC Analysis Center for Financial Research Consumer Research FDIC National Survey of Unbanked and Underbanked Households Quarterly Banking Profile FDIC Academic Challenge FDIC Banking Issues in Focus Annual Risk Review"}], "answer": "The FDIC offers extensive research tools and reports, including the Center for Financial Research, Consumer Research, the FDIC National Survey of Unbanked and Underbanked Households, the Quarterly Banking Profile, the FDIC Academic Challenge, FDIC Banking Issues in Focus, and the Annual Risk Review. Recent events reported by the FDIC include FDIC-insured institutions reporting a return on assets of 1. The FDIC keeps the public informed through regular updates on news and activities, including announcements, speeches, testimony on banking issues, policy changes for banks, and details on upcoming conferences and events.", "output": "Answer: The FDIC provides resources for researching banking performance data, such as the FDIC National Survey of Unbanked and Underbanked Households, the Quarterly Banking Profile, and the FDIC Banking Issues in Focus [1].", "intermediate": ["[Retrieval]", "Answer: The FDIC provides resources for researching banking performance data, such as the FDIC National Survey of Unbanked and Underbanked Households, the Quarterly Banking Profile, and the FDIC Banking Issues in Focus."]}, {"qa_pairs": [{"context": "No context provided", "question": "What was the reported return on assets for FDIC-insured institutions in the February 25, 2025 report?", "short_answers": ["1.11 percent", "Return on assets"], "wikipage": null}, {"context": "No context provided", "question": "How much net income did FDIC-insured institutions report on September 05, 2024?", "short_answers": ["$71.5 billion", "Net income"], "wikipage": null}, {"context": "No context provided", "question": "When was the Quarterly Banking Profile for the first quarter of 2024 published?", "short_answers": ["May 29, 2024", "Quarterly Banking Profile"], "wikipage": null}], "wikipages": [{"title": "AML Topic 25", "url": "https://www.fdic.gov/about/privacy-program"}], "annotations": [{"knowledge": [], "long_answer": "In the February 25, 2025 report, FDIC-insured institutions reported a return on assets of 1. FDIC-insured institutions reported a net income of $71. The Quarterly Banking Profile for the first quarter of 2024 was published on May 29, 2024."}, {"knowledge": [{"content": "EVENT / February 25, 2025 FDIC-Insured Institutions Reported Return on Assets of 1.11 Percent and Net Inc\u2026", "wikipage": "AML Topic 25"}, {"content": "EVENT / September 05, 2024 FDIC-Insured Institutions Reported Net Income of $71.5 Billion", "wikipage": "AML Topic 25"}, {"content": "EVENT / May 29, 2024 Quarterly Banking Profile for First Quarter 2024", "wikipage": "AML Topic 25"}], "long_answer": "In the February 25, 2025 report, FDIC-insured institutions reported a return on assets of 1.11 percent.\n\nFDIC-insured institutions reported a net income of $71.5 billion on September 05, 2024.\n\nThe Quarterly Banking Profile for the first quarter of 2024 was published on May 29, 2024."}], "sample_id": "aml-topic-25-3", "question": "What was the reported return on assets for FDIC-insured institutions in the February 25, 2025 report?", "docs": [{"id": "doc-aml-topic-25-3-1", "title": "AML Topic 25 Part 1", "text": "nking performance data. Browse our extensive research tools and reports.\nMore FDIC Analysis\nCenter for Financial Research\nConsumer Research\nFDIC National Survey of Unbanked and Underbanked Households\nQuarterly Banking Profile\nFDIC Academic Challenge\nFDIC Banking Issues in Focus\nAnnual Risk Review\nEVENT / February 25, 2025\nFDIC-Insured Institutions Reported Return on Assets of 1.11 Percent and Net Inc\u2026\nEVENT / December 12, 2024\nFDIC-Insured Institutions Reported Net Income of $65.4 Billion\nEVENT", "score": 0.9, "summary": "nking performance data. Browse our extensive research tools and reports. More FDIC Analysis Center for Financial Research Consumer Research FDIC Natio...", "extraction": "EVENT / February 25, 2025 FDIC-Insured Institutions Reported Return on Assets of 1.11 Percent and Net Inc\u2026"}], "answer": "In the February 25, 2025 report, FDIC-insured institutions reported a return on assets of 1. FDIC-insured institutions reported a net income of $71. The Quarterly Banking Profile for the first quarter of 2024 was published on May 29, 2024.", "output": "According to the February 25, 2025 FDIC-Insured Institutions Report, the reported return on assets for FDIC-insured institutions was 1. 11 percent [1].", "intermediate": ["[Retrieval]", "According to the February 25, 2025 FDIC-Insured Institutions Report, the reported return on assets for FDIC-insured institutions was 1.11 percent."]}, {"qa_pairs": [{"context": "No context provided", "question": "What resources does the FDIC offer for consumers and bankers?", "short_answers": ["Financial education materials", "Data tools", "Laws and regulations documentation"], "wikipage": null}, {"context": "No context provided", "question": "Where can bankers find information on FDIC supervision and examinations?", "short_answers": ["Banker Resource Center", "Supervision & Examinations"], "wikipage": null}, {"context": "No context provided", "question": "What type of research does the FDIC conduct related to community banking?", "short_answers": ["Community Banking Research Program", "FDIC research"], "wikipage": null}], "wikipages": [{"title": "AML Topic 26", "url": "https://www.fdic.gov/about/plain-writing-act-2010"}], "annotations": [{"knowledge": [], "long_answer": "The FDIC provides a wealth of resources for consumers and bankers, including financial education materials, data tools, documentation of laws and regulations, and information on important initiatives. Bankers can find information on FDIC supervision and examinations in the Banker Resource Center provided by the FDIC. The FDIC conducts research related to community banking as part of its Community Banking Research Program."}, {"knowledge": [{"content": "The FDIC provides a wealth of resources for consumers, bankers, analysts, and other stakeholders. Browse our collection of financial education materials, data tools, documentation of laws and regulations, information on important initiatives, and more.", "wikipage": "AML Topic 26"}, {"content": "Additional FDIC Resources Consumer Resource Center Banker Resource Center Deposit Insurance Supervision & Examinations Laws & Regulations", "wikipage": "AML Topic 26"}, {"content": "Community Banking Research Program International Seminars and Training", "wikipage": "AML Topic 26"}], "long_answer": "The FDIC provides a wealth of resources for consumers and bankers, including financial education materials, data tools, documentation of laws and regulations, and information on important initiatives.\n\nBankers can find information on FDIC supervision and examinations in the Banker Resource Center provided by the FDIC.\n\nThe FDIC conducts research related to community banking as part of its Community Banking Research Program."}], "sample_id": "aml-topic-26-2", "question": "What resources does the FDIC offer for consumers and bankers?", "docs": [{"id": "doc-aml-topic-26-2-1", "title": "AML Topic 26 Part 1", "text": "k, Des Plaines, Ill. Assumes All Deposits of Pulaski Savings\u2026\nPODCASTS / January 06, 2025\nSmall Business Lending\nResources\nToggle submenu\nResources\nThe FDIC provides a wealth of resources for consumers, bankers, analysts, and other stakeholders. Browse our collection of financial education materials, data tools, documentation of laws and regulations, information on important initiatives, and more.\nAdditional FDIC Resources\nConsumer Resource Center\nBanker Resource Center\nDeposit Insurance\nSupervi", "score": 0.9, "summary": "k, Des Plaines, Ill. Assumes All Deposits of Pulaski Savings\u2026 PODCASTS / January 06, 2025 Small Business Lending Resources Toggle submenu Resources Th...", "extraction": "The FDIC provides a wealth of resources for consumers, bankers, analysts, and other stakeholders. Browse our collection of financial education materials, data tools, documentation of laws and regulations, information on important initiatives, and more."}], "answer": "The FDIC provides a wealth of resources for consumers and bankers, including financial education materials, data tools, documentation of laws and regulations, and information on important initiatives. Bankers can find information on FDIC supervision and examinations in the Banker Resource Center provided by the FDIC. The FDIC conducts research related to community banking as part of its Community Banking Research Program.", "output": "Answer: The FDIC provides a wealth of resources for consumers, bankers, analysts, and other stakeholders [1].", "intermediate": ["[Retrieval]", "Answer: The FDIC provides a wealth of resources for consumers, bankers, analysts, and other stakeholders."]}, {"qa_pairs": [{"context": "No context provided", "question": "What resources does the FDIC provide for bankers to enhance their understanding of financial regulations?", "short_answers": ["Banker Resource Center", "Financial education materials"], "wikipage": null}, {"context": "No context provided", "question": "How can consumers access information on deposit insurance through the FDIC?", "short_answers": ["Consumer Resource Center", "Deposit Insurance"], "wikipage": null}, {"context": "No context provided", "question": "What type of research programs does the FDIC offer to support community banking?", "short_answers": ["Community Banking Research Program", "Research initiatives"], "wikipage": null}], "wikipages": [{"title": "AML Topic 27", "url": "https://www.fdic.gov/about/no-fear-act"}], "annotations": [{"knowledge": [], "long_answer": "The FDIC provides a Banker Resource Center, which includes a collection of financial education materials, data tools, documentation of laws and regulations, and other important initiatives. Consumers can access information on deposit insurance through the FDIC's Consumer Resource Center, which is part of the additional resources provided by the FDIC. The FDIC offers a Community Banking Research Program as part of its resources to support community banking, which includes various research initiatives."}, {"knowledge": [{"content": "The FDIC provides a wealth of resources for consumers, bankers, analysts, and other stakeholders. Browse our collection of financial education materials, data tools, documentation of laws and regulations, information on important initiatives, and more.", "wikipage": "AML Topic 27"}, {"content": "Additional FDIC Resources Consumer Resource Center Deposit Insurance", "wikipage": "AML Topic 27"}, {"content": "Community Banking Research Program", "wikipage": "AML Topic 27"}], "long_answer": "The FDIC provides a Banker Resource Center, which includes a collection of financial education materials, data tools, documentation of laws and regulations, and other important initiatives.\n\nConsumers can access information on deposit insurance through the FDIC's Consumer Resource Center, which is part of the additional resources provided by the FDIC.\n\nThe FDIC offers a Community Banking Research Program as part of its resources to support community banking, which includes various research initiatives."}], "sample_id": "aml-topic-27-2", "question": "What resources does the FDIC provide for bankers to enhance their understanding of financial regulations?", "docs": [{"id": "doc-aml-topic-27-2-1", "title": "AML Topic 27 Part 1", "text": ", Ill. Assumes All Deposits of Pulaski Savings\u2026\nPODCASTS / January 06, 2025\nSmall Business Lending\nResources\nToggle submenu\nResources\nThe FDIC provides a wealth of resources for consumers, bankers, analysts, and other stakeholders. Browse our collection of financial education materials, data tools, documentation of laws and regulations, information on important initiatives, and more.\nAdditional FDIC Resources\nConsumer Resource Center\nBanker Resource Center\nDeposit Insurance\nSupervision & Examina", "score": 0.9, "summary": ", Ill. Assumes All Deposits of Pulaski Savings\u2026 PODCASTS / January 06, 2025 Small Business Lending Resources Toggle submenu Resources The FDIC provide...", "extraction": "The FDIC provides a wealth of resources for consumers, bankers, analysts, and other stakeholders. Browse our collection of financial education materials, data tools, documentation of laws and regulations, information on important initiatives, and more."}], "answer": "The FDIC provides a Banker Resource Center, which includes a collection of financial education materials, data tools, documentation of laws and regulations, and other important initiatives. Consumers can access information on deposit insurance through the FDIC's Consumer Resource Center, which is part of the additional resources provided by the FDIC. The FDIC offers a Community Banking Research Program as part of its resources to support community banking, which includes various research initiatives.", "output": "Answer: The FDIC provides a wealth of resources for consumers, bankers, analysts, and other stakeholders [1].", "intermediate": ["[Retrieval]", "Answer: The FDIC provides a wealth of resources for consumers, bankers, analysts, and other stakeholders."]}, {"qa_pairs": [{"context": "No context provided", "question": "What measures does the FDIC take to ensure the security of its official websites?", "short_answers": [".gov domain", "HTTPS security"], "wikipage": null}, {"context": "No context provided", "question": "What resources does the FDIC offer to consumers to help them make informed financial decisions?", "short_answers": ["news and resources", "educational tools"], "wikipage": null}, {"context": "No context provided", "question": "How does the FDIC support financial education for consumers?", "short_answers": ["financial education resources", "consumer protection"], "wikipage": null}], "wikipages": [{"title": "AML Topic 28", "url": "https://www.fdic.gov/espanol"}], "annotations": [{"knowledge": [], "long_answer": "The FDIC ensures the security of its official websites by using the . The FDIC provides news, resources, and educational tools to help consumers make smart decisions and protect their savings. The FDIC supports financial education by offering resources aimed at strengthening financial knowledge and protecting consumers."}, {"knowledge": [{"content": "Official websites use .gov  \nA .gov website belongs to an official organization of the United States Government.  \nSecure .gov websites use HTTPS  \nAn https:// means you have securely connected to a .gov website. Share sensitive information only on official and secure websites.", "wikipage": "AML Topic 28"}, {"content": "The FDIC provides news, resources, and educational tools to help consumers make smart decisions and protect their savings \u2014 including this website in Spanish.\n\nFinancial Education\n\nIn addition to insuring your deposits, the FDIC offers resources to strengthen financial education and protect consumers.", "wikipage": "AML Topic 28"}, {"content": "Financial Education\nIn addition to insuring deposits, the FDIC offers resources to strengthen financial education and protect consumers.", "wikipage": "AML Topic 28"}], "long_answer": "The FDIC ensures the security of its official websites by using the .gov domain, which indicates that the site belongs to an official U.S. Government organization. Additionally, secure .gov websites use HTTPS, which means the connection to the site is secure and sensitive information should only be shared on these official and secure sites.\n\nThe FDIC provides news, resources, and educational tools to help consumers make smart decisions and protect their savings. This includes offering financial education resources to strengthen consumer knowledge.\n\nThe FDIC supports financial education by offering resources aimed at strengthening financial knowledge and protecting consumers. This is part of their broader mission to ensure consumers can make informed decisions regarding their finances."}], "sample_id": "aml-topic-28-1", "question": "What measures does the FDIC take to ensure the security of its official websites?", "docs": [{"id": "doc-aml-topic-28-1-1", "title": "AML Topic 28 Part 1", "text": "Welcome to the FDIC | FDIC.gov\nSkip to main content\nAn official website of the United States government\nOfficial websites use .gov\nA .gov website belongs to an official organization of the United States Government.\nSecure .gov websites use HTTPS\nAn\nhttps://\nmeans you\u2019ve safely connected to a .gov website. Share sensitive information only on official, secure websites.\nSwitch to English\n|\nGlossary\nSearch FDIC.gov\nSearch\nFinancial Education\nInsurance", "score": 0.9, "summary": "Welcome to the FDIC | FDIC.gov\n\nSkip to main content\n\nAn official website of the United States government\n\nOfficial websites use .gov", "extraction": "Official websites use .gov  \nA .gov website belongs to an official organization of the United States Government.  \nSecure .gov websites use HTTPS  \nAn https:// means you have securely connected to a .gov website. Share sensitive information only on official and secure websites."}], "answer": "The FDIC ensures the security of its official websites by using the . The FDIC provides news, resources, and educational tools to help consumers make smart decisions and protect their savings. The FDIC supports financial education by offering resources aimed at strengthening financial knowledge and protecting consumers.", "output": "Answer: The FDIC ensures the security of its official websites by using HTTPS, which means the website uses encryption to protect the transmission of data [1].", "intermediate": ["[Retrieval]", "Answer: The FDIC ensures the security of its official websites by using HTTPS, which means the website uses encryption to protect the transmission of data."]}, {"qa_pairs": [{"context": "No context provided", "question": "What is the standard insurance coverage limit provided by the FDIC for depositors?", "short_answers": ["$250,000 per depositor", "Per insured bank"], "wikipage": null}, {"context": "No context provided", "question": "What types of account ownership categories are covered by the FDIC insurance?", "short_answers": ["Individual accounts", "Joint accounts", "Retirement accounts", "Revocable trust accounts"], "wikipage": null}, {"context": "No context provided", "question": "What is the mission of the Federal Deposit Insurance Corporation (FDIC)?", "short_answers": ["Maintain stability", "Public confidence in financial system"], "wikipage": null}], "wikipages": [{"title": "AML Topic 28", "url": "https://www.fdic.gov/espanol"}], "annotations": [{"knowledge": [], "long_answer": "The standard insurance coverage limit provided by the FDIC is $250,000 per depositor, per insured bank, for each account ownership category. The FDIC insurance covers several account ownership categories including individual accounts, joint accounts, retirement accounts, and revocable trust accounts. The mission of the Federal Deposit Insurance Corporation (FDIC) is to maintain stability and public confidence in the nation's financial system."}, {"knowledge": [{"content": "The standard deposit insurance amount is $250,000 per depositor, per insured bank for each account ownership category: individual accounts, joint accounts, retirement accounts, and revocable trust accounts.", "wikipage": "AML Topic 28"}, {"content": "The standard deposit insurance amount is $250,000 per depositor, per insured bank for each account ownership category: individual accounts, joint accounts, retirement accounts, and revocable trust accounts.", "wikipage": "AML Topic 28"}, {"content": "The mission of the Federal Deposit Insurance Corporation (FDIC) is to maintain stability and public confidence in the nation's financial system.", "wikipage": "AML Topic 28"}], "long_answer": "The standard insurance coverage limit provided by the FDIC is $250,000 per depositor, per insured bank, for each account ownership category.\n\nThe FDIC insurance covers several account ownership categories including individual accounts, joint accounts, retirement accounts, and revocable trust accounts.\n\nThe mission of the Federal Deposit Insurance Corporation (FDIC) is to maintain stability and public confidence in the nation's financial system."}], "sample_id": "aml-topic-28-2", "question": "What is the standard insurance coverage limit provided by the FDIC for depositors?", "docs": [{"id": "doc-aml-topic-28-2-1", "title": "AML Topic 28 Part 1", "text": "In the event that your bank fails, FDIC insurance covers depositors' accounts at insured banks up to the insurance coverage limit, including principal and interest up to the date of the bank's closure. The standard deposit insurance amount is $250,000 per depositor, per insured bank, for each account ownership category: individual accounts, joint accounts, retirement accounts, and revocable trust accounts.\n\nLearn more\nEDIE\u2014the Calculator", "score": 0.9, "summary": "In the event that your bank fails, FDIC insurance covers depositors' accounts at insured banks up to the coverage limit.", "extraction": "The standard deposit insurance amount is $250,000 per depositor, per insured bank for each account ownership category: individual accounts, joint accounts, retirement accounts, and revocable trust accounts."}], "answer": "The standard insurance coverage limit provided by the FDIC is $250,000 per depositor, per insured bank, for each account ownership category. The FDIC insurance covers several account ownership categories including individual accounts, joint accounts, retirement accounts, and revocable trust accounts. The mission of the Federal Deposit Insurance Corporation (FDIC) is to maintain stability and public confidence in the nation's financial system.", "output": "The standard insurance coverage limit provided by the FDIC for depositors is $250,000 per depositor, per insured bank, for each account ownership category: individual accounts, joint accounts, retirement accounts, and revocable trust accounts [1].", "intermediate": ["[Retrieval]", "The standard insurance coverage limit provided by the FDIC for depositors is $250,000 per depositor, per insured bank, for each account ownership category: individual accounts, joint accounts, retirement accounts, and revocable trust accounts."]}, {"qa_pairs": [{"context": "No context provided", "question": "What is the role of the FDIC's Community Affairs Program?", "short_answers": ["Promote stability", "Public confidence in financial system"], "wikipage": null}, {"context": "No context provided", "question": "How can consumers get in touch with the FDIC for assistance?", "short_answers": ["Contact FDIC", "Assistance available"], "wikipage": null}, {"context": "No context provided", "question": "How does the FDIC ensure consumers are well-informed?", "short_answers": ["Subscriptions available", "Active on social media"], "wikipage": null}], "wikipages": [{"title": "AML Topic 28", "url": "https://www.fdic.gov/espanol"}], "annotations": [{"knowledge": [], "long_answer": "The FDIC's Community Affairs Program supports the mission of the FDIC by promoting stability and public confidence in the nation's financial system. Consumers can get in touch with the FDIC for assistance by contacting them directly. The FDIC ensures consumers are well-informed by offering subscriptions to updates and maintaining a presence on multiple social media platforms such as Facebook, X, Instagram, LinkedIn, Flickr, and YouTube."}, {"knowledge": [{"content": "The Community Affairs Program supports the FDIC's mission to promote stability and public confidence in the nation's financial system.", "wikipage": "AML Topic 28"}, {"content": "Contact the FDIC.", "wikipage": "AML Topic 28"}, {"content": "Stay Informed (English) Enter your email address Subscribe Follow the FDIC on Facebook Follow the FDIC on X Share on X Follow the FDIC on Instagram Follow the FDIC on LinkedIn Follow the FDIC on Flickr Follow the FDIC on YouTube", "wikipage": "AML Topic 28"}], "long_answer": "The FDIC's Community Affairs Program supports the mission of the FDIC by promoting stability and public confidence in the nation's financial system.\n\nConsumers can get in touch with the FDIC for assistance by contacting them directly.\n\nThe FDIC ensures consumers are well-informed by offering subscriptions to updates and maintaining a presence on multiple social media platforms such as Facebook, X, Instagram, LinkedIn, Flickr, and YouTube."}], "sample_id": "aml-topic-28-3", "question": "What is the role of the FDIC's Community Affairs Program?", "docs": [{"id": "doc-aml-topic-28-3-1", "title": "AML Topic 28 Part 1", "text": "Consumer Protection\n\nThe Consumer Protection Center strives to provide optimal service by responding to consumer inquiries and complaints in an objective, informed, professional, precise, and timely manner.\n\nLearn more\n\nCommunity Affairs Program and Contact Information\n\nThe Community Affairs Program supports the FDIC's mission to promote stability and public confidence in the nation's financial system.\n\nLearn more\n\nContact us", "score": 0.9, "summary": "Consumer Protection The Consumer Protection Center strives to offer optimal service by responding to inquiries and complaints from...", "extraction": "The Community Affairs Program supports the FDIC's mission to promote stability and public confidence in the nation's financial system."}], "answer": "The FDIC's Community Affairs Program supports the mission of the FDIC by promoting stability and public confidence in the nation's financial system. Consumers can get in touch with the FDIC for assistance by contacting them directly. The FDIC ensures consumers are well-informed by offering subscriptions to updates and maintaining a presence on multiple social media platforms such as Facebook, X, Instagram, LinkedIn, Flickr, and YouTube.", "output": "Answer: The FDIC's Community Affairs Program supports the agency's mission to promote stability and public confidence in the nation's financial system [1].", "intermediate": ["[Retrieval]", "Answer: The FDIC's Community Affairs Program supports the agency's mission to promote stability and public confidence in the nation's financial system."]}, {"qa_pairs": [{"context": "No context provided", "question": "What resources does the FDIC offer for bankers seeking financial education materials?", "short_answers": ["Financial education materials", "Data tools", "Laws and regulations documentation"], "wikipage": null}, {"context": "No context provided", "question": "Where can bankers find information about FDIC supervision and examinations?", "short_answers": ["Banker Resource Center", "Supervision & Examinations"], "wikipage": null}, {"context": "No context provided", "question": "What type of research does the FDIC offer related to community banking?", "short_answers": ["Community Banking Research Program"], "wikipage": null}], "wikipages": [{"title": "AML Topic 29", "url": "https://www.fdic.gov/about/what-we-do"}], "annotations": [{"knowledge": [], "long_answer": "The FDIC provides a variety of resources for bankers, including financial education materials, data tools, documentation of laws and regulations, and information on important initiatives. Bankers can find information about FDIC supervision and examinations in the Banker Resource Center. The FDIC offers a Community Banking Research Program as part of its resources."}, {"knowledge": [{"content": "The FDIC provides a wealth of resources for consumers, bankers, analysts, and other stakeholders. Browse our collection of financial education materials, data tools, documentation of laws and regulations, information on important initiatives, and more.", "wikipage": "AML Topic 29"}, {"content": "Additional FDIC Resources\nConsumer Resource Center\nBanker Resource Center\nDeposit Insurance\nSupervision & Examinations", "wikipage": "AML Topic 29"}, {"content": "Community Banking Research Program", "wikipage": "AML Topic 29"}], "long_answer": "The FDIC provides a variety of resources for bankers, including financial education materials, data tools, documentation of laws and regulations, and information on important initiatives.\n\nBankers can find information about FDIC supervision and examinations in the Banker Resource Center.\n\nThe FDIC offers a Community Banking Research Program as part of its resources."}], "sample_id": "aml-topic-29-2", "question": "What resources does the FDIC offer for bankers seeking financial education materials?", "docs": [{"id": "doc-aml-topic-29-2-1", "title": "AML Topic 29 Part 1", "text": "Ill. Assumes All Deposits of Pulaski Savings\u2026\nPODCASTS / January 06, 2025\nSmall Business Lending\nResources\nToggle submenu\nResources\nThe FDIC provides a wealth of resources for consumers, bankers, analysts, and other stakeholders. Browse our collection of financial education materials, data tools, documentation of laws and regulations, information on important initiatives, and more.\nAdditional FDIC Resources\nConsumer Resource Center\nBanker Resource Center\nDeposit Insurance\nSupervision & Examinati", "score": 0.9, "summary": "Ill. Assumes All Deposits of Pulaski Savings\u2026 PODCASTS / January 06, 2025 Small Business Lending Resources Toggle submenu Resources The FDIC provides ...", "extraction": "The FDIC provides a wealth of resources for consumers, bankers, analysts, and other stakeholders. Browse our collection of financial education materials, data tools, documentation of laws and regulations, information on important initiatives, and more."}], "answer": "The FDIC provides a variety of resources for bankers, including financial education materials, data tools, documentation of laws and regulations, and information on important initiatives. Bankers can find information about FDIC supervision and examinations in the Banker Resource Center. The FDIC offers a Community Banking Research Program as part of its resources.", "output": "Answer: The FDIC provides a wealth of resources for consumers, bankers, analysts, and other stakeholders [1].", "intermediate": ["[Retrieval]", "Answer: The FDIC provides a wealth of resources for consumers, bankers, analysts, and other stakeholders."]}, {"qa_pairs": [{"context": "No context provided", "question": "What kind of data does the FDIC provide through its Quarterly Banking Profile?", "short_answers": ["Performance data", "Quarterly Banking Profile"], "wikipage": null}, {"context": "No context provided", "question": "How can I stay updated with the latest FDIC announcements and policy changes?", "short_answers": ["Regular updates", "Speeches and testimony", "Conferences and events"], "wikipage": null}, {"context": "No context provided", "question": "What type of reports does the FDIC offer for consumer research?", "short_answers": ["FDIC National Survey", "Unbanked and Underbanked Households"], "wikipage": null}], "wikipages": [{"title": "AML Topic 29", "url": "https://www.fdic.gov/about/what-we-do"}], "annotations": [{"knowledge": [], "long_answer": "The FDIC provides performance data of FDIC-insured institutions through its Quarterly Banking Profile. You can stay updated with the latest FDIC announcements and policy changes by reading their regular updates, speeches, testimony on banking issues, and details on upcoming conferences and events. The FDIC offers reports such as the FDIC National Survey of Unbanked and Underbanked Households for consumer research."}, {"knowledge": [{"content": "Quarterly Banking Profile", "wikipage": "AML Topic 29"}, {"content": "The FDIC publishes regular updates on news and activities. Keep up with FDIC announcements, read speeches and testimony on the latest banking issues, learn about policy changes for banks, and get the details on upcoming conferences and events.", "wikipage": "AML Topic 29"}, {"content": "Consumer Research FDIC National Survey of Unbanked and Underbanked Households", "wikipage": "AML Topic 29"}], "long_answer": "The FDIC provides performance data of FDIC-insured institutions through its Quarterly Banking Profile.\n\nYou can stay updated with the latest FDIC announcements and policy changes by reading their regular updates, speeches, testimony on banking issues, and details on upcoming conferences and events.\n\nThe FDIC offers reports such as the FDIC National Survey of Unbanked and Underbanked Households for consumer research."}], "sample_id": "aml-topic-29-3", "question": "What kind of data does the FDIC provide through its Quarterly Banking Profile?", "docs": [{"id": "doc-aml-topic-29-3-1", "title": "AML Topic 29 Part 1", "text": "performance data. Browse our extensive research tools and reports.\nMore FDIC Analysis\nCenter for Financial Research\nConsumer Research\nFDIC National Survey of Unbanked and Underbanked Households\nQuarterly Banking Profile\nFDIC Academic Challenge\nFDIC Banking Issues in Focus\nAnnual Risk Review\nEVENT / February 25, 2025\nFDIC-Insured Institutions Reported Return on Assets of 1.11 Percent and Net Inc\u2026\nEVENT / December 12, 2024\nFDIC-Insured Institutions Reported Net Income of $65.4 Billion\nEVENT / Sept", "score": 0.9, "summary": "performance data. Browse our extensive research tools and reports. More FDIC Analysis Center for Financial Research Consumer Research FDIC National Su...", "extraction": "Quarterly Banking Profile"}], "answer": "The FDIC provides performance data of FDIC-insured institutions through its Quarterly Banking Profile. You can stay updated with the latest FDIC announcements and policy changes by reading their regular updates, speeches, testimony on banking issues, and details on upcoming conferences and events. The FDIC offers reports such as the FDIC National Survey of Unbanked and Underbanked Households for consumer research.", "output": "Answer: The FDIC provides performance data, such as net income, assets, and deposits, through its Quarterly Banking Profile [1].", "intermediate": ["[Retrieval]", "Answer: The FDIC provides performance data, such as net income, assets, and deposits, through its Quarterly Banking Profile."]}, {"qa_pairs": [{"context": "No context provided", "question": "What resources does the FDIC provide for consumers and bankers?", "short_answers": ["Financial education materials", "Data tools", "Laws and regulations documentation"], "wikipage": null}, {"context": "No context provided", "question": "Where can bankers find resources related to deposit insurance and supervision?", "short_answers": ["Banker Resource Center", "Deposit Insurance", "Supervision & Examinations"], "wikipage": null}, {"context": "No context provided", "question": "What types of research programs does the FDIC offer?", "short_answers": ["Community Banking Research Program", "International seminars and training"], "wikipage": null}], "wikipages": [{"title": "AML Topic 30", "url": "https://www.fdic.gov/about/board-directors-senior-executives"}], "annotations": [{"knowledge": [], "long_answer": "The FDIC provides a wealth of resources for consumers and bankers, including financial education materials, data tools, documentation of laws and regulations, and information on important initiatives. Bankers can find resources related to deposit insurance and supervision in the FDIC's Banker Resource Center. The FDIC offers research programs such as the Community Banking Research Program and provides resources for international seminars and training."}, {"knowledge": [{"content": "The FDIC provides a wealth of resources for consumers, bankers, analysts, and other stakeholders. Browse our collection of financial education materials, data tools, documentation of laws and regulations, information on important initiatives, and more.", "wikipage": "AML Topic 30"}, {"content": "Additional FDIC Resources Consumer Resource Center Banker Resource Center Deposit Insurance Supervision & Examinations", "wikipage": "AML Topic 30"}, {"content": "Community Banking Research Program International Seminars and Training", "wikipage": "AML Topic 30"}], "long_answer": "The FDIC provides a wealth of resources for consumers and bankers, including financial education materials, data tools, documentation of laws and regulations, and information on important initiatives.\n\nBankers can find resources related to deposit insurance and supervision in the FDIC's Banker Resource Center.\n\nThe FDIC offers research programs such as the Community Banking Research Program and provides resources for international seminars and training."}], "sample_id": "aml-topic-30-2", "question": "What resources does the FDIC provide for consumers and bankers?", "docs": [{"id": "doc-aml-topic-30-2-1", "title": "AML Topic 30 Part 1", "text": "illennium Bank, Des Plaines, Ill. Assumes All Deposits of Pulaski Savings\u2026\nPODCASTS / January 06, 2025\nSmall Business Lending\nResources\nToggle submenu\nResources\nThe FDIC provides a wealth of resources for consumers, bankers, analysts, and other stakeholders. Browse our collection of financial education materials, data tools, documentation of laws and regulations, information on important initiatives, and more.\nAdditional FDIC Resources\nConsumer Resource Center\nBanker Resource Center\nDeposit Insu", "score": 0.9, "summary": "illennium Bank, Des Plaines, Ill. Assumes All Deposits of Pulaski Savings\u2026 PODCASTS / January 06, 2025 Small Business Lending Resources Toggle submenu...", "extraction": "The FDIC provides a wealth of resources for consumers, bankers, analysts, and other stakeholders. Browse our collection of financial education materials, data tools, documentation of laws and regulations, information on important initiatives, and more."}], "answer": "The FDIC provides a wealth of resources for consumers and bankers, including financial education materials, data tools, documentation of laws and regulations, and information on important initiatives. Bankers can find resources related to deposit insurance and supervision in the FDIC's Banker Resource Center. The FDIC offers research programs such as the Community Banking Research Program and provides resources for international seminars and training.", "output": "Answer: The FDIC provides a wealth of resources for consumers, bankers, analysts, and other stakeholders [1].", "intermediate": ["[Retrieval]", "Ans