he FDIC provides a collection of resources for bankers, including financial education materials, data tools, documentation of laws and regulations, and information on important initiatives.\n\nConsumers can find information on deposit insurance in the Consumer Resource Center provided by the FDIC.\n\nThe FDIC conducts research and analysis on the U.S. banking industry, including quarterly banking profiles, working papers, and state banking analysis."}], "sample_id": "aml-topic-32-2", "question": "What resources does the FDIC offer to bankers for compliance and operational support?", "docs": [{"id": "doc-aml-topic-32-2-1", "title": "AML Topic 32 Part 1", "text": ", Ill. Assumes All Deposits of Pulaski Savings\u2026\nPODCASTS / January 06, 2025\nSmall Business Lending\nResources\nToggle submenu\nResources\nThe FDIC provides a wealth of resources for consumers, bankers, analysts, and other stakeholders. Browse our collection of financial education materials, data tools, documentation of laws and regulations, information on important initiatives, and more.\nAdditional FDIC Resources\nConsumer Resource Center\nBanker Resource Center\nDeposit Insurance\nSupervision & Examina", "score": 0.9, "summary": ", Ill. Assumes All Deposits of Pulaski Savings\u2026 PODCASTS / January 06, 2025 Small Business Lending Resources Toggle submenu Resources The FDIC provide...", "extraction": "The FDIC provides a wealth of resources for consumers, bankers, analysts, and other stakeholders. Browse our collection of financial education materials, data tools, documentation of laws and regulations, information on important initiatives, and more."}], "answer": "The FDIC provides a collection of resources for bankers, including financial education materials, data tools, documentation of laws and regulations, and information on important initiatives. Consumers can find information on deposit insurance in the Consumer Resource Center provided by the FDIC. The FDIC conducts research and analysis on the U.", "output": "Answer: The FDIC provides a wealth of resources for consumers, bankers, analysts, and other stakeholders [1].", "intermediate": ["[Retrieval]", "Answer: The FDIC provides a wealth of resources for consumers, bankers, analysts, and other stakeholders."]}, {"qa_pairs": [{"context": "No context provided", "question": "What is the main purpose of the FDIC?", "short_answers": ["Maintain financial stability", "Public confidence"], "wikipage": null}, {"context": "No context provided", "question": "How can you ensure that you are on an official FDIC website?", "short_answers": [".gov or .mil URL", "https:// for secure connection"], "wikipage": null}, {"context": "No context provided", "question": "What type of information can you learn about on the FDIC's website?", "short_answers": ["FDIC mission", "Leadership", "History", "Career opportunities"], "wikipage": null}], "wikipages": [{"title": "AML Topic 33", "url": "https://www.fdic.gov/strategic-plans"}], "annotations": [{"knowledge": [], "long_answer": "The Federal Deposit Insurance Corporation (FDIC) is an independent agency created by Congress to maintain stability and public confidence in the nation\u2019s financial system. To ensure you are on an official FDIC website, check that the URL ends in . On the FDIC's website, you can learn about the FDIC\u2019s mission, leadership, history, career opportunities, initiatives, strategic plans, financial reports, governance, and more."}, {"knowledge": [{"content": "The Federal Deposit Insurance Corporation (FDIC) is an independent agency created by the Congress to maintain stability and public confidence in the nation\u2019s financial system.", "wikipage": "AML Topic 33"}, {"content": "The .gov means it\u2019s official. Federal government websites often end in .gov or .mil. Before sharing sensitive information, make sure you\u2019re on a federal government site. The site is secure. The https:// ensures that you are connecting to the official website and that any information you provide is encrypted and transmitted securely.", "wikipage": "AML Topic 33"}, {"content": "Learn about the FDIC\u2019s mission, leadership, history, career opportunities, and more.", "wikipage": "AML Topic 33"}], "long_answer": "The Federal Deposit Insurance Corporation (FDIC) is an independent agency created by Congress to maintain stability and public confidence in the nation\u2019s financial system.\n\nTo ensure you are on an official FDIC website, check that the URL ends in .gov or .mil and that it begins with https://, indicating a secure connection.\n\nOn the FDIC's website, you can learn about the FDIC\u2019s mission, leadership, history, career opportunities, initiatives, strategic plans, financial reports, governance, and more."}], "sample_id": "aml-topic-33-1", "question": "What is the main purpose of the FDIC?", "docs": [{"id": "doc-aml-topic-33-1-2", "title": "AML Topic 33 Part 2", "text": "ut\nThe Federal Deposit Insurance Corporation (FDIC) is an independent agency created by the Congress to maintain stability and public confidence in the nation\u2019s financial system. Learn about the FDIC\u2019s mission, leadership, history, career opportunities, and more.\nLearn More About the FDIC\nWhat We Do\nLeadership\nCareers\nInitiatives\nStrategic Plans\nFinancial Reports\nHistory\nGovernance\nOmbudsman\nDoing Business with the FDIC\nPRESS RELEASE / February 25, 2025\nFDIC-Insured Institutions Reported Return", "score": 0.85, "summary": "ut The Federal Deposit Insurance Corporation (FDIC) is an independent agency created by the Congress to maintain stability and public confidence in th...", "extraction": "ut\nThe Federal Deposit Insurance Corporation (FDIC) is an independent agency created by the Congress to maintain stability and public confidence in the nation\u2019s financial system. Learn about the FDIC\u2019"}], "answer": "The Federal Deposit Insurance Corporation (FDIC) is an independent agency created by Congress to maintain stability and public confidence in the nation\u2019s financial system. To ensure you are on an official FDIC website, check that the URL ends in . On the FDIC's website, you can learn about the FDIC\u2019s mission, leadership, history, career opportunities, initiatives, strategic plans, financial reports, governance, and more.", "output": "Answer: The main purpose of the FDIC is to maintain stability and public confidence in the U. S. financial system [1].", "intermediate": ["[Retrieval]", "Answer: The main purpose of the FDIC is to maintain stability and public confidence in the U.S. financial system."]}, {"qa_pairs": [{"context": "No context provided", "question": "What kind of resources does the FDIC provide for bankers?", "short_answers": ["Banker Resource Center", "Laws and regulations documentation", "Supervision and examinations"], "wikipage": null}, {"context": "No context provided", "question": "Where can stakeholders find information about FDIC's laws and regulations?", "short_answers": ["FDIC's resource collection", "Documentation of laws and regulations"], "wikipage": null}, {"context": "No context provided", "question": "Does the FDIC offer resources for international stakeholders?", "short_answers": ["International seminars", "International training"], "wikipage": null}], "wikipages": [{"title": "AML Topic 33", "url": "https://www.fdic.gov/strategic-plans"}], "annotations": [{"knowledge": [], "long_answer": "The FDIC provides a variety of resources for bankers, including a Banker Resource Center, documentation of laws and regulations, supervision and examinations, and data tools. Stakeholders can find information about FDIC's laws and regulations in the FDIC's collection of resources, which includes documentation of laws and regulations. Yes, the FDIC offers resources for international stakeholders, including international seminars and training."}, {"knowledge": [{"content": "The FDIC provides a wealth of resources for consumers, bankers, analysts, and other stakeholders. Browse our collection of financial education materials, data tools, documentation of laws and regulations, information on important initiatives, and more.", "wikipage": "AML Topic 33"}, {"content": "The FDIC provides a wealth of resources for consumers, bankers, analysts, and other stakeholders. Browse our collection of financial education materials, data tools, documentation of laws and regulations, information on important initiatives, and more.", "wikipage": "AML Topic 33"}, {"content": "Additional FDIC Resources: Consumer Resource Center, Banker Resource Center, Deposit Insurance, Supervision & Examinations, Laws & Regulations, Resolutions, Publications, Forms, Data Tools, Community Banking Research Program, International Seminars and Training.", "wikipage": "AML Topic 33"}], "long_answer": "The FDIC provides a variety of resources for bankers, including a Banker Resource Center, documentation of laws and regulations, supervision and examinations, and data tools.\n\nStakeholders can find information about FDIC's laws and regulations in the FDIC's collection of resources, which includes documentation of laws and regulations.\n\nYes, the FDIC offers resources for international stakeholders, including international seminars and training."}], "sample_id": "aml-topic-33-2", "question": "What kind of resources does the FDIC provide for bankers?", "docs": [{"id": "doc-aml-topic-33-2-1", "title": "AML Topic 33 Part 1", "text": "ines, Ill. Assumes All Deposits of Pulaski Savings\u2026\nPODCASTS / January 06, 2025\nSmall Business Lending\nResources\nToggle submenu\nResources\nThe FDIC provides a wealth of resources for consumers, bankers, analysts, and other stakeholders. Browse our collection of financial education materials, data tools, documentation of laws and regulations, information on important initiatives, and more.\nAdditional FDIC Resources\nConsumer Resource Center\nBanker Resource Center\nDeposit Insurance\nSupervision & Exa", "score": 0.9, "summary": "ines, Ill. Assumes All Deposits of Pulaski Savings\u2026 PODCASTS / January 06, 2025 Small Business Lending Resources Toggle submenu Resources The FDIC pro...", "extraction": "The FDIC provides a wealth of resources for consumers, bankers, analysts, and other stakeholders. Browse our collection of financial education materials, data tools, documentation of laws and regulations, information on important initiatives, and more."}], "answer": "The FDIC provides a variety of resources for bankers, including a Banker Resource Center, documentation of laws and regulations, supervision and examinations, and data tools. Stakeholders can find information about FDIC's laws and regulations in the FDIC's collection of resources, which includes documentation of laws and regulations. Yes, the FDIC offers resources for international stakeholders, including international seminars and training.", "output": "Answer: The FDIC provides a wealth of resources for consumers, bankers, analysts, and other stakeholders [1].", "intermediate": ["[Retrieval]", "Answer: The FDIC provides a wealth of resources for consumers, bankers, analysts, and other stakeholders."]}, {"qa_pairs": [{"context": "No context provided", "question": "What was the reported net income for FDIC-insured institutions in December 2024?", "short_answers": ["$65.4 billion", "December 2024"], "wikipage": null}, {"context": "No context provided", "question": "How did the return on assets for FDIC-insured institutions fare in February 2025?", "short_answers": ["1.11 percent", "February 2025"], "wikipage": null}, {"context": "No context provided", "question": "What was the quarterly net income for FDIC-insured institutions in September 2024?", "short_answers": ["$71.5 billion", "September 2024"], "wikipage": null}], "wikipages": [{"title": "AML Topic 33", "url": "https://www.fdic.gov/strategic-plans"}], "annotations": [{"knowledge": [], "long_answer": "The FDIC-insured institutions reported a net income of $65. In February 2025, FDIC-insured institutions reported a return on assets of 1. The FDIC-insured institutions reported a net income of $71."}, {"knowledge": [{"content": "EVENT / December 12, 2024\nFDIC-Insured Institutions Reported Net Income of $65.4 Billion", "wikipage": "AML Topic 33"}, {"content": "EVENT / February 25, 2025\nFDIC-Insured Institutions Reported Return on Assets of 1.11 Percent", "wikipage": "AML Topic 33"}, {"content": "EVENT / September 05, 2024\nFDIC-Insured Institutions Reported Net Income of $71.5 Billion", "wikipage": "AML Topic 33"}], "long_answer": "The FDIC-insured institutions reported a net income of $65.4 billion in December 2024.\n\nIn February 2025, FDIC-insured institutions reported a return on assets of 1.11 percent.\n\nThe FDIC-insured institutions reported a net income of $71.5 billion in September 2024."}], "sample_id": "aml-topic-33-3", "question": "What was the reported net income for FDIC-insured institutions in December 2024?", "docs": [{"id": "doc-aml-topic-33-3-1", "title": "AML Topic 33 Part 1", "text": "nking performance data. Browse our extensive research tools and reports.\nMore FDIC Analysis\nCenter for Financial Research\nConsumer Research\nFDIC National Survey of Unbanked and Underbanked Households\nQuarterly Banking Profile\nFDIC Academic Challenge\nFDIC Banking Issues in Focus\nAnnual Risk Review\nEVENT / February 25, 2025\nFDIC-Insured Institutions Reported Return on Assets of 1.11 Percent and Net Inc\u2026\nEVENT / December 12, 2024\nFDIC-Insured Institutions Reported Net Income of $65.4 Billion\nEVENT", "score": 0.9, "summary": "nking performance data. Browse our extensive research tools and reports. More FDIC Analysis Center for Financial Research Consumer Research FDIC Natio...", "extraction": "EVENT / December 12, 2024\nFDIC-Insured Institutions Reported Net Income of $65.4 Billion"}], "answer": "The FDIC-insured institutions reported a net income of $65. In February 2025, FDIC-insured institutions reported a return on assets of 1. The FDIC-insured institutions reported a net income of $71.", "output": "According to the FDIC, FDIC-insured institutions reported net income of $65. 4 billion in December 2024 [1].", "intermediate": ["[Retrieval]", "According to the FDIC, FDIC-insured institutions reported net income of $65.4 billion in December 2024."]}, {"qa_pairs": [{"context": "No context provided", "question": "What kind of performance data does the FDIC provide for banking institutions?", "short_answers": ["Return on assets", "Net income figures"], "wikipage": null}, {"context": "No context provided", "question": "How can I stay updated on the latest FDIC announcements and banking issues?", "short_answers": ["Regular updates", "Speeches and testimony", "Policy changes"], "wikipage": null}, {"context": "No context provided", "question": "What resources does the FDIC offer for understanding banking issues and performance?", "short_answers": ["Quarterly Banking Profile", "Annual Risk Review", "FDIC Academic Challenge"], "wikipage": null}], "wikipages": [{"title": "AML Topic 34", "url": "https://www.fdic.gov/financial-reports"}], "annotations": [{"knowledge": [], "long_answer": "The FDIC provides performance data such as the return on assets and net income for FDIC-insured institutions. You can stay updated on FDIC announcements and banking issues by following their regular updates, which include news, speeches, testimony on banking issues, policy changes, and details on upcoming conferences and events. The FDIC offers various resources such as the Quarterly Banking Profile, Annual Risk Review, and events like the FDIC Academic Challenge and Banking Issues in Focus to understand banking issues and performance."}, {"knowledge": [{"content": "EVENT / February 25, 2025\nFDIC-Insured Institutions Reported Return on Assets of 1.11 Percent and Net Inc\u2026\nEVENT / December 12, 2024\nFDIC-Insured Institutions Reported Net Income of $65.4 Billion\nEVENT / September 05, 2024\nFDIC-Insured Institutions Reported Net Income of $71.5 Billion", "wikipage": "AML Topic 34"}, {"content": "The FDIC publishes regular updates on news and activities. Keep up with FDIC announcements, read speeches and testimony on the latest banking issues, learn about policy changes for banks, and get the details on upcoming conferences and events.", "wikipage": "AML Topic 34"}, {"content": "Quarterly Banking Profile\nFDIC Academic Challenge\nFDIC Banking Issues in Focus\nAnnual Risk Review", "wikipage": "AML Topic 34"}], "long_answer": "The FDIC provides performance data such as the return on assets and net income for FDIC-insured institutions. For example, they reported a return on assets of 1.11 percent and net income figures such as $65.4 billion in December 2024 and $71.5 billion in September 2024.\n\nYou can stay updated on FDIC announcements and banking issues by following their regular updates, which include news, speeches, testimony on banking issues, policy changes, and details on upcoming conferences and events.\n\nThe FDIC offers various resources such as the Quarterly Banking Profile, Annual Risk Review, and events like the FDIC Academic Challenge and Banking Issues in Focus to understand banking issues and performance."}], "sample_id": "aml-topic-34-3", "question": "What kind of performance data does the FDIC provide for banking institutions?", "docs": [{"id": "doc-aml-topic-34-3-1", "title": "AML Topic 34 Part 1", "text": "banking performance data. Browse our extensive research tools and reports.\nMore FDIC Analysis\nCenter for Financial Research\nConsumer Research\nFDIC National Survey of Unbanked and Underbanked Households\nQuarterly Banking Profile\nFDIC Academic Challenge\nFDIC Banking Issues in Focus\nAnnual Risk Review\nEVENT / February 25, 2025\nFDIC-Insured Institutions Reported Return on Assets of 1.11 Percent and Net Inc\u2026\nEVENT / December 12, 2024\nFDIC-Insured Institutions Reported Net Income of $65.4 Billion\nEVEN", "score": 0.9, "summary": "banking performance data. Browse our extensive research tools and reports. More FDIC Analysis Center for Financial Research Consumer Research FDIC Nat...", "extraction": "EVENT / February 25, 2025\nFDIC-Insured Institutions Reported Return on Assets of 1.11 Percent and Net Inc\u2026\nEVENT / December 12, 2024\nFDIC-Insured Institutions Reported Net Income of $65.4 Billion\nEVENT / September 05, 2024\nFDIC-Insured Institutions Reported Net Income of $71.5 Billion"}], "answer": "The FDIC provides performance data such as the return on assets and net income for FDIC-insured institutions. You can stay updated on FDIC announcements and banking issues by following their regular updates, which include news, speeches, testimony on banking issues, policy changes, and details on upcoming conferences and events. The FDIC offers various resources such as the Quarterly Banking Profile, Annual Risk Review, and events like the FDIC Academic Challenge and Banking Issues in Focus to understand banking issues and performance.", "output": "The FDIC provides performance data for banking institutions in the form of the Quarterly Banking Profile, which includes data on a bank's income, assets, and capital [1].", "intermediate": ["[Retrieval]", "The FDIC provides performance data for banking institutions in the form of the Quarterly Banking Profile, which includes data on a bank's income, assets, and capital."]}, {"qa_pairs": [{"context": "No context provided", "question": "What resources does the FDIC offer for bankers looking to understand financial regulations?", "short_answers": ["Financial education materials", "Data tools", "Documentation of laws and regulations"], "wikipage": null}, {"context": "No context provided", "question": "Where can consumers find information about FDIC deposit insurance?", "short_answers": ["Consumer Resource Center", "Deposit Insurance"], "wikipage": null}, {"context": "No context provided", "question": "What type of banking industry research does the FDIC offer?", "short_answers": ["Quarterly banking profiles", "Working papers"], "wikipage": null}], "wikipages": [{"title": "AML Topic 35", "url": "https://www.fdic.gov/history"}], "annotations": [{"knowledge": [], "long_answer": "The FDIC provides a variety of resources for bankers, including financial education materials, data tools, documentation of laws and regulations, and information on important initiatives. Consumers can find information about FDIC deposit insurance in the Consumer Resource Center provided by the FDIC. The FDIC offers U."}, {"knowledge": [{"content": "The FDIC provides a wealth of resources for consumers, bankers, analysts, and other stakeholders. Browse our collection of financial education materials, data tools, documentation of laws and regulations, information on important initiatives, and more.", "wikipage": "AML Topic 35"}, {"content": "Additional FDIC Resources Consumer Resource Center Banker Resource Center Deposit Insurance Supervision & Examinations Laws & Regulations Resolutions Publications Forms Data Tools Community Banking Research Program International Seminars and Training", "wikipage": "AML Topic 35"}, {"content": "The FDIC is proud to be a pre-eminent source of U.S. banking industry research, including quarterly banking profiles, working papers, and stat", "wikipage": "AML Topic 35"}], "long_answer": "The FDIC provides a variety of resources for bankers, including financial education materials, data tools, documentation of laws and regulations, and information on important initiatives.\n\nConsumers can find information about FDIC deposit insurance in the Consumer Resource Center provided by the FDIC.\n\nThe FDIC offers U.S. banking industry research, including quarterly banking profiles and working papers."}], "sample_id": "aml-topic-35-2", "question": "What resources does the FDIC offer for bankers looking to understand financial regulations?", "docs": [{"id": "doc-aml-topic-35-2-1", "title": "AML Topic 35 Part 1", "text": "Plai