nce"], "wikipage": null}, {"context": "No context provided", "question": "Does the FDIC offer any programs focused on community banking research?", "short_answers": ["Community Banking Research Program"], "wikipage": null}], "wikipages": [{"title": "AML Topic 36", "url": "https://www.fdic.gov/about/fdic-governance"}], "annotations": [{"knowledge": [], "long_answer": "The FDIC provides a Banker Resource Center, which is part of its collection of resources that includes financial education materials, data tools, documentation of laws and regulations, and information on important initiatives. Consumers can access information on FDIC deposit insurance through the Consumer Resource Center, which is part of the FDIC's additional resources. Yes, the FDIC offers a Community Banking Research Program as part of its resources."}, {"knowledge": [{"content": "The FDIC provides a wealth of resources for consumers, bankers, analysts, and other stakeholders. Browse our collection of financial education materials, data tools, documentation of laws and regulations, information on important initiatives, and more.", "wikipage": "AML Topic 36"}, {"content": "Additional FDIC Resources Consumer Resource Center Banker Resource Center Deposit Insurance Supervision & Examinations Laws & Regulations Resolutions Publications Forms Data Tools", "wikipage": "AML Topic 36"}, {"content": "Community Banking Research Program", "wikipage": "AML Topic 36"}], "long_answer": "The FDIC provides a Banker Resource Center, which is part of its collection of resources that includes financial education materials, data tools, documentation of laws and regulations, and information on important initiatives.\n\nConsumers can access information on FDIC deposit insurance through the Consumer Resource Center, which is part of the FDIC's additional resources.\n\nYes, the FDIC offers a Community Banking Research Program as part of its resources."}], "sample_id": "aml-topic-36-2", "question": "What resources does the F