ation materials", "Data tools", "Documentation of laws and regulations"], "wikipage": null}, {"context": "No context provided", "question": "Where can consumers find FDIC resources tailored for them?", "short_answers": ["Consumer Resource Center"], "wikipage": null}, {"context": "No context provided", "question": "What type of research does the FDIC conduct on the U.S. banking industry?", "short_answers": ["Quarterly banking profiles", "Working papers"], "wikipage": null}], "wikipages": [{"title": "AML Topic 37", "url": "https://www.fdic.gov/about/about-ombudsman"}], "annotations": [{"knowledge": [], "long_answer": "The FDIC offers a variety of resources for bankers, including financial education materials, data tools, documentation of laws and regulations, information on important initiatives, and more. Consumers can find FDIC resources tailored for them at the Consumer Resource Center. The FDIC conducts research on the U."}, {"knowledge": [{"content": "The FDIC provides a wealth of resources for consumers, bankers, analysts, and other stakeholders. Browse our collection of financial education materials, data tools, documentation of laws and regulations, information on important initiatives, and more.", "wikipage": "AML Topic 37"}, {"content": "Additional FDIC Resources\nConsumer Resource Center\nBanker Resource Center", "wikipage": "AML Topic 37"}, {"content": "The FDIC is proud to be a pre-eminent source of U.S. banking industry research, including quarterly banking profiles, working papers, and stat", "wikipage": "AML Topic 37"}], "long_answer": "The FDIC offers a variety of resources for bankers, including financial education materials, data tools, documentation of laws and regulations, information on important initiatives, and more.\n\nConsumers can find FDIC resources tailored for them at the Consumer Resource Center.\n\nThe FDIC conducts research on the U.S. banking industry, including quarterly banking profiles and working papers."}], "sample_id": "aml-topic-37-2", "question": "What resources does the FDIC offer to bankers?", "docs": [{"id": "doc-aml-topic-37-2-1", "title": "AML Topic 37 Part 1", "text": "Plaines, Ill. Assumes All Deposits of Pulaski Savings\u2026\nPODCASTS / January 06, 2025\nSmall Business Lending\nResources\nToggle submenu\nResources\nThe FDIC provides a wealth of resources for consumers, bankers, analysts, and other stakeholders. Browse our collection of financial education materials, data tools, documentation of laws and regulations, information on important initiatives, and more.\nAdditional FDIC Resources\nConsumer Resource Center\nBanker Resource Center\nDeposit Insurance\nSupervision &", "score": 0.9, "summary": "Plaines, Ill. Assumes All Deposits of Pulaski Savings\u2026 PODCASTS / January 06, 2025 Small Business Lending Resources Toggle submenu Resources The FDIC ...", "extraction": "The FDIC provides a wealth of resources for consumers, bankers, analysts, and other stakeholders. Browse our collection of financial education materials, data tools, documentation of laws and regulations, information on important initiatives, and more."}], "answer": "The FDIC offers a variety of resources for bankers, including financial education materials, data tools, documentation of laws and regulations, information on important initiatives, and more. Consumers can find FDIC resources tailored for them at the Consumer Resource Center. The FDIC conducts research on the U.", "output": "Answer: The FDIC provides a wealth of resources for consumers, bankers, analysts, and other stakeholders [1].", "intermediate": ["[Retrieval]", "Answer: The FDIC provides a wealth of resources for consumers, bankers, analysts, and other stakeholders."]}, {"qa_pairs": [{"context": "No context provided", "question": "What is the significance of the FDIC's Annual Risk Review for financial institutions?", "short_answers": ["Analyzes current banking risks", "Prepares for regulatory expectations"], "wikipage": null}, {"context": "No context provided", "question": "How does the FDIC's Quarterly Banking Profile benefit financial institutions?", "short_answers": ["Overview of financial health", "Insights into banking trends"], "wikipage": null}, {"context": "No context provided", "question": "What role does the FDIC National Survey of Unbanked and Underbanked Households play in consumer research?", "short_answers": ["Data on underserved populations", "Aids in developing inclusive products"], "wikipage": null}], "wikipages": [{"title": "AML Topic 37", "url": "https://www.fdic.gov/about/about-ombudsman"}], "annotations": [{"knowledge": [], "long_answer": "The FDIC's Annual Risk Review provides an analysis of the current risks facing the banking industry. The FDIC's Quarterly Banking Profile offers a comprehensive overview of the financial health and performance of FDIC-insured institutions. The FDIC National Survey of Unbanked and Underbanked Households provides critical data on the banking habits and needs of underserved populations."}, {"knowledge": [{"content": "Annual Risk Review", "wikipage": "AML Topic 37"}, {"content": "Quarterly Banking Profile", "wikipage": "AML Topic 37"}, {"content": "FDIC National Survey of Unbanked and Underbanked Households", "wikipage": "AML Topic 37"}], "long_answer": "The FDIC's Annual Risk Review provides an analysis of the current risks facing the banking industry. It helps financial institutions understand potential challenges and prepare for regulatory expectations, thus ensuring stability and compliance within the banking sector.\n\nThe FDIC's Quarterly Banking Profile offers a comprehensive overview of the financial health and performance of FDIC-insured institutions. It provides valuable insights into trends and economic conditions affecting the banking sector, aiding institutions in strategic planning and risk management.\n\nThe FDIC National Survey of Unbanked and Underbanked Households provides critical data on the banking habits and needs of underserved populations. This information helps financial institutions develop inclusive banking products and services, aiming to increase financial access and literacy."}], "sample_id": "aml-topic-37-3", "question": "What is the significance of the FDIC's Annual Risk Review for financial institutions?", "docs": [{"id": "doc-aml-topic-37-3-1", "title": "AML Topic 37 Part 1", "text": "e banking performance data. Browse our extensive research tools and reports.\nMore FDIC Analysis\nCenter for Financial Research\nConsumer Research\nFDIC National Survey of Unbanked and Underbanked Households\nQuarterly Banking Profile\nFDIC Academic Challenge\nFDIC Banking Issues in Focus\nAnnual Risk Review\nEVENT / February 25, 2025\nFDIC-Insured Institutions Reported Return on Assets of 1.11 Percent and Net Inc\u2026\nEVENT / December 12, 2024\nFDIC-Insured Institutions Reported Net Income of $65.4 Billion\nEV", "score": 0.9, "summary": "e banking performance data. Browse our extensive research tools and reports. More FDIC Analysis Center for Financial Research Consumer Research FDIC N...", "extraction": "Annual Risk Review"}], "answer": "The FDIC's Annual Risk Review provides an analysis of the current risks facing the banking industry. The FDIC's Quarterly Banking Profile offers a comprehensive overview of the financial health and performance of FDIC-insured institutions. The FDIC National Survey of Unbanked and Underbanked Households provides critical data on the banking habits and needs of underserved populations.", "output": "Answer: The FDIC's Annual Risk Review is significant because it provides the FDIC with a comprehensive view of the risks facing insured institutions and allows the FDIC to identify areas where institutions may need additional supervisory attention [1].", "intermediate": ["[Retrieval]", "Answer: The FDIC's Annual Risk Review is significant because it provides the FDIC with a comprehensive view of the risks facing insured institutions and allows the FDIC to identify areas where institutions may need additional supervisory attention."]}, {"qa_pairs": [{"context": "No context provided", "question": "What are some of the key events where FDIC-insured institutions reported their financial performance?", "short_answers": ["February 25, 2025: Return on assets 1.11%", "December 12, 2024: Net income $65.4 billion", "September 05, 2024: Net income $71.5 billion"], "wikipage": null}, {"context": "No context provided", "question": "Where can I find updates on FDIC's latest banking issues and policy changes?", "short_answers": ["FDIC announcements", "Speeches and testimony", "Policy changes for banks"], "wikipage": null}, {"context": "No context provided", "question": "What research resources does the FDIC offer for understanding banking performance and issues?", "short_answers": ["Center for Financial Research", "Consumer Research", "Quarterly Banking Profile"], "wikipage": null}], "wikipages": [{"title": "AML Topic 38", "url": "https://www.fdic.gov/doing-business-fdic"}], "annotations": [{"knowledge": [], "long_answer": "Key events include the February 25, 2025 report where FDIC-insured institutions reported a return on assets of 1. You can find updates on the latest banking issues and policy changes by keeping up with FDIC announcements, reading speeches and testimony, and learning about policy changes for banks. The FDIC offers several research resources including the Center for Financial Research, Consumer Research, the FDIC National Survey of Unbanked and Underbanked Households, the Quarterly Banking Profile, and the Annual Risk Review."}, {"knowledge": [{"content": "EVENT / February 25, 2025\nFDIC-Insured Institutions Reported Return on Assets of 1.11 Percent and Net Inc\u2026\nEVENT / December 12, 2024\nFDIC-Insured Institutions Reported Net Income of $65.4 Billion\nEVENT / September 05, 2024\nFDIC-Insured Institutions Reported Net Income of $71.5 Billion", "wikipage": "AML Topic 38"}, {"content": "The FDIC publishes regular updates on news and activities. Keep up with FDIC announcements, read speeches and testimony on the latest banking issues, learn about policy changes for banks, and get the details on upcoming conferences and events.", "wikipage": "AML Topic 38"}, {"content": "and state banking performance data. Browse our extensive research tools and reports.\nMore FDIC Analysis\nCenter for Financial Research\nConsumer Research\nFDIC National Survey of Unbanked and Underbanked Households\nQuarterly Banking Profile\nAnnual Risk Review", "wikipage": "AML Topic 38"}], "long_answer": "Key events include the February 25, 2025 report where FDIC-insured institutions reported a return on assets of 1.11 percent, and the December 12, 2024 report where they reported a net income of $65.4 billion. Additionally, on September 05, 2024, the institutions reported a net income of $71.5 billion.\n\nYou can find updates on the latest banking issues and policy changes by keeping up with FDIC announcements, reading speeches and testimony, and learning about policy changes for banks. The FDIC also publishes details on upcoming conferences and events.\n\nThe FDIC offers several research resources including the Center for Financial Research, Consumer Research, the FDIC National Survey of Unbanked and Underbanked Households, the Quarterly Banking Profile, and the Annual Risk Review."}], "sample_id": "aml-topic-38-3", "question": "What are some of the key events where FDIC-insured institutions reported their financial performance?", "docs": [{"id": "doc-aml-topic-38-3-1", "title": "AML Topic 38 Part 1", "text": "and state banking performance data. Browse our extensive research tools and reports.\nMore FDIC Analysis\nCenter for Financial Research\nConsumer Research\nFDIC National Survey of Unbanked and Underbanked Households\nQuarterly Banking Profile\nFDIC Academic Challenge\nFDIC Banking Issues in Focus\nAnnual Risk Review\nEVENT / February 25, 2025\nFDIC-Insured Institutions Reported Return on Assets of 1.11 Percent and Net Inc\u2026\nEVENT / December 12, 2024\nFDIC-Insured Institutions Reported Net Income of $65.4 Bi", "score": 0.9, "summary": "and state banking performance data. Browse our extensive research tools and reports. More FDIC Analysis Center for Financial Research Consumer Researc...", "extraction": "EVENT / February 25, 2025\nFDIC-Insured Institutions Reported Return on Assets of 1.11 Percent and Net Inc\u2026\nEVENT / December 12, 2024\nFDIC-Insured Institutions Reported Net Income of $65.4 Billion\nEVENT / September 05, 2024\nFDIC-Insured Institutions Reported Net Income of $71.5 Billion"}], "answer": "Key events include the February 25, 2025 report where FDIC-insured institutions reported a return on assets of 1. You can find updates on the latest banking issues and policy changes by keeping up with FDIC announcements, reading speeches and testimony, and learning about policy changes for banks. The FDIC offers several research resources including the Center for Financial Research, Consumer Research, the FDIC National Survey of Unbanked and Underbanked Households, the Quarterly Banking Profile, and the Annual Risk Review.", "output": "Answer: FDIC-insured institutions reported their financial performance at the FDIC's Quarterly Banking Profile, which is released quarterly [1].", "intermediate": ["[Retrieval]", "Answer: FDIC-insured institutions reported their financial performance at the FDIC's Quarterly Banking Profile, which is released quarterly."]}, {"qa_pairs": [{"context": "No context provided", "question": "What was the reported return on assets for FDIC-insured institutions in the fourth quarter?", "short_answers": ["1.11 percent"], "wikipage": null}, {"context": "No context provided", "question": "How much net income did FDIC-insured institutions report in the fourth quarter?", "short_answers": ["$66.8 billion"], "wikipage": null}, {"context": "No context provided", "question": "What is the role of the FDIC in the financial system?", "short_answers": ["Maintain stability", "Public confidence"], "wikipage": null}], "wikipages": [{"title": "AML Topic 39", "url": "https://www.fdic.gov/news/press-releases/2025/fdic-insured-institutions-reported-return-assets-111-percent-and-net"}], "annotations": [{"knowledge": [], "long_answer": "The reported return on assets for FDIC-insured institutions in the fourth quarter was 1. FDIC-insured institutions reported a net income of $66. The FDIC is an independent agency created by Congress to maintain stability and public confidence in the nation\u2019s financial system."}, {"knowledge": [{"content": "FDIC-Insured Institutions Reported Return on Assets of 1.11 Percent and Net Income of $66.8 Billion in the Fourth Quarter | FDIC.gov", "wikipage": "AML Topic 39"}, {"content": "FDIC-Insured Institutions Reported Return on Assets of 1.11 Percent and Net Income of $66.8 Billion in the Fourth Quarter | FDIC.gov", "wikipage": "AML Topic 39"}, {"content": "The Federal Deposit Insurance Corporation (FDIC) is an independent agency created by the Congress to maintain stability and public confidence in the nation\u2019s financial system.", "wikipage": "AML Topic 39"}], "long_answer": "The reported return on assets for FDIC-insured institutions in the fourth quarter was 1.11 percent.\n\nFDIC-insured institutions reported a net income of $66.8 billion in the fourth quarter.\n\nThe FDIC is an independent agency created by Congress to maintain stability and public confidence in the nation\u2019s financial system."}], "sample_id": "aml-topic-39-1", "question": "What was the reported return on assets for FDIC-insured institutions in the fourth quarter?", "docs": [{"id": "doc-aml-topic-39-1-1", "title": "AML Topic 39 Part 1", "text": "FDIC-Insured Institutions Reported Return on Assets of 1.11 Percent and Net Income of $66.8 Billion in the Fourth Quarter | FDIC.gov\nSkip to main content\nAn official website of the United States government\nThe .gov means it\u2019s official.\nFederal government websites often end in .gov or .mil. Before sharing sensitive information, make sure you\u2019re on a federal government site.\nThe site is secure.\nThe\nhttps://\nensures that you are connecting to the official website and that any information you provid", "score": 0.9, "summary": "FDIC-Insured Institutions Reported Return on Assets of 1.11 Percent and Net Income of $66.8 Billion in the Fourth Quarter | FDIC.gov Skip to main cont...", "extraction": "FDIC-Insured Institutions Reported Return on Assets of 1.11 Percent and Net Income of $66.8 Billion in the Fourth Quarter | FDIC.gov"}], "answer": "The reported return on assets for FDIC-insured institutions in the fourth quarter was 1. FDIC-insured institutions reported a net income of $66. The FDIC is an independent agency created by Congress to maintain stability and public confidence in the nation\u2019s financial system.", "output": "Answer: FDIC-insured institutions reported a return on assets of 1. 11 percent in the fourth quarter [1].", "intermediate": ["[Retrieval]", "Answer: FDIC-insured institutions reported a return on assets of 1.11 percent in the fourth quarter."]}, {"qa_pairs": [{"context": "No context provided", "question": "What resources does the FDIC provide for bankers seeking financial education materials?", "short_answers": ["Financial education materials", "Data tools", "Documentation of laws and regulations"], "wikipage": null}, {"context": "No context provided", "question": "Where can bankers find information about FDIC deposit insurance and supervision?", "short_answers": ["Banker Resource Center", "Deposit Insurance", "Supervision & Examinations"], "wikipage": null}, {"context": "No context provided", "question": "What type of analysis does the FDIC offer to stakeholders?", "short_answers": ["Pre-eminent source of analysis"], "wikipage": null}], "wikipages": [{"title": "AML Topic 39", "url": "https://www.fdic.gov/news/press-releases/2025/fdic-insured-institutions-reported-return-assets-111-percent-and-net"}], "annotations": [{"knowledge": [], "long_answer": "The FDIC offers a variety of resources for bankers, including financial education materials, data tools, documentation of laws and regulations, and information on important initiatives. Bankers can find information about FDIC deposit insurance and supervision in the Banker Resource Center, which is part of the additional FDIC resources. The FDIC is proud to be a pre-eminent source of analysis for stakeholders, although the specific types of analysis are not detailed in the provided content."}, {"knowledge": [{"content": "The FDIC provides a wealth of resources for consumers, bankers, analysts, and other stakeholders. Browse our collection of financial education materials, data tools, documentation of laws and regulations, information on important initiatives, and more.", "wikipage": "AML Topic 39"}, {"content": "Additional FDIC Resources: Consumer Resource Center, Banker Resource Center, Deposit Insurance, Supervision & Examinations.", "wikipage": "AML Topic 39"}, {"content": "Analysis: The FDIC is proud to be a pre-eminent so", "wikipage": "AML Topic 39"}], "long_answer": "The FDIC offers a variety of resources for bankers, including financial education materials, data tools, documentation of laws and regulations, and information on important initiatives.\n\nBankers can find information about FDIC deposit insurance and supervision in the Banker Resource Center, which is part of the additional FDIC resources.\n\nThe FDIC is proud to be a pre-eminent source of analysis for stakeholders, although the specific types of analysis are not detailed in the provided content."}], "sample_id": "aml-topic-39-2", "question": "What resources does the FDIC provide for bankers seeking financial education materials?", "docs": [{"id": "doc-aml-topic-39-2-2", "title": "AML Topic 39 Part 2", "text": "itional FDIC Resources\nConsumer Resource Center\nBanker Resource Center\nDeposit Insurance\nSupervision & Examinations\nLaws &