intain stability and public confidence in the nation\u2019s financial system. The FDIC ensures the security of information shared on its website by using 'https://' which confirms that you are connecting to the official website and that any information you provide is encrypted and transmitted securely. Before sharing sensitive information on a federal government website, you should verify that you are on a ."}, {"knowledge": [{"content": "The Federal Deposit Insurance Corporation (FDIC) is an independent agency created by the Congress to maintain stability and public confidence in the nation\u2019s financial system.", "wikipage": "AML Topic 43"}, {"content": "The https:// ensures that you are connecting to the official website and that any information you provide is encrypted and transmitted securely.", "wikipage": "AML Topic 43"}, {"content": "Federal government websites often end in .gov or .mil. Before sharing sensitive information, make sure you\u2019re on a federal government site.", "wikipage": "AML Topic 43"}], "long_answer": "The primary role of the FDIC is to maintain stability and public confidence in the nation\u2019s financial system.\n\nThe FDIC ensures the security of information shared on its website by using 'https://' which confirms that you are connecting to the official website and that any information you provide is encrypted and transmitted securely.\n\nBefore sharing sensitive information on a federal government website, you should verify that you are on a .gov or .mil site to ensure it\u2019s official."}], "sample_id": "aml-topic-43-1", "question": "What is the primary role of the FDIC in the financial system?", "docs": [{"id": "doc-aml-topic-43-1-2", "title": "AML Topic 43 Part 2", "text": "enu\nAbout\nThe Federal Deposit Insurance Corporation (FDIC) is an independent agency created by the Congress to maintain stability and public confidence in the nation\u2019s financial system. Learn about the FDIC\u2019s mission, leadership, history, caree