ulations documentation"], "wikipage": null}, {"context": "No context provided", "question": "How can bankers access information on FDIC's supervision and examination processes?", "short_answers": ["Banker Resource Center", "Supervision & Examinations"], "wikipage": null}, {"context": "No context provided", "question": "What programs does the FDIC offer for community banking research?", "short_answers": ["Community Banking Research Program"], "wikipage": null}], "wikipages": [{"title": "AML Topic 44", "url": "https://www.fdic.gov/resources/deposit-insurance"}], "annotations": [{"knowledge": [], "long_answer": "The FDIC provides a variety of resources for bankers, including financial education materials, data tools, documentation of laws and regulations, and information on important initiatives. Bankers can access information on the FDIC's supervision and examination processes through the Banker Resource Center and additional resources provided by the FDIC. The FDIC offers a Community Banking Research Program as part of its resources, providing research and insights into the community banking sector."}, {"knowledge": [{"content": "The FDIC provides a wealth of resources for consumers, bankers, analysts, and other stakeholders. Browse our collection of financial education materials, data tools, documentation of laws and regulations, information on important initiatives, and more.", "wikipage": "AML Topic 44"}, {"content": "Additional FDIC Resources Consumer Resource Center Banker Resource Center Deposit Insurance Supervision & Examinations Laws & Regulations Resolutions Publications Forms Data Tools Community Banking Research Program International Seminars and Training", "wikipage": "AML Topic 44"}, {"content": "Additional FDIC Resources Consumer Resource Center Banker Resource Center Deposit Insurance Supervision & Examinations Laws & Regulations Resolutions Publications Forms Data Tools Community Banking Research Program International Seminars and Training", "wikipag