 Research Program for community banking research.", "output": "Answer: The FDIC provides a wealth of resources for consumers, bankers, analysts, and other stakeholders [1].", "intermediate": ["[Retrieval]", "Answer: The FDIC provides a wealth of resources for consumers, bankers, analysts, and other stakeholders."]}, {"qa_pairs": [{"context": "No context provided", "question": "What is the FDIC's Quarterly Banking Profile and when was it last reported?", "short_answers": ["Quarterly Banking Profile", "First quarter of 2024"], "wikipage": null}, {"context": "No context provided", "question": "How much net income did FDIC-insured institutions report in December 2024?", "short_answers": ["Net income of $65.4 billion", "December 2024"], "wikipage": null}, {"context": "No context provided", "question": "Where can I find updates on the latest FDIC news and activities?", "short_answers": ["FDIC website", "News and activities"], "wikipage": null}], "wikipages": [{"title": "AML Topic 48", "url": "https://www.fdic.gov/publications"}], "annotations": [{"knowledge": [], "long_answer": "The FDIC's Quarterly Banking Profile provides insights into the performance of FDIC-insured institutions. In December 2024, FDIC-insured institutions reported a net income of $65. Updates on the latest FDIC news and activities can be found on their website, including announcements, speeches, policy changes, and details on upcoming conferences and events."}, {"knowledge": [{"content": "EVENT / May 29, 2024 Quarterly Banking Profile for First Quarter 2024", "wikipage": "AML Topic 48"}, {"content": "EVENT / December 12, 2024 FDIC-Insured Institutions Reported Net Income of $65.4 Billion", "wikipage": "AML Topic 48"}, {"content": "The FDIC publishes regular updates on news and activities. Keep up with FDIC announcements, read speeches and testimony on the latest banking issues, learn about policy changes for banks, and get the details on upcoming conferences and events.", "wikipage": "AML Topic 48"}], "long_answer": "The FDIC's Quarterly Banking Profile provides insights into the performance of FDIC-insured institutions. The last report was for the first quarter of 2024, released on May 29, 2024.\n\nIn December 2024, FDIC-insured institutions reported a net income of $65.4 billion.\n\nUpdates on the latest FDIC news and activities can be found on their website, including announcements, speeches, policy changes, and details on upcoming conferences and events."}], "sample_id": "aml-topic-48-3", "question": "What is the FDIC's Quarterly Banking Profile and when was it last reported?", "docs": [{"id": "doc-aml-topic-48-3-2", "title": "AML Topic 48 Part 2", "text": "eptember 05, 2024\nFDIC-Insured Institutions Reported Net Income of $71.5 Billion\nEVENT / May 29, 2024\nQuarterly Banking Profile for First Quarter 2024\nNews\nToggle submenu\nNews\nThe FDIC publishes regular updates on news and activities. Keep up with FDIC announcements, read speeches and testimony on the latest banking issues, learn about policy changes for banks, and get the details on upcoming conferences and events.\nFind More FDIC News\nPress Releases\nFinancial Institution Letters\nConferences & E", "score": 0.85, "summary": "eptember 05, 2024 FDIC-Insured Institutions Reported Net Income of $71.5 Billion EVENT / May 29, 2024 Quarterly Banking Profile for First Quarter 2024...", "extraction": "eptember 05, 2024\nFDIC-Insured Institutions Reported Net Income of $71.5 Billion\nEVENT / May 29, 2024\nQuarterly Banking Profile for First Quarter 2024\nNews\nToggle submenu\nNews\nThe FDIC publishes regul"}], "answer": "The FDIC's Quarterly Banking Profile provides insights into the performance of FDIC-insured institutions. In December 2024, FDIC-insured institutions reported a net income of $65. Updates on the latest FDIC news and activities can be found on their website, including announcements, speeches, policy changes, and details on upcoming conferences and events.", "output": "Answer: The FDIC's Quarterly Banking Profile is a report that provides a detailed look at the financial condition of insured banks and thrifts in the United States [1].", "intermediate": ["[Retrieval]", "Answer: The FDIC's Quarterly Banking Profile is a report that provides a detailed look at the financial condition of insured banks and thrifts in the United States."]}, {"qa_pairs": [{"context": "No context provided", "question": "What resources does the FDIC offer for bankers looking to understand regulations?", "short_answers": ["Banker Resource Center", "Laws & Regulations documentation"], "wikipage": null}, {"context": "No context provided", "question": "Where can consumers find educational materials provided by the FDIC?", "short_answers": ["Consumer Resource Center", "Financial education materials"], "wikipage": null}, {"context": "No context provided", "question": "What kind of analysis and research does the FDIC conduct on the banking industry?", "short_answers": ["Quarterly banking profiles", "Working papers"], "wikipage": null}], "wikipages": [{"title": "AML Topic 49", "url": "https://www.fdic.gov/formsdocuments"}], "annotations": [{"knowledge": [], "long_answer": "The FDIC provides a variety of resources for bankers, including documentation of laws and regulations, as well as access to the Banker Resource Center. Consumers can find educational materials through the FDIC's Consumer Resource Center, which is part of their collection of financial education resources. The FDIC conducts extensive research and analysis on the U."}, {"knowledge": [{"content": "The FDIC provides a wealth of resources for consumers, bankers, analysts, and other stakeholders... Banker Resource Center... Laws & Regulations...", "wikipage": "AML Topic 49"}, {"content": "The FDIC provides a wealth of resources for consumers, bankers, analysts, and other stakeholders... Consumer Resource Center...", "wikipage": "AML Topic 49"}, {"content": "The FDIC is proud to be a pre-eminent source of U.S. banking industry research, including quarterly banking profiles, working papers...", "wikipage": "AML Topic 49"}], "long_answer": "The FDIC provides a variety of resources for bankers, including documentation of laws and regulations, as well as access to the Banker Resource Center.\n\nConsumers can find educational materials through the FDIC's Consumer Resource Center, which is part of their collection of financial education resources.\n\nThe FDIC conducts extensive research and analysis on the U.S. banking industry, including quarterly banking profiles and working papers."}], "sample_id": "aml-topic-49-2", "question": "What resources does the FDIC offer for bankers looking to understand regulations?", "docs": [{"id": "doc-aml-topic-49-2-1", "title": "AML Topic 49 Part 1", "text": "Plaines, Ill. Assumes All Deposits of Pulaski Savings\u2026\nPODCASTS / January 06, 2025\nSmall Business Lending\nResources\nToggle submenu\nResources\nThe FDIC provides a wealth of resources for consumers, bankers, analysts, and other stakeholders. Browse our collection of financial education materials, data tools, documentation of laws and regulations, information on important initiatives, and more.\nAdditional FDIC Resources\nConsumer Resource Center\nBanker Resource Center\nDeposit Insurance\nSupervision &", "score": 0.9, "summary": "Plaines, Ill. Assumes All Deposits of Pulaski Savings\u2026 PODCASTS / January 06, 2025 Small Business Lending Resources Toggle submenu Resources The FDIC ...", "extraction": "The FDIC provides a wealth of resources for consumers, bankers, analysts, and other stakeholders... Banker Resource Center... Laws & Regulations..."}], "answer": "The FDIC provides a variety of resources for bankers, including documentation of laws and regulations, as well as access to the Banker Resource Center. Consumers can find educational materials through the FDIC's Consumer Resource Center, which is part of their collection of financial education resources. The FDIC conducts extensive research and analysis on the U.", "output": "Answer: The FDIC provides a wealth of resources for consumers, bankers, analysts, and other stakeholders [1].", "intermediate": ["[Retrieval]", "Answer: The FDIC provides a wealth of resources for consumers, bankers, analysts, and other stakeholders."]}, {"qa_pairs": [{"context": "No context provided", "question": "What is the primary purpose of the FDIC?", "short_answers": ["Maintain stability", "Public confidence in financial system"], "wikipage": null}, {"context": "No context provided", "question": "How can you verify that you are visiting the official FDIC website?", "short_answers": ["URL starts with 'https://'", "Ends with '.gov'", "Connection is secure"], "wikipage": null}, {"context": "No context provided", "question": "What recent action did the FDIC take regarding the Network of Central Banks and Supervisors for Green?", "short_answers": ["FDIC withdrew from the Network", "Press release on January 21, 2025"], "wikipage": null}], "wikipages": [{"title": "AML Topic 50", "url": "https://www.fdic.gov/resources/data-tools"}], "annotations": [{"knowledge": [], "long_answer": "The primary purpose of the FDIC is to maintain stability and public confidence in the nation\u2019s financial system. You can verify you are visiting the official FDIC website by checking that the URL starts with 'https://' and ends with '. The FDIC withdrew from the Network of Central Banks and Supervisors for Green as reported in a press release dated January 21, 2025."}, {"knowledge": [{"content": "The Federal Deposit Insurance Corporation (FDIC) is an independent agency created by the Congress to maintain stability and public confidence in the nation\u2019s financial system.", "wikipage": "AML Topic 50"}, {"content": "The .gov means it\u2019s official. Federal government websites often end in .gov or .mil. Before sharing sensitive information, make sure you\u2019re on a federal government site. The site is secure. The https:// ensures that you are connecting to the official website and that any information you provide is encrypted and transmitted securely.", "wikipage": "AML Topic 50"}, {"content": "PRESS RELEASE / January 21, 2025 FDIC Withdraws from the Network of Central Banks and Supervisors for Green\u2026", "wikipage": "AML Topic 50"}], "long_answer": "The primary purpose of the FDIC is to maintain stability and public confidence in the nation\u2019s financial system.\n\nYou can verify you are visiting the official FDIC website by checking that the URL starts with 'https://' and ends with '.gov', ensuring the connection is secure and the information is encrypted.\n\nThe FDIC withdrew from the Network of Central Banks and Supervisors for Green as reported in a press release dated January 21, 2025."}], "sample_id": "aml-topic-50-1", "question": "What is the primary purpose of the FDIC?", "docs": [{"id": "doc-aml-topic-50-1-2", "title": "AML Topic 50 Part 2", "text": "e Federal Deposit Insurance Corporation (FDIC) is an independent agency created by the Congress to maintain stability and public confidence in the nation\u2019s financial system. Learn about the FDIC\u2019s mission, leadership, history, career opportunities, and more.\nLearn More About the FDIC\nWhat We Do\nLeadership\nCareers\nInitiatives\nStrategic Plans\nFinancial Reports\nHistory\nGovernance\nOmbudsman\nDoing Business with the FDIC\nPRESS RELEASE / February 25, 2025\nFDIC-Insured Institutions Reported Return on As", "score": 0.85, "summary": "e Federal Deposit Insurance Corporation (FDIC) is an independent agency created by the Congress to maintain stability and public confidence in the nat...", "extraction": "e Federal Deposit Insurance Corporation (FDIC) is an independent agency created by the Congress to maintain stability and public confidence in the nation\u2019s financial system. Learn about the FDIC\u2019s mis"}], "answer": "The primary purpose of the FDIC is to maintain stability and public confidence in the nation\u2019s financial system. You can verify you are visiting the official FDIC website by checking that the URL starts with 'https://' and ends with '. The FDIC withdrew from the Network of Central Banks and Supervisors for Green as reported in a press release dated January 21, 2025.", "output": "Answer: The FDIC's mission is to maintain stability and public confidence in the U. S. financial system [1].", "intermediate": ["[Retrieval]", "Answer: The FDIC's mission is to maintain stability and public confidence in the U.S. financial system."]}, {"qa_pairs": [{"context": "No context provided", "question": "What are some of the regular updates provided by the FDIC?", "short_answers": ["FDIC announcements", "Speeches and testimonies", "Policy changes"], "wikipage": null}, {"context": "No context provided", "question": "How does the FDIC share information about policy changes for banks?", "short_answers": ["Announcements", "Speeches", "Testimonies"], "wikipage": null}, {"context": "No context provided", "question": "Where can one find details about upcoming FDIC conferences and events?", "short_answers": ["FDIC updates", "Conferences and events"], "wikipage": null}], "wikipages": [{"title": "AML Topic 51", "url": "https://www.fdic.gov/community-banking-research-program"}], "annotations": [{"knowledge": [], "long_answer": "The FDIC publishes regular updates on news and activities, including announcements, speeches, and testimonies on the latest banking issues, policy changes for banks, and details on upcoming conferences and events. The FDIC shares information about policy changes for banks through regular updates, which include announcements, speeches, and testimonies. Details about upcoming FDIC conferences and events can be found in their regular updates, which include sections on conferences and events."}, {"knowledge": [{"content": "The FDIC publishes regular updates on news and activities. Keep up with FDIC announcements, read speeches and testimony on the latest banking issues, learn about policy changes for banks, and get the details on upcoming conferences and events.", "wikipage": "AML Topic 51"}, {"content": "The FDIC publishes regular updates on news and activities. Keep up with FDIC announcements, read speeches and testimony on the latest banking issues, learn about policy changes for banks, and get the details on upcoming conferences and events.", "wikipage": "AML Topic 51"}, {"content": "The FDIC publishes regular updates on news and activities. Keep up with FDIC announcements, read speeches and testimony on the latest banking issues, learn about policy changes for banks, and get the details on upcoming conferences and events.", "wikipage": "AML Topic 51"}], "long_answer": "The FDIC publishes regular updates on news and activities, including announcements, speeches, and testimonies on the latest banking issues, policy changes for banks, and details on upcoming conferences and events.\n\nThe FDIC shares information about policy changes for banks through regular updates, which include announcements, speeches, and testimonies.\n\nDetails about upcoming FDIC conferences and events can be found in their regular updates, which include sections on conferences and events."}], "sample_id": "aml-topic-51-3", "question": "What are some of the regular updates provided by the FDIC?", "docs": [{"id": "doc-aml-topic-51-3-2", "title": "AML Topic 51 Part 2", "text": "65.4 Billion\nEVENT / September 05, 2024\nFDIC-Insured Institutions Reported Net Income of $71.5 Billion\nEVENT / May 29, 2024\nQuarterly Banking Profile for First Quarter 2024\nNews\nToggle submenu\nNews\nThe FDIC publishes regular updates on news and activities. Keep up with FDIC announcements, read speeches and testimony on the latest banking issues, learn about policy changes for banks, and get the details on upcoming conferences and events.\nFind More FDIC News\nPress Releases\nFinancial Institution L", "score": 0.85, "summary": "65.4 Billion EVENT / September 05, 2024 FDIC-Insured