 submenu\nResources\nThe FDIC provides a wealth of resources for consumers, bankers, analysts, and other stakeholders. Browse our collection of financial education materials, data tools, documentation of laws and regulations, information on important initiatives, and more.\nAdditional FDIC Resources\nConsumer Resource Center\nBanker Resource Center\nDeposit Insurance\nSupervision & Examina", "score": 0.9, "summary": ", Ill. Assumes All Deposits of Pulaski Savings\u2026 PODCASTS / January 06, 2025 Small Business Lending Resources Toggle submenu Resources The FDIC provide...", "extraction": "The FDIC provides a wealth of resources for consumers, bankers, analysts, and other stakeholders. Browse our collection of financial education materials, data tools, documentation of laws and regulations, information on important initiatives, and more. Additional FDIC Resources: Consumer Resource Center, Banker Resource Center, Deposit Insurance, Supervision & Examinations, Laws & Regulations, Resolutions, Publications, Forms, Data Tools, Community Banking Research Program, International Seminars and Training."}], "answer": "The FDIC provides a variety of resources for bankers, including a Banker Resource Center, documentation of laws and regulations, and supervision and examinations materials. Community banks can find research and educational resources through the FDIC's Community Banking Research Program and International Seminars and Training. Consumers can access financial education materials through the FDIC's Consumer Resource Center, which is part of a broader collection of resources offered by the FDIC.", "output": "Answer: The FDIC provides a wealth of resources for consumers, bankers, analysts, and other stakeholders [1].", "intermediate": ["[Retrieval]", "Answer: The FDIC provides a wealth of resources for consumers, bankers, analysts, and other stakeholders."]}, {"qa_pairs": [{"context": "No context provided", "question": "What types of resources does the FDIC provide for bankers and other stakeholders?", "short_answers": ["Financial education materials", "Data tools", "Laws and regulations documentation"], "wikipage": null}, {"context": "No context provided", "question": "Where can bankers find specific FDIC resources tailored to their needs?", "short_answers": ["Banker Resource Center"], "wikipage": null}, {"context": "No context provided", "question": "What kind of banking industry research does the FDIC provide?", "short_answers": ["U.S. banking industry research", "Quarterly banking analysis"], "wikipage": null}], "wikipages": [{"title": "AML Topic 61", "url": "https://www.fdic.gov/quarterly-banking-profile/fdic-quarterly-banking-profile-fourth-quarter-2024"}], "annotations": [{"knowledge": [], "long_answer": "The FDIC provides a collection of financial education materials, data tools, documentation of laws and regulations, information on important initiatives, and more. Bankers can find specific FDIC resources tailored to their needs at the Banker Resource Center, which is part of the additional FDIC resources offered. The FDIC provides U."}, {"knowledge": [{"content": "The FDIC provides a wealth of resources for consumers, bankers, analysts, and other stakeholders. Browse our collection of financial education materials, data tools, documentation of laws and regulations, information on important initiatives, and more.", "wikipage": "AML Topic 61"}, {"content": "Additional FDIC Resources: Consumer Resource Center, Banker Resource Center, Deposit Insurance, Supervision & Examinations, Laws & Regulations, Resolutions, Publications, Forms, Data Tools, Community Banking Research Program, International Seminars and Training", "wikipage": "AML Topic 61"}, {"content": "The FDIC is proud to be a pre-eminent source of U.S. banking industry research, including quarterly banking p", "wikipage": "AML Topic 61"}], "long_answer": "The FDIC provides a collection of financial education materials, data tools, documentation of laws and regulations, information on important initiatives, and more. They also offer specific resources such as the Consumer Resource Center, Banker Resource Center, Deposit Insurance, Supervision & Examinations, and more.\n\nBankers can find specific FDIC resources tailored to their needs at the Banker Resource Center, which is part of the additional FDIC resources offered.\n\nThe FDIC provides U.S. banking industry research, including quarterly banking performance analysis."}], "sample_id": "aml-topic-61-2", "question": "What types of resources does the FDIC provide for bankers and other stakeholders?", "docs": [{"id": "doc-aml-topic-61-2-1", "title": "AML Topic 61 Part 1", "text": "ary 17, 2025\nMillennium Bank, Des Plaines, Ill. Assumes All Deposits of Pulaski Savings\u2026\nPODCASTS / January 06, 2025\nSmall Business Lending\nResources\nToggle submenu\nResources\nThe FDIC provides a wealth of resources for consumers, bankers, analysts, and other stakeholders. Browse our collection of financial education materials, data tools, documentation of laws and regulations, information on important initiatives, and more.\nAdditional FDIC Resources\nConsumer Resource Center\nBanker Resource Cente", "score": 0.9, "summary": "ary 17, 2025 Millennium Bank, Des Plaines, Ill. Assumes All Deposits of Pulaski Savings\u2026 PODCASTS / January 06, 2025 Small Business Lending Resources ...", "extraction": "The FDIC provides a wealth of resources for consumers, bankers, analysts, and other stakeholders. Browse our collection of financial education materials, data tools, documentation of laws and regulations, information on important initiatives, and more."}], "answer": "The FDIC provides a collection of financial education materials, data tools, documentation of laws and regulations, information on important initiatives, and more. Bankers can find specific FDIC resources tailored to their needs at the Banker Resource Center, which is part of the additional FDIC resources offered. The FDIC provides U.", "output": "Answer: The FDIC provides a wealth of resources for consumers, bankers, analysts, and other stakeholders [1].", "intermediate": ["[Retrieval]", "Answer: The FDIC provides a wealth of resources for consumers, bankers, analysts, and other stakeholders."]}, {"qa_pairs": [{"context": "No context provided", "question": "What is the FDIC Academic Challenge, and how does it relate to financial research?", "short_answers": ["Engages academic institutions", "Promotes study of banking topics"], "wikipage": null}, {"context": "No context provided", "question": "How often does the FDIC publish the Quarterly Banking Profile, and what is its purpose?", "short_answers": ["Published quarterly", "Overview of banking industry's performance"], "wikipage": null}, {"context": "No context provided", "question": "What information can be found in the FDIC's Annual Risk Review?", "short_answers": ["Analysis of risks in banking", "Informs stakeholders about potential challenges"], "wikipage": null}], "wikipages": [{"title": "AML Topic 62", "url": "https://www.fdic.gov/quarterly-banking-profile/fdic-quarterly-banking-profile-third-quarter-2024"}], "annotations": [{"knowledge": [], "long_answer": "The FDIC Academic Challenge is an initiative by the FDIC to engage with academic institutions and students, encouraging them to explore and analyze banking issues. The FDIC publishes the Quarterly Banking Profile four times a year, corresponding to each financial quarter. The FDIC's Annual Risk Review provides an analysis of the risks facing the banking industry, including economic, financial, and operational risks."}, {"knowledge": [{"content": "FDIC Academic Challenge", "wikipage": "AML Topic 62"}, {"content": "Quarterly Banking Profile", "wikipage": "AML Topic 62"}, {"content": "Annual Risk Review", "wikipage": "AML Topic 62"}], "long_answer": "The FDIC Academic Challenge is an initiative by the FDIC to engage with academic institutions and students, encouraging them to explore and analyze banking issues. This challenge relates to financial research as it promotes the study of various banking topics, fostering a deeper understanding of financial systems.\n\nThe FDIC publishes the Quarterly Banking Profile four times a year, corresponding to each financial quarter. Its purpose is to provide a comprehensive overview of the banking industry's performance, including metrics such as return on assets and net income.\n\nThe FDIC's Annual Risk Review provides an analysis of the risks facing the banking industry, including economic, financial, and operational risks. It aims to inform stakeholders about potential challenges and developments that could impact the stability of financial institutions."}], "sample_id": "aml-topic-62-3", "question": "What is the FDIC Academic Challenge, and how does it relate to financial research?", "docs": [{"id": "doc-aml-topic-62-3-1", "title": "AML Topic 62 Part 1", "text": "ofiles, working papers, and state banking performance data. Browse our extensive research tools and reports.\nMore FDIC Analysis\nCenter for Financial Research\nConsumer Research\nFDIC National Survey of Unbanked and Underbanked Households\nQuarterly Banking Profile\nFDIC Academic Challenge\nFDIC Banking Issues in Focus\nAnnual Risk Review\nEVENT / February 25, 2025\nFDIC-Insured Institutions Reported Return on Assets of 1.11 Percent and Net Inc\u2026\nEVENT / December 12, 2024\nFDIC-Insured Institutions Reporte", "score": 0.9, "summary": "ofiles, working papers, and state banking performance data. Browse our extensive research tools and reports. More FDIC Analysis Center for Financial R...", "extraction": "FDIC Academic Challenge"}], "answer": "The FDIC Academic Challenge is an initiative by the FDIC to engage with academic institutions and students, encouraging them to explore and analyze banking issues. The FDIC publishes the Quarterly Banking Profile four times a year, corresponding to each financial quarter. The FDIC's Annual Risk Review provides an analysis of the risks facing the banking industry, including economic, financial, and operational risks.", "output": "The FDIC Academic Challenge is an annual competition that encourages students to use the FDIC's data to conduct original research on a variety of topics related to banking and financial services [1].", "intermediate": ["[Retrieval]", "The FDIC Academic Challenge is an annual competition that encourages students to use the FDIC's data to conduct original research on a variety of topics related to banking and financial services."]}, {"qa_pairs": [{"context": "No context provided", "question": "What are some key events where FDIC-insured institutions reported their financial performance?", "short_answers": ["Return on assets of 1.11% on February 25, 2025", "Net income of $65.4 billion on December 12, 2024", "Net income of $71.5 billion on September 05, 2024"], "wikipage": null}, {"context": "No context provided", "question": "Where can I find updates on FDIC's news and activities?", "short_answers": ["FDIC announcements", "Speeches and testimony on banking issues", "Policy changes and conferences"], "wikipage": null}, {"context": "No context provided", "question": "What type of content does the FDIC provide to keep the public informed?", "short_answers": ["Press releases and financial institution letters", "Conferences, events, and board matters", "Speeches, testimonies, and media campaigns"], "wikipage": null}], "wikipages": [{"title": "AML Topic 63", "url": "https://www.fdic.gov/quarterly-banking-profile/fdic-quarterly-banking-profile-second-quarter-2024"}], "annotations": [{"knowledge": [], "long_answer": "Some key events include the FDIC-insured institutions reporting a return on assets of 1. Updates on FDIC's news and activities can be found in their regular publications, including announcements, speeches, testimony on banking issues, policy changes, conferences, and events. The FDIC provides press releases, financial institution letters, conferences and events, board matters, information on natural disasters, media campaigns, speeches, statements, testimonies, podcasts, videos, and opinion editorials to keep the public informed."}, {"knowledge": [{"content": "EVENT / February 25, 2025 FDIC-Insured Institutions Reported Return on Assets of 1.11 Percent and Net Inc\u2026 EVENT / December 12, 2024 FDIC-Insured Institutions Reported Net Income of $65.4 Billion EVENT / September 05, 2024 FDIC-Insured Institutions Reported Net Income of $71.5 Billion", "wikipage": "AML Topic 63"}, {"content": "The FDIC publishes regular updates on news and activities. Keep up with FDIC announcements, read speeches and testimony on the latest banking issues, learn about policy changes for banks, and get the details on upcoming conferences and events.", "wikipage": "AML Topic 63"}, {"content": "Find More FDIC News Press Releases Financial Institution Letters Conferences & Events Board Matters Natural Disasters Media Campaigns Speeches, Statements & Testimonies Podcasts Videos Opinion Editorials", "wikipage": "AML Topic 63"}], "long_answer": "Some key events include the FDIC-insured institutions reporting a return on assets of 1.11 percent on February 25, 2025, a net income of $65.4 billion on December 12, 2024, and a net income of $71.5 billion on September 05, 2024.\n\nUpdates on FDIC's news and activities can be found in their regular publications, including announcements, speeches, testimony on banking issues, policy changes, conferences, and events.\n\nThe FDIC provides press releases, financial institution letters, conferences and events, board matters, information on natural disasters, media campaigns, speeches, statements, testimonies, podcasts, videos, and opinion editorials to keep the public informed."}], "sample_id": "aml-topic-63-3", "question": "What are some key events where FDIC-insured institutions reported their financial performance?", "docs": [{"id": "doc-aml-topic-63-3-1", "title": "AML Topic 63 Part 1", "text": "rofiles, working papers, and state banking performance data. Browse our extensive research tools and reports.\nMore FDIC Analysis\nCenter for Financial Research\nConsumer Research\nFDIC National Survey of Unbanked and Underbanked Households\nQuarterly Banking Profile\nFDIC Academic Challenge\nFDIC Banking Issues in Focus\nAnnual Risk Review\nEVENT / February 25, 2025\nFDIC-Insured Institutions Reported Return on Assets of 1.11 Percent and Net Inc\u2026\nEVENT / December 12, 2024\nFDIC-Insured Institutions Report", "score": 0.9, "summary": "rofiles, working papers, and state banking performance data. Browse our extensive research tools and reports. More FDIC Analysis Center for Financial ...", "extraction": "EVENT / February 25, 2025 FDIC-Insured Institutions Reported Return on Assets of 1.11 Percent and Net Inc\u2026 EVENT / December 12, 2024 FDIC-Insured Institutions Reported Net Income of $65.4 Billion EVENT / September 05, 2024 FDIC-Insured Institutions Reported Net Income of $71.5 Billion"}], "answer": "Some key events include the FDIC-insured institutions reporting a return on assets of 1. Updates on FDIC's news and activities can be found in their regular publications, including announcements, speeches, testimony on banking issues, policy changes, conferences, and events. The FDIC provides press releases, financial institution letters, conferences and events, board matters, information on natural disasters, media campaigns, speeches, statements, testimonies, podcasts, videos, and opinion editorials to keep the public informed.", "output": "Answer: FDIC-insured institutions reported their financial performance on December 12, 2024 and February 25, 2025 [1].", "intermediate": ["[Retrieval]", "Answer: FDIC-insured institutions reported their financial performance on December 12, 2024 and February 25, 2025."]}, {"qa_pairs": [{"context": "No context provided", "question": "What is the primary purpose of the Federal Deposit Insurance Corporation (FDIC)?", "short_answers": ["Maintain stability", "Public confidence"], "wikipage": null}, {"context": "No context provided", "question": "How can you ensure that you are securely connecting to an official FDIC website?", "short_answers": ["URL begins with 'https://'", "Ends in '.gov'"], "wikipage": null}, {"context": "No context provided", "question": "What type of information can you learn about the FDIC from their website?", "short_answers": ["Mission", "Leadership", "History", "Career opportunities"], "wikipage": null}], "wikipages": [{"title": "AML Topic 65", "url": "https://www.fdic.gov/news"}], "annotations": [{"knowledge": [], "long_answer": "The primary purpose of the Federal Deposit Insurance Corporation (FDIC) is to maintain stability and public confidence in the nation's financial system. To ensure a secure connection to an official FDIC website, check that the URL begins with 'https://' and that it ends in '. From the FDIC's website, you can learn about their mission, leadership, history, career opportunities, and more, including strategic plans, financial reports, and governance."}, {"knowledge": [{"content": "The Federal Deposit Insurance Corporation (FDIC) is an independent agency created by the Congress to maintain stability and public confidence in the nation\u2019s financial system.", "wikipage": "AML Topic 65"}, {"content": "The .gov means it\u2019s official... The https:// ensures that you are connecting to the official website and that any information you provide is encrypted and transmitted securely.", "wikipage": "AML Topic 65"}, {"content": "Learn about the FDIC\u2019s mission, leadership, history, career opportunities, and more.", "wikipage": "AML Topic 65"}], "long_answer": "The primary purpose of the Federal Deposit Insurance Corporation (FDIC) is to maintain stability and public confidence in the nation's financial system.\n\nTo ensure a secure connection to an official FDIC website, check that the URL begins with 'https://' and that it ends in '.gov', indicating it is an official government site. This ensures that any information provided is encrypted and transmitted securely.\n\nFrom the FDIC's website, you can learn about their mission, leadership, history, career opportunities, and more, including strategic plans, financial reports, and governance."}], "sample_id": "aml-topic-65-1", "question": "What is the primary purpose of the Federal Deposit Insurance Corporation (FDIC)?", "docs": [{"id": "doc-aml-topic-65-1-2", "title": "AML Topic 65 Part 2", "text": "ral Deposit Insurance Corporation (FDIC) is an independent agency created by the Congress to maintain stability and public confidence in the nation\u2019s financial system. Learn about the FDIC\u2019s mission, leadership, history, career opportunities, and more.\nLearn More About the FDIC\nWhat We Do\nLeadership\nCareers\nInitiatives\nStrategic Plans\nFinancial Reports\nHistory\nGovernance\nOmbudsman\nDoing Business with the FDIC\nPRESS RELEASE / February 25, 2025\nFDIC-Insured Institutions Reported Return on Assets o", "score": 0.85, "summary": "ral Deposit Insurance Corporation (FDIC) is an independent agency created by the Congress to maintain stability and public confidence in the nation\u2019s ...", "extraction": "ral Deposit Insurance Corporation (FDIC) is an independent agency created by the Congress to maintain stability and public confidence in the nation\u2019s financial system. Learn about the FDIC\u2019s mission, "}], "answer": "The primary purpose of the Federal Deposit Insurance Corporation (FDIC) is to maintain stability and public confidence in the nation's financial system. To ensure a secure connection to an official FDIC website, check that the URL begins with 'https://' and that it ends in '. From the FDIC's website, you can learn about their mission, leadership, history, career opportunities, and more, including strategic plans, financial reports, and governance.", "output": "Answer: The FDIC's mission is to maintain stability and public confidence in the U. S. financial system [1].", "intermediate": ["[Retrieval]", "Answer: The FDIC's mission is to maintain stability and public confidence in the U.S. financial system."]}, {"qa_pairs": [{"context": "No context provided", "question": "What is the FDIC's Quarterly Banking Profile and when was the latest report released?", "short_answers": ["Quarterly Banking Profile", "May 29, 2024"], "wikipage": null}, {"context": "No context provided", "question": "How much net income did FDIC-insured institutions report in September 2024?", "short_answers": ["$71.5 billion", "September 2024"], "wikipage": null}, {"context": "No context provided", "question": "What return on assets did FDIC-insured institutions report in February 2025?", "short_answers": ["1.11 percent", "February 2025"], "wikipage": null}], "wikipages": [{"title": "AML Topic 66", "url": "https://www.fdic.gov/news/press-releases/current.html"}], "annotations": [{"knowledge": [], "long_answer": "The FDIC's Quarterly Banking Profile is a report that provides data on the financial performance of FDIC-insured institutions. FDIC-insured institutions reported a net income of $71. In February 2025, FDIC-insured institutions reported a return on assets of 1."}, {"knowledge": [{"content": "Quarterly Banking Profile for First Quarter 2024", "wikipage": "AML Topic 66"}, {"content": "EVENT / September 05, 2024 FDIC-Insured Institutions Reported Net Income of $71.5 Billion", "wikipage": "AML Topic 66"}, {"content": "EVENT / February 25, 2025 FDIC-Insured Institutions Reported Return on Assets of 1.11 Percent", "wikipage": "AML Topic 66"}], "long_answer": "The FDIC's Quarterly Banking Profile is a report that provides data on the financial performance of FDIC-insured institutions. The latest report for the first quarter of 2024 was released on May 29, 2024.\n\nFDIC-insured institutions reported a net income of $71.5 billion in September 2024.\n\nIn February 2025, FDIC-insured institutions reported a return on assets of 1.11 percent."}], "sample_id": "aml-topic-66-3", "question": "What is the FDIC's Quarterly Banking Profile and when was the latest report released?", "docs": [{"id": "doc-aml-topic-66-3-2", "title": "AML Topic 66 Part 2", "text": "September 05, 2024\nFDIC-Insured Institutions Reported Net Income of $71.5 Billion\nEVENT / May 29, 2024\nQuarterly Banking Profile for First Quarter 2024\nNews\nToggle submenu\nNews\nThe FDIC publishes regular updates on news and activities. Keep up with FDIC announcements, read speeches and testimony on the latest banking issues, learn about policy changes for banks, and get the details on upcoming conferences and events.\nFind More FDIC News\nPress Releases\nFinancial Institution Letters\nConferences &", "score": 0.85, "summary": "September 05, 2024 FDIC-Insured Institutions Reported Net Income of $71.5 Billion EVENT / May 29, 2024 Quarterly Banking Profile for First Quarter 202...", "extraction": "September 05, 2024\nFDIC-Insured Institutions Reported Net Income of $71.5 Billion\nEVENT / May 29, 2024\nQuarterly Banking Profile for First Quarter 2024\nNews\nToggle submenu\nNews\nThe FDIC publishes regu"}], "answer": "The FDIC's Quarterly Banking Profile is a report that provides data on the financial performance of FDIC-insured institutions. FDIC-insured institutions reported a net income of $71. In February 2025, FDIC-insured institutions reported a return on assets of 1.", "output": "Answer: The FDIC's Quarterly Banking Profile is a report released quarterly that provides a statistical summary of the condition of the U. S. banking industry [1].", "intermediate": ["[Retrieval]", "Answer: The FDIC's Quarterly Banking Profile is a report released quarterly that provides a statistical summary of the condition of the U.S. banking industry."]}, {"qa_pairs": [{"context": "No context provided", "question": "What resources does the FDIC offer for bankers to help them understand deposit insurance?", "short_answers": ["Banker Resou