t resources does the FDIC offer for bankers to help them understand deposit insurance?", "docs": [{"id": "doc-aml-topic-68-2-1", "title": "AML Topic 68 Part 1", "text": "s Plaines, Ill. Assumes All Deposits of Pulaski Savings\u2026\nPODCASTS / January 06, 2025\nSmall Business Lending\nResources\nToggle submenu\nResources\nThe FDIC provides a wealth of resources for consumers, bankers, analysts, and other stakeholders. Browse our collection of financial education materials, data tools, documentation of laws and regulations, information on important initiatives, and more.\nAdditional FDIC Resources\nConsumer Resource Center\nBanker Resource Center\nDeposit Insurance\nSupervision", "score": 0.9, "summary": "s Plaines, Ill. Assumes All Deposits of Pulaski Savings\u2026 PODCASTS / January 06, 2025 Small Business Lending Resources Toggle submenu Resources The FDI...", "extraction": "The FDIC provides a wealth of resources for consumers, bankers, analysts, and other stakeholders. Additional FDIC Resources: Consumer Resource Center, Banker Resource Center, Deposit Insurance..."}], "answer": "The FDIC provides a Banker Resource Center, which includes information on deposit insurance, among other resources. Stakeholders can find FDIC documentation on laws and regulations in the resources section provided by the FDIC. Yes, the FDIC offers International Seminars and Training as part of its resources.", "output": "Answer: The FDIC offers a wealth of resources for consumers, bankers, analysts, and other stakeholders [1].", "intermediate": ["[Retrieval]", "Answer: The FDIC offers a wealth of resources for consumers, bankers, analysts, and other stakeholders."]}, {"qa_pairs": [{"context": "No context provided", "question": "What kind of financial performance data does the FDIC provide in their reports?", "short_answers": ["Return on assets", "Net income figures"], "wikipage": null}, {"context": "No context provided", "question": "How can I stay updated with the latest news and policy changes from the FDIC?", "short_answers": ["FDIC announcements", "Policy changes"], "wikipage": null}, {"context": "No context provided", "question": "What resources does the FDIC offer for understanding banking issues and risks?", "short_answers": ["Quarterly Banking Profile", "Annual Risk Review"], "wikipage": null}], "wikipages": [{"title": "AML Topic 69", "url": "https://www.fdic.gov/news/board-matters"}], "annotations": [{"knowledge": [], "long_answer": "The FDIC provides financial performance data such as the return on assets and net income of FDIC-insured institutions. You can stay updated with the latest FDIC news and policy changes by following their regular updates, which include announcements, speeches, testimony on banking issues, policy changes, and details on conferences and events. The FDIC offers various resources for understanding banking issues and risks, including the Quarterly Banking Profile, Annual Risk Review, and other reports like the FDIC Banking Issues in Focus."}, {"knowledge": [{"content": "EVENT / February 25, 2025 FDIC-Insured Institutions Reported Return on Assets of 1.11 Percent and Net Inc\u2026 EVENT / December 12, 2024 FDIC-Insured Institutions Reported Net Income of $65.4 Billion EVENT / September 05, 2024 FDIC-Insured Institutions Reported Net Income of $71.5 Billion", "wikipage": "AML Topic 69"}, {"content": "The FDIC publishes regular updates on news and activities. Keep up with FDIC announcements, read speeches and testimony on the latest banking issues, learn about policy changes for banks, and get the details on upcoming conferences and events.", "wikipage": "AML Topic 69"}, {"content": "More FDIC Analysis Center for Financial Research Consumer Research FDIC National Survey of Unbanked and Underbanked Households Quarterly Banking Profile FDIC Academic Challenge FDIC Banking Issues in Focus Annual Risk Review", "wikipage": "AML Topic 69"}], "long_answer": "The FDIC provides financial performance data such as the return on assets and net income of FDIC-insured institutions. For example, FDIC-insured institutions reported a return on assets of 1.11 percent and net income figures like $65.4 billion and $71.5 billion in recent reports.\n\nYou can stay updated with the latest FDIC news and policy changes by following their regular updates, which include announcements, speeches, testimony on banking issues, policy changes, and details on conferences and events.\n\nThe FDIC offers various resources for understanding banking issues and risks, including the Quarterly Banking Profile, Annual Risk Review, and other reports like the FDIC Banking Issues in Focus."}], "sample_id": "aml-topic-69-3", "question": "What kind of financial performance data does the FDIC provide in their reports?", "docs": [{"id": "doc-aml-topic-69-3-2", "title": "AML Topic 69 Part 2", "text": "September 05, 2024\nFDIC-Insured Institutions Reported Net Income of $71.5 Billion\nEVENT / May 29, 2024\nQuarterly Banking Profile for First Quarter 2024\nNews\nToggle submenu\nNews\nThe FDIC publishes regular updates on news and activities. Keep up with FDIC announcements, read speeches and testimony on the latest banking issues, learn about policy changes for banks, and get the details on upcoming conferences and events.\nFind More FDIC News\nPress Releases\nFinancial Institution Letters\nConferences &", "score": 0.85, "summary": "September 05, 2024 FDIC-Insured Institutions Reported Net Income of $71.5 Billion EVENT / May 29, 2024 Quarterly Banking Profile for First Quarter 202...", "extraction": "September 05, 2024\nFDIC-Insured Institutions Reported Net Income of $71.5 Billion\nEVENT / May 29, 2024\nQuarterly Banking Profile for First Quarter 2024\nNews\nToggle submenu\nNews\nThe FDIC publishes regu"}], "answer": "The FDIC provides financial performance data such as the return on assets and net income of FDIC-insured institutions. You can stay updated with the latest FDIC news and policy changes by following their regular updates, which include announcements, speeches, testimony on banking issues, policy changes, and details on conferences and events. The FDIC offers various resources for understanding banking issues and risks, including the Quarterly Banking Profile, Annual Risk Review, and other reports like the FDIC Banking Issues in Focus.", "output": "Answer: The FDIC provides financial performance data in their reports, such as the Quarterly Banking Profile, which provides quarterly financial data on insured institutions, and the Summary of Deposits, which provides annual data on the number and type of deposit accounts at insured institutions [1].", "intermediate": ["[Retrieval]", "Answer: The FDIC provides financial performance data in their reports, such as the Quarterly Banking Profile, which provides quarterly financial data on insured institutions, and the Summary of Deposits, which provides annual data on the number and type of deposit accounts at insured institutions."]}, {"qa_pairs": [{"context": "No context provided", "question": "What types of reports and tools does the FDIC offer for financial analysis?", "short_answers": ["Center for Financial Research", "Quarterly Banking Profile"], "wikipage": null}, {"context": "No context provided", "question": "How can I stay updated on the latest FDIC news and activities?", "short_answers": ["FDIC announcements", "policy changes for banks"], "wikipage": null}, {"context": "No context provided", "question": "What kind of financial performance data is available from FDIC-insured institutions?", "short_answers": ["Return on assets of 1.11%", "Net income of $65.4 billion"], "wikipage": null}], "wikipages": [{"title": "AML Topic 73", "url": "https://www.fdic.gov/news/podcasts"}], "annotations": [{"knowledge": [], "long_answer": "The FDIC offers various research tools and reports, including the Center for Financial Research, Consumer Research, the FDIC National Survey of Unbanked and Underbanked Households, the Quarterly Banking Profile, the FDIC Academic Challenge, and the FDIC Banking Issues in Focus. You can stay updated on the latest FDIC news and activities by following their regular updates, reading speeches and testimony on banking issues, learning about policy changes for banks, and checking details on upcoming conferences and events. FDIC-insured institutions reported a return on assets of 1."}, {"knowledge": [{"content": "Browse our extensive research tools and reports. More FDIC Analysis Center for Financial Research Consumer Research FDIC National Survey of Unbanked and Underbanked Households Quarterly Banking Profile FDIC Academic Challenge FDIC Banking Issues in Focus", "wikipage": "AML Topic 73"}, {"content": "The FDIC publishes regular updates on news and activities. Keep up with FDIC announcements, read speeches and testimony on the latest banking issues, learn about policy changes for banks, and get the details on upcoming conferences and events.", "wikipage": "AML Topic 73"}, {"content": "EVENT / February 25, 2025 FDIC-Insured Institutions Reported Return on Assets of 1.11 Percent and Net Inc\u2026 EVENT / December 12, 2024 FDIC-Insured Institutions Reported Net Income of $65.4 Billion EVENT / September 05, 2024 FDIC-Insured Institutions Reported Net Income of $71.5 Billion", "wikipage": "AML Topic 73"}], "long_answer": "The FDIC offers various research tools and reports, including the Center for Financial Research, Consumer Research, the FDIC National Survey of Unbanked and Underbanked Households, the Quarterly Banking Profile, the FDIC Academic Challenge, and the FDIC Banking Issues in Focus.\n\nYou can stay updated on the latest FDIC news and activities by following their regular updates, reading speeches and testimony on banking issues, learning about policy changes for banks, and checking details on upcoming conferences and events.\n\nFDIC-insured institutions reported a return on assets of 1.11 percent and net incomes of $65.4 billion and $71.5 billion in their respective reports."}], "sample_id": "aml-topic-73-3", "question": "What types of reports and tools does the FDIC offer for financial analysis?", "docs": [{"id": "doc-aml-topic-73-3-1", "title": "AML Topic 73 Part 1", "text": "erformance data. Browse our extensive research tools and reports.\nMore FDIC Analysis\nCenter for Financial Research\nConsumer Research\nFDIC National Survey of Unbanked and Underbanked Households\nQuarterly Banking Profile\nFDIC Academic Challenge\nFDIC Banking Issues in Focus\nAnnual Risk Review\nEVENT / February 25, 2025\nFDIC-Insured Institutions Reported Return on Assets of 1.11 Percent and Net Inc\u2026\nEVENT / December 12, 2024\nFDIC-Insured Institutions Reported Net Income of $65.4 Billion\nEVENT / Septe", "score": 0.9, "summary": "erformance data. Browse our extensive research tools and reports. More FDIC Analysis Center for Financial Research Consumer Research FDIC National Sur...", "extraction": "Browse our extensive research tools and reports. More FDIC Analysis Center for Financial Research Consumer Research FDIC National Survey of Unbanked and Underbanked Households Quarterly Banking Profile FDIC Academic Challenge FDIC Banking Issues in Focus"}], "answer": "The FDIC offers various research tools and reports, including the Center for Financial Research, Consumer Research, the FDIC National Survey of Unbanked and Underbanked Households, the Quarterly Banking Profile, the FDIC Academic Challenge, and the FDIC Banking Issues in Focus. You can stay updated on the latest FDIC news and activities by following their regular updates, reading speeches and testimony on banking issues, learning about policy changes for banks, and checking details on upcoming conferences and events. FDIC-insured institutions reported a return on assets of 1.", "output": "The FDIC offers a variety of reports and tools for financial analysis, including the Quarterly Banking Profile, the FDIC National Survey of Unbanked and Underbanked Households, the FDIC Banking Issues in Focus, the FDIC National Risk Review, and the FDIC-Insured Institutions Report [1].", "intermediate": ["[Retrieval]", "The FDIC offers a variety of reports and tools for financial analysis, including the Quarterly Banking Profile, the FDIC National Survey of Unbanked and Underbanked Households, the FDIC Banking Issues in Focus, the FDIC National Risk Review, and the FDIC-Insured Institutions Report."]}, {"qa_pairs": [{"context": "No context provided", "question": "What type of performance data does the FDIC provide for banking institutions?", "short_answers": ["banking performance data", "research tools and reports"], "wikipage": null}, {"context": "No context provided", "question": "How often does the FDIC release updates on banking issues and activities?", "short_answers": ["regular updates", "announcements and events"], "wikipage": null}, {"context": "No context provided", "question": "What are some of the resources available for understanding FDIC policy changes?", "short_answers": ["press releases", "policy fact sheets"], "wikipage": null}], "wikipages": [{"title": "AML Topic 75", "url": "https://www.fdic.gov/news/editorials"}], "annotations": [{"knowledge": [], "long_answer": "The FDIC provides banking performance data, including reports and extensive research tools related to financial institutions. The FDIC publishes regular updates on news and activities, including announcements, speeches, testimonies, policy changes, and details on conferences and events. Resources available for understanding FDIC policy changes include press releases, financial institution letters, speeches, statements, testimonies, policy fact sheets, and more."}, {"knowledge": [{"content": "banking performance data. Browse our extensive research tools and reports.", "wikipage": "AML Topic 75"}, {"content": "The FDIC publishes regular updates on news and activities. Keep up with FDIC announcements, read speeches and testimony on the latest banking issues, learn about policy changes for banks, and get the details on upcoming conferences and events.", "wikipage": "AML Topic 75"}, {"content": "Press Releases, Financial Institution Letters, Conferences & Events, Board Matters, Natural Disasters, Media Campaigns, Speeches, Statements & Testimonies, Podcasts, Videos, Opinion Editorials, Policy Fact Sheets", "wikipage": "AML Topic 75"}], "long_answer": "The FDIC provides banking performance data, including reports and extensive research tools related to financial institutions.\n\nThe FDIC publishes regular updates on news and activities, including announcements, speeches, testimonies, policy changes, and details on conferences and events.\n\nResources available for understanding FDIC policy changes include press releases, financial institution letters, speeches, statements, testimonies, policy fact sheets, and more."}], "sample_id": "aml-topic-75-3", "question": "What type of performance data does the FDIC provide for banking institutions?", "docs": [{"id": "doc-aml-topic-75-3-1", "title": "AML Topic 75 Part 1", "text": "banking performance data. Browse our extensive research tools and reports.\nMore FDIC Analysis\nCenter for Financial Research\nConsumer Research\nFDIC National Survey of Unbanked and Underbanked Households\nQuarterly Banking Profile\nFDIC Academic Challenge\nFDIC Banking Issues in Focus\nAnnual Risk Review\nEVENT / February 25, 2025\nFDIC-Insured Institutions Reported Return on Assets of 1.11 Percent and Net Inc\u2026\nEVENT / December 12, 2024\nFDIC-Insured Institutions Reported Net Income of $65.4 Billion\nEVEN", "score": 0.9, "summary": "banking performance data. Browse our extensive research tools and reports. More FDIC Analysis Center for Financial Research Consumer Research FDIC Nat...", "extraction": "banking performance data. Browse our extensive research tools and reports."}], "answer": "The FDIC provides banking performance data, including reports and extensive research tools related to financial institutions. The FDIC publishes regular updates on news and activities, including announcements, speeches, testimonies, policy changes, and details on conferences and events. Resources available for understanding FDIC policy changes include press releases, financial institution letters, speeches, statements, testimonies, policy fact sheets, and more.", "output": "The FDIC provides performance data for banking institutions in the form of the Quarterly Banking Profile, which includes data on a bank's income, assets, and liabilities, as well as other financial metrics such as return on assets and net interest margin [1].", "intermediate": ["[Retrieval]", "The FDIC provides performance data for banking institutions in the form of the Quarterly Banking Profile, which includes data on a bank's income, assets, and liabilities, as well as other financial metrics such as return on assets and net interest margin."]}, {"qa_pairs": [{"context": "No context provided", "question": "What are some of the regular updates provided by the FDIC on banking issues?", "short_answers": ["FDIC announcements", "Policy changes for banks"], "wikipage": null}, {"context": "No context provided", "question": "What kind of research does the FDIC conduct related to consumer banking?", "short_answers": ["Consumer research", "Survey of Unbanked and Underbanked Households"], "wikipage": null}, {"context": "No context provided", "question": "How does the FDIC engage with the academic community?", "short_answers": ["FDIC Academic Challenge", "Engagement with academia"], "wikipage": null}], "wikipages": [{"title": "AML Topic 77", "url": "https://www.fdic.gov/search/help.html"}], "annotations": [{"knowledge": [], "long_answer": "The FDIC provides regular updates on news and activities, including announcements, speeches and testimony on the latest banking issues, policy changes for banks, and details on upcoming conferences and events. The FDIC conducts consumer research, including the FDIC National Survey of Unbanked and Underbanked Households, to understand consumer banking trends. The FDIC engages with the academic community through initiatives like the FDIC Academic Challenge, which encourages research and discussion on banking issues."}, {"knowledge": [{"content": "The FDIC publishes regular updates on news and activities. Keep up with FDIC announcements, read speeches and testimony on the latest banking issues, learn about policy changes for banks, and get the details on upcoming conferences and events.", "wikipage": "AML Topic 77"}, {"content": "Consumer Research FDIC National Survey of Unbanked and Underbanked Households", "wikipage": "AML Topic 77"}, {"content": "FDIC Academic Challenge", "wikipage": "AML Topic 77"}], "long_answer": "The FDIC provides regular updates on news and activities, including announcements, speeches and testimony on the latest banking issues, policy changes for banks, and details on upcoming conferences and events.\n\nThe FDIC conducts consumer research, including the FDIC National Survey of Unbanked and Underbanked Households, to understand consumer banking trends.\n\nThe FDIC engages with the academic community through initiatives like the FDIC Academic Challenge, which encourages research and discussion on banking issues."}], "sample_id": "aml-topic-77-3", "question": "What are some of the regular updates provided by the FDIC on banking issues?", "docs": [{"id": "doc-aml-topic-77-3-2", "title": "AML Topic 77 Part 2", "text": "/ September 05, 2024\nFDIC-Insured Institutions Reported Net Income of $71.5 Billion\nEVENT / May 29, 2024\nQuarterly Banking Profile for First Quarter 2024\nNews\nToggle submenu\nNews\nThe FDIC publishes regular updates on news and activities. Keep up with FDIC announcements, read speeches and testimony on the latest banking issues, learn about policy changes for banks, and get the details on upcoming conferences and events.\nFind More FDIC News\nPress Releases\nFinancial Institution Letters\nConferences", "score": 0.85, "summary": "/ September 05, 2024 FDIC-Insured Institutions Reported Net Income of $71.5 Billion EVENT / May 29, 2024 Quarterly Banking Profile for First Quarter 2...", "extraction": "/ September 05, 2024\nFDIC-Insured Institutions Reported Net Income of $71.5 Billion\nEVENT / May 29, 2024\nQuarterly Banking Profile for First Quarter 2024\nNews\nToggle submenu\nNews\nThe FDIC publishes re"}], "answer": "The FDIC provides regular updates on news and activities, including announcements, speeches and testimony on the latest banking issues, policy changes for banks, and details on upcoming conferences and events. The FDIC conducts consumer research, including the FDIC National Survey of Unbanked and Underbanked Households, to understand consumer banking trends. The FDIC engages with the academic community through initiatives like the FDIC Academic Challenge, which encourages research and discussion on banking issues.", "output": "Answer: The FDIC publishes regular updates on news and activities [1].", "intermediate": ["[Retrieval]", "Answer: The FDIC publishes regular updates on news and activities."]}, {"qa_pairs": [{"context": "No context provided", "question": "What resources does the FDIC offer for financial education and regulatory compliance?", "short_answers": ["Financial education materials", "Data tools", "Laws and regulations documentation"], "wikipage": null}, {"context": "No context provided", "question": "Where can bankers find specific resources tailored for their needs from the FDIC?", "short_answers": ["Banker Resource Center"], "wikipage": null}, {"context": "No context provided", "question": "What kind of research and analysis does the FDIC provide on the U.S. banking industry?", "short_answers": ["Quarterly banking profiles", "Working papers", "State bank analysis"], "wikipage": null}], "wikipages": [{"title": "AML Topic 80", "url": "https://www.fdic.gov/news/board/"}], "annotations": [{"knowledge": [], "long_answer": "The FDIC offers a variety of resources for financial education and regulatory compliance, including financial education materials, data tools, documentation of laws and regulations, and information on important initiatives. Bankers can find specific resources tailored for their needs at the Banker Resource Center provided by the FDIC. The FDIC provides research and analysis on the U."}, {"knowledge": [{"content": "The FDIC provides a wealth of resources for consumers, bankers, analysts, and other stakeholders. Browse our collection of financial education materials, data tools, documentation of laws and regulations, information on important initiatives, and more.", "wikipage": "AML Topic 80"}, {"content": "Additional FDIC Resources: Consumer Resource Center, Banker Resource Center, Deposit Insurance, Supervision & Examinations, Laws & Regulations, Resolutions, Publications, Forms, Data Tools, Community Banking Research Program, International Seminars and Training", "wikipage": "AML Topic 80"}, {"content": "The FDIC is proud to be a pre-eminent source of U.S. banking industry research, including quarterly banking profiles, working papers, and state bank", "wikipage": "AML Topic 80"}], "long_answer": "The FDIC offers a variety of resources for financial education and regulatory compliance, including financial education materials, data tools, documentation of laws and regulations, and information on important initiatives.\n\nBankers can find specific resources tailored for their needs at the Banker Resource Center provided by the FDIC.\n\nThe FDIC provides research and analysis on the U.S. banking industry, including quarterly banking profiles, working papers, and state bank analysis."}], "sample_id": "aml-topic-80-2", "question": "What resources does the FDIC offer for financial education and regulatory compliance?", "docs": [{"id": "doc-aml-topic-80-2-1", "title": "AML Topic 80 Part 1", "text": "es, Ill. Assumes All Deposits of Pulaski Savings\u2026\nPODCASTS / January 06, 2025\nSmall Business Lending\nResources\nToggle submenu\nResources\nThe FDIC provides a wealth of resources for consumers, bankers, analysts, and other stakeholders. Browse our collection of financial education materials, data tools, documentation of laws and regulations, information on important initiatives, and more.\nAdditional FDIC Resources\nConsumer Resource Center\nBanker Resource Center\nDeposit Insurance\nSupervision & Exami", "score": 0.9, "summary": "es, Ill. Assumes All Deposits of Pulaski Savings\u2026 PODCASTS / January 06, 2025 Small Business Lending Resources Toggle submenu Resources The FDIC provi...", "extraction": "The FDIC provides a wealth of resources for consumers, bankers, analysts, and other stakeholders. Browse our collection of financial education materials, data tools, documentation of laws and regulations, information on important initiatives, and more."}], "answer": "The FDIC offers a variety of resources for financial education and regulatory compliance, including financial education materials, data tools, documentation of laws and regulations, and information on important initiatives. Bankers can find specific resources tailored for their needs at the Banker Resource Center provided by the FDIC. The FDIC provides research and analysis on the U.", "output": "Answer: The FDIC provides a wealth of resources for consumers, bankers, analysts, and other stakeholders [1].", "intermediate": ["[Retrieval]", "Answer: The FDIC provides a wealth of resources for consumers, bankers, analysts, and other stakeholders."]}, {"qa_pairs": [{"context": "No context provided", "question": "What kind of data does the FDIC provide in their Quarterly Banking Profile?", "short_answers": ["Performance data of FDIC-insured institutions", "Return on assets and net income figures"], "wikipage": null}, {"context": "No context provided", "question": "How does the FDIC keep stakeholders informed about banking issues and policy changes?", "short_answers": ["Regular updates and announcements", "Speeches and testimony on banking issues"], "wikipage": null}, {"context": "No context provided", "question": "What types of events and reports does the FDIC host or release that are relevant to financial institutions?", "short_answers": ["Conferences and events", "Quarterly Banking Profile and Annual Risk Review"], "wikipage": null}], "wikipages": [{"title": "AML Topic 82", "url": "https://www.fdic.gov/contact/regional-offices/"}], "annotations": [{"knowledge": [], "long_answer": "The FDIC's Quarterly Banking Profile includes data on the performance of FDIC-insured institutions, such as return on assets and net income figures. The FDIC keeps stakeholders informed through regular updates, announcements, speeches, testimony, policy changes, and details on upcoming conferences and events. The FDIC hosts events such as conferences and releases reports like the Quarterly Banking Profile and Annual Risk Review, which are relevant to financial institutions."}, {"knowledge": [{"content": "Quarterly Banking Profile for First Quarter 2024", "wikipage": "AML Topic 82"}, {"content": "The FDIC publishes regular updates on news and activities. Keep up with FDIC announcements, read speeches and testimony on the latest banking issues, learn about policy changes for banks, and get the details on upcoming conferences and events.", "wikipage": "AML Topic 82"}, {"content": "Conferences & Events, Quarterly Banking Profile, Annual Risk Review", "wikipage": "AML Topic 82"}], "long_answer": "The FDIC's Quarterly Banking Profile includes data on the performance of FDIC-insured institutions, such as return on assets and net income figures.\n\nThe FDIC keeps stakeholders informed through regular updates, announcements, speeches, testimony, policy changes, and details on upcoming conferences and events.\n\nThe FDIC hosts events such as conferences and releases reports like the Quarterly Banking Profile and Annual Risk Review, which are relevant to financial institutions."}], "sample_id": "aml-topic-82-3", "question": "What kind of data does the FDIC provide in their Quarterly Banking Profile?", "docs": [{"id": "doc-aml-topic-82-3-1", "title": "AML Topic 82 Part 1", "text": "rking papers, and state banking performance data. Browse our extensive research tools and reports.\nMore FDIC Analysis\nCenter for Financial Research\nConsumer Research\nFDIC National Survey of Unbanked and Underbanked Households\nQuarterly Banking Profile\nFDIC Academic Challenge\nFDIC Banking Issues in Focus\nAnnual Risk Review\nEVENT / February 25, 2025\nFDIC-Insured Institutions Reported Return on Assets of 1.11 Percent and Net Inc\u2026\nEVENT / December 12, 2024\nFDIC-Insured Institutions Reported Net Inco", "score": 0.9, "summary": "rking papers, and state banking performance data. Browse our extensive research tools and reports. More FDIC Analysis Center for Financial Research Co...", "extraction": "Quarterly Banking Profile for First Quarter 2024"}], "answer": "The FDIC's Quarterly Banking Profile includes data on the performance of FDIC-insured institutions, such as return on assets and net income figures. The FDIC keeps stakeholders informed through regular updates, announcements, speeches, testimony, policy changes, and details on upcoming conferences and events. The FDIC hosts events such as conferences and releases reports like the Quarterly Banking Profile and Annual Risk Review, which are relevant to financial institutions.", "output": "Answer: The FDIC provides data on the number of insured institutions, insured deposits, and the number of branches in their Quarterly Banking Profile [1].", "intermediate": ["[Retrieval]", "Answer: The FDIC provides data on the number of insured institutions, insured deposits, and the number of branches in their Quarterly Banking Profile."]}, {"qa_pairs": [{"context": "No context provided", "question": "What resources does the FDIC offer to bankers for compliance and operational guidance?", "short_answers": ["Banker Resource Center", "Deposit Insurance", "Supervision & Examinations"], "wikipage": null}, {"context": "No context provided", "question": "How can the FDIC's data tools be utilized by financial analysts?", "short_answers": ["Access financial education materials", "Documentation of laws and regulations", "Important initiatives"], "wikipage": null}, {"context": "No context provided", "question": "What educational programs does the FDIC offer for international banking professionals?", "short_answers": ["International seminars", "Training programs"], "wikipage": null}], "wikipages": [{"title": "AML Topic 84", "url": "https://www.fdic.gov/about/initiatives/trust-through-transparency/"}], "annotations": [{"knowledge": [], "long_answer": "The FDIC offers a variety of resources for bankers, including the Banker Resource Center, which provides information on deposit insurance, supervision and examinations, laws and regulations, resolutions, and more. Financial analysts can utilize the FDIC's data tools to access a wide range of financial education materials, documentation of laws and regulations, and important initiatives. The FDIC offers international seminars and training programs as part of its resources."}, {"knowledge": [{"content": "The FDIC provides a wealth of resources for consumers, bankers, analysts, and other stakeholders. Browse our collection of financial education materials, data tools, documentation of laws and regulations, information on important initiatives, and more. Additional FDIC Resources: Consumer Resource Center, Banker Resource Center, Deposit Insurance, Supervision & Examinations, Laws & Regulations, Resolutions, Publications, Forms, Data Tools, Community Banking Research Program, International Seminars and Training.", "wikipage": "AML Topic 84"}, {"content": "The FDIC provides a wealth of resources for consumers, bankers, analysts, and other stakeholders. Browse our collection of financial education materials, data tools, documentation of laws and regulations, information on important initiatives, and more.", "wikipage": "AML Topic 84"}, {"content": "Additional FDIC Resources: Consumer Resource Center, Banker Resource Center, Deposit Insurance, Supervision & Examinations, Laws & Regulations, Resolutions, Publications, Forms, Data Tools, Community Banking Research Program, International Seminars and Training.", "wikipage": "AML Topic 84"}], "long_answer": "The FDIC offers a variety of resources for bankers, including the Banker Resource Center, which provides information on deposit insurance, supervision and examinations, laws and regulations, resolutions, and more.\n\nFinancial analysts can utilize the FDIC's data tools to access a wide range of financial education materials, documentation of laws and regulations, and important initiatives. These tools support comprehensive analysis and research within the banking industry.\n\nThe FDIC offers international seminars and training programs as part of its resources. These programs are designed to educate and train international banking professionals on various aspects of banking and financial regulations."}], "sample_id": "aml-topic-84-2", "question": "What resources does the FDIC offer to bankers for compliance and operational guidance?", "docs": [{"id": "doc-aml-topic-84-2-1", "title": "AML Topic 84 Part 1", "text": "nk, Des Plaines, Ill. Assumes All Deposits of Pulaski Savings\u2026\nPODCASTS / January 06, 2025\nSmall Business Lending\nResources\nToggle submenu\nResources\nThe FDIC provides a wealth of resources for consumers, bankers, analysts, and other stakeholders. Browse our collection of financial education materials, data tools, documentation of laws and regulations, information on important initiatives, and more.\nAdditional FDIC Resources\nConsumer Resource Center\nBanker Resource Center\nDeposit Insurance\nSuperv", "score": 0.9, "summary": "nk, Des Plaines, Ill. Assumes All Deposits of Pulaski Savings\u2026 PODCASTS / January 06, 2025 Small Business Lending Resources Toggle submenu Resources T...", "extraction": "The FDIC provides a wealth of resources for consumers, bankers, analysts, and other stakeholders. Browse our collection of financial education materials, data tools, documentation of laws and regulations, information on important initiatives, and more. Additional FDIC Resources: Consumer Resource Center, Banker Resource Center, Deposit Insurance, Supervision & Examinations, Laws & Regulations, Resolutions, Publications, Forms, Data Tools, Community Banking Research Program, International Seminars and Training."}], "answer": "The FDIC offers a variety of resources for bankers, including the Banker Resource Center, which provides information on deposit insurance, supervision and examinations, laws and regulations, resolutions, and more. Financial analysts can utilize the FDIC's data tools to access a wide range of financial education materials, documentation of laws and regulations, and important initiatives. The FDIC offers international seminars and training programs as part of its resources.", "output": "Answer: The FDIC provides a wealth of resources for consumers, bankers, analysts, and other stakeholders [1].", "intermediate": ["[Retrieval]", "Answer: The FDIC provides a wealth of resources for consumers, bankers, analysts, and other stakeholders."]}, {"qa_pairs": [{"context": "No context provided", "question": "What is the FDIC's Quarterly Banking Profile and when was the first quarter 2024 report released?", "short_answers": ["Quarterly Banking Profile", "May 29, 2024"], "wikipage": null}, {"context": "No context provided", "question": "How much net income did FDIC-insured institutions report for the third quarter of 2024?", "short_answers": ["$71.5 billion", "third quarter 2024"], "wikipage": null}, {"context": "No context provided", "question": "What was the return on assets for FDIC-insured institutions as reported in February 2025?", "short_answers": ["1.11 percent", "February 2025"], "wikipage": null}], "wikipages": [{"title": "AML Topic 87", "url": "https://www.fdic.gov/resources/consumers/#connecting"}], "annotations": [{"knowledge": [], "long_answer": "The FDIC's Quarterly Banking Profile provides detailed analysis and data on the performance of FDIC-insured institutions. FDIC-insured institutions reported a net income of $71. In February 2025, FDIC-insured institutions reported a return on assets of 1."}, {"knowledge": [{"content": "EVENT / May 29, 2024 Quarterly Banking Profile for First Quarter 2024", "wikipage": "AML Topic 87"}, {"content": "EVENT / September 05, 2024 FDIC-Insured Institutions Reported Net Income of $71.5 Billion", "wikipage": "AML Topic 87"}, {"content": "EVENT / February 25, 2025 FDIC-Insured Institutions Reported Return on Assets of 1.11 Percent", "wikipage": "AML Topic 87"}], "long_answer": "The FDIC's Quarterly Banking Profile provides detailed analysis and data on the performance of FDIC-insured institutions. The report for the first quarter of 2024 was released on May 29, 2024.\n\nFDIC-insured institutions reported a net income of $71.5 billion for the third quarter of 2024.\n\nIn February 2025, FDIC-insured institutions reported a return on assets of 1.11 percent."}], "sample_id": "aml-topic-87-3", "question": "What is the FDIC's Quarterly Banking Profile and when was the first quarter 2024 report released?", "docs": [{"id": "doc-aml-topic-87-3-2", "title": "AML Topic 87 Part 2", "text": "n\nEVENT / September 05, 2024\nFDIC-Insured Institutions Reported Net Income of $71.5 Billion\nEVENT / May 29, 2024\nQuarterly Banking Profile for First Quarter 2024\nNews\nToggle submenu\nNews\nThe FDIC publishes regular updates on news and activities. Keep up with FDIC announcements, read speeches and testimony on the latest banking issues, learn about policy changes for banks, and get the details on upcoming conferences and events.\nFind More FDIC News\nPress Releases\nFinancial Institution Letters\nConf", "score": 0.85, "summary": "n EVENT / September 05, 2024 FDIC-Insured Institutions Reported Net Income of $71.5 Billion EVENT / May 29, 2024 Quarterly Banking Profile for First Q...", "extraction": "n\nEVENT / September 05, 2024\nFDIC-Insured Institutions Reported Net Income of $71.5 Billion\nEVENT / May 29, 2024\nQuarterly Banking Profile for First Quarter 2024\nNews\nToggle submenu\nNews\nThe FDIC publ"}], "answer": "The FDIC's Quarterly Banking Profile provides detailed analysis and data on the performance of FDIC-insured institutions. FDIC-insured institutions reported a net income of $71. In February 2025, FDIC-insured institutions reported a return on assets of 1.", "output": "The FDIC's Quarterly Banking Profile is a report that provides a summary of the financial condition of insured U. S. commercial banks and thrift institutions [1].", "intermediate": ["[Retrieval]", "The FDIC's Quarterly Banking Profile is a report that provides a summary of the financial condition of insured U.S. commercial banks and thrift institutions."]}, {"qa_pairs": [{"context": "No context provided", "question": "What type of reports does the FDIC provide to analyze banking performance?", "short_answers": ["Quarterly Banking Profile", "Annual Risk Review", "Research tools and reports"], "wikipage": null}, {"context": "No context provided", "question": "How often does the FDIC release updates on banking issues and policy changes?", "short_answers": ["Regular updates", "Announcements and policy changes"], "wikipage": null}, {"context": "No context provided", "question": "What were the reported net incomes for FDIC-insured institutions in 2024?", "short_answers": ["$65.4 billion in December 2024", "$71.5 billion in September 2024"], "wikipage": null}], "wikipages": [{"title": "AML Topic 91", "url": "https://www.fdic.gov/about/financial-reports"}], "annotations": [{"knowledge": [], "long_answer": "The FDIC provides various reports to analyze banking performance, including the Quarterly Banking Profile, Annual Risk Review, and other research tools and reports. The FDIC publishes regular updates on news and activities, which include announcements, speeches, testimony on banking issues, policy changes, and details on upcoming conferences and events. In 2024, FDIC-insured institutions reported net incomes of $65."}, {"knowledge": [{"content": "banking performance data. Browse our extensive research tools and reports. More FDIC Analysis Center for Financial Research Consumer Research FDIC National Survey of Unbanked and Underbanked Households Quarterly Banking Profile FDIC Academic Challenge FDIC Banking Issues in Focus Annual Risk Review", "wikipage": "AML Topic 91"}, {"content": "The FDIC publishes regular updates on news and activities. Keep up with FDIC announcements, read speeches and testimony on the latest banking issues, learn about policy changes for banks, and get the details on upcoming conferences and events.", "wikipage": "AML Topic 91"}, {"content": "EVENT / December 12, 2024 FDIC-Insured Institutions Reported Net Income of $65.4 Billion EVENT / September 05, 2024 FDIC-Insured Institutions Reported Net Income of $71.5 Billion", "wikipage": "AML Topic 91"}], "long_answer": "The FDIC provides various reports to analyze banking performance, including the Quarterly Banking Profile, Annual Risk Review, and other research tools and reports.\n\nThe FDIC publishes regular updates on news and activities, which include announcements, speeches, testimony on banking issues, policy changes, and details on upcoming conferences and events.\n\nIn 2024, FDIC-insured institutions reported net incomes of $65.4 billion in December and $71.5 billion in September."}], "sample_id": "aml-topic-91-3", "question": "What type of reports does the FDIC provide to analyze banking performance?", "docs": [{"id": "doc-aml-topic-91-3-1", "title": "AML Topic 91 Part 1", "text": "banking performance data. Browse our extensive research tools and reports.\nMore FDIC Analysis\nCenter for Financial Research\nConsumer Research\nFDIC National Survey of Unbanked and Underbanked Households\nQuarterly Banking Profile\nFDIC Academic Challenge\nFDIC Banking Issues in Focus\nAnnual Risk Review\nEVENT / February 25, 2025\nFDIC-Insured Institutions Reported Return on Assets of 1.11 Percent and Net Inc\u2026\nEVENT / December 12, 2024\nFDIC-Insured Institutions Reported Net Income of $65.4 Billion\nEVEN", "score": 0.9, "summary": "banking performance data. Browse our extensive research tools and reports. More FDIC Analysis Center for Financial Research Consumer Research FDIC Nat...", "extraction": "banking performance data. Browse our extensive research tools and reports. More FDIC Analysis Center for Financial Research Consumer Research FDIC National Survey of Unbanked and Underbanked Households Quarterly Banking Profile FDIC Academic Challenge FDIC Banking Issues in Focus Annual Risk Review"}], "answer": "The FDIC provides various reports to analyze banking performance, including the Quarterly Banking Profile, Annual Risk Review, and other research tools and reports. The FDIC publishes regular updates on news and activities, which include announcements, speeches, testimony on banking issues, policy changes, and details on upcoming conferences and events. In 2024, FDIC-insured institutions reported net incomes of $65.", "output": "The FDIC provides reports to analyze banking performance, such as the Quarterly Banking Profile and the FDIC National Survey of Unbanked and Underbanked Households [1].", "intermediate": ["[Retrieval]", "The FDIC provides reports to analyze banking performance, such as the Quarterly Banking Profile and the FDIC National Survey of Unbanked and Underbanked Households."]}, {"qa_pairs": [{"context": "No context provided", "question": "What is the significance of the Quarterly Banking Profile published by the FDIC?", "short_answers": ["Detailed insights into financial performance", "Overview of banking sector's health"], "wikipage": null}, {"context": "No context provided", "question": "How does the FDIC keep stakeholders informed about changes in banking policies?", "short_answers": ["Regular updates on policy changes", "Disseminated through announcements and speeches"], "wikipage": null}, {"context": "No context provided", "question": "What resources does the FDIC offer for understanding the performance of state banking?", "short_answers": ["State banking performance data", "Research tools and reports"], "wikipage": null}], "wikipages": [{"title": "AML Topic 94", "url": "https://www.fdic.gov/about/doing-business"}], "annotations": [{"knowledge": [], "long_answer": "The Quarterly Banking Profile provides detailed insights into the financial performance of FDIC-insured institutions. The FDIC regularly publishes updates on news and activities, including policy changes for banks. The FDIC provides state banking performance data along with extensive research tools and reports."}, {"knowledge": [{"content": "Quarterly Banking Profile for First Quarter 2024", "wikipage": "AML Topic 94"}, {"content": "The FDIC publishes regular updates on news and activities. Keep up with FDIC announcements, read speeches and testimony on the latest banking issues, learn about policy changes for banks, and get the details on upcoming conferences and events.", "wikipage": "AML Topic 94"}, {"content": "and state banking performance data. Browse our extensive research tools and reports.", "wikipage": "AML Topic 94"}], "long_answer": "The Quarterly Banking Profile provides detailed insights into the financial performance of FDIC-insured institutions. It covers metrics such as return on assets and net income, offering a comprehensive overview of the banking sector's health and trends.\n\nThe FDIC regularly publishes updates on news and activities, including policy changes for banks. This information is disseminated through announcements, speeches, testimony, and detailed policy fact sheets.\n\nThe FDIC provides state banking performance data along with extensive research tools and reports. These resources help stakeholders analyze and understand the performance metrics and trends within the state banking sector."}], "sample_id": "aml-topic-94-3", "question": "What is the significance of the Quarterly Banking Profile published by the FDIC?", "docs": [{"id": "doc-aml-topic-94-3-1", "title": "AML Topic 94 Part 1", "text": "and state banking performance data. Browse our extensive research tools and reports.\nMore FDIC Analysis\nCenter for Financial Research\nConsumer Research\nFDIC National Survey of Unbanked and Underbanked Households\nQuarterly Banking Profile\nFDIC Academic Challenge\nFDIC Banking Issues in Focus\nAnnual Risk Review\nEVENT / February 25, 2025\nFDIC-Insured Institutions Reported Return on Assets of 1.11 Percent and Net Inc\u2026\nEVENT / December 12, 2024\nFDIC-Insured Institutions Reported Net Income of $65.4 Bi", "score": 0.9, "summary": "and state banking performance data. Browse our extensive research tools and reports. More FDIC Analysis Center for Financial Research Consumer Researc...", "extraction": "Quarterly Banking Profile for First Quarter 2024"}], "answer": "The Quarterly Banking Profile provides detailed insights into the financial performance of FDIC-insured institutions. The FDIC regularly publishes updates on news and activities, including policy changes for banks. The FDIC provides state banking performance data along with extensive research tools and reports.", "output": "Answer: The Quarterly Banking Profile is a report that provides detailed financial data about FDIC-insured institutions [1].", "intermediate": ["[Retrieval]", "Answer: The Quarterly Banking Profile is a report that provides detailed financial data about FDIC-insured institutions."]}, {"qa_pairs": [{"context": "No context provided", "question": "What was the reported net income for FDIC-insured institutions in the third quarter of 2024?", "short_answers": ["$71.5 billion", "third quarter 2024"], "wikipage": null}, {"context": "No context provided", "question": "How did FDIC-insured institutions perform in terms of return on assets as of February 2025?", "short_answers": ["1.11 percent", "February 2025"], "wikipage": null}, {"context": "No context provided", "question": "What was the net income reported by FDIC-insured institutions in the fourth quarter of 2024?", "short_answers": ["$65.4 billion", "fourth quarter 2024"], "wikipage": null}], "wikipages": [{"title": "AML Topic 96", "url": "https://www.fdic.gov/resources/consumers"}], "annotations": [{"knowledge": [], "long_answer": "FDIC-insured institutions reported a net income of $71. As of February 2025, FDIC-insured institutions reported a return on assets of 1. In the fourth quarter of 2024, FDIC-insured institutions reported a net income of $65."}, {"knowledge": [{"content": "EVENT / September 05, 2024 FDIC-Insured Institutions Reported Net Income of $71.5 Billion", "wikipage": "AML Topic 96"}, {"content": "EVENT / February 25, 2025 FDIC-Insured Institutions Reported Return on Assets of 1.11 Percent", "wikipage": "AML Topic 96"}, {"content": "EVENT / December 12, 2024 FDIC-Insured Institutions Reported Net Income of $65.4 Billion", "wikipage": "AML Topic 96"}], "long_answer": "FDIC-insured institutions reported a net income of $71.5 billion in the third quarter of 2024.\n\nAs of February 2025, FDIC-insured institutions reported a return on assets of 1.11 percent.\n\nIn the fourth quarter of 2024, FDIC-insured institutions reported a net income of $65.4 billion."}], "sample_id": "aml-topic-96-3", "question": "What was the reported net income for FDIC-insured institutions in the third quarter of 2024?", "docs": [{"id": "doc-aml-topic-96-3-1", "title": "AML Topic 96 Part 1", "text": "state banking performance data. Browse our extensive research tools and reports.\nMore FDIC Analysis\nCenter for Financial Research\nConsumer Research\nFDIC National Survey of Unbanked and Underbanked Households\nQuarterly Banking Profile\nFDIC Academic Challenge\nFDIC Banking Issues in Focus\nAnnual Risk Review\nEVENT / February 25, 2025\nFDIC-Insured Institutions Reported Return on Assets of 1.11 Percent and Net Inc\u2026\nEVENT / December 12, 2024\nFDIC-Insured Institutions Reported Net Income of $65.4 Billio", "score": 0.9, "summary": "state banking performance data. Browse our extensive research tools and reports. More FDIC Analysis Center for Financial Research Consumer Research FD...", "extraction": "EVENT / September 05, 2024 FDIC-Insured Institutions Reported Net Income of $71.5 Billion"}], "answer": "FDIC-insured institutions reported a net income of $71. As of February 2025, FDIC-insured institutions reported a return on assets of 1. In the fourth quarter of 2024, FDIC-insured institutions reported a net income of $65.", "output": "Answer: FDIC-insured institutions reported net income of $65. 4 billion in the third quarter of 2024 [1].", "intermediate": ["[Retrieval]", "Answer: FDIC-insured institutions reported net income of $65.4 billion in the third quarter of 2024."]}, {"qa_pairs": [{"context": "No context provided", "question": "What resources does the FDIC provide for bankers to stay compliant with laws and regulations?", "short_answers": ["Banker Resource Center", "Documentation of laws and regulations"], "wikipage": null}, {"context": "No context provided", "question": "How can the FDIC's Community Banking Research Program assist small banks?", "short_answers": ["Community Banking Research Program", "Research on industry trends"], "wikipage": null}, {"context": "No context provided", "question": "What type of financial education materials does the FDIC offer to consumers?", "short_answers": ["Consumer Resource Center", "Financial education materials"], "wikipage": null}], "wikipages": [{"title": "AML Topic 98", "url": "https://www.fdic.gov/about/fdic-accessibility-statement"}], "annotations": [{"knowledge": [], "long_answer": "The FDIC offers a Banker Resource Center that includes documentation of laws and regulations, along with other financial education materials, data tools, and information on important initiatives. The FDIC's Community Banking Research Program provides resources and research that help small banks understand industry trends and challenges, enabling them to make informed decisions. The FDIC offers a range of financial education materials to consumers through its Consumer Resource Center, which includes information on deposit insurance, supervision, examinations, and more."}, {"knowledge": [{"content": "The FDIC provides a wealth of resources for consumers, bankers, analysts, and other stakeholders. Browse our collection of financial education materials, data tools, documentation of laws and regulations, information on important initiatives, and more.", "wikipage": "AML Topic 98"}, {"content": "Resources... Community Banking Research Program", "wikipage": "AML Topic 98"}, {"content": "Additional FDIC Resources Consumer Resource Center Deposit Insurance Supervision & Examinations", "wikipage": "AML Topic 98"}], "long_answer": "The FDIC offers a Banker Resource Center that includes documentation of laws and regulations, along with other financial education materials, data tools, and information on important initiatives.\n\nThe FDIC's Community Banking Research Program provides resources and research that help small banks understand industry trends and challenges, enabling them to make informed decisions.\n\nThe FDIC offers a range of financial education materials to consumers through its Consumer Resource Center, which includes information on deposit insurance, supervision, examinations, and more."}], "sample_id": "aml-topic-98-2", "question": "What resources does the FDIC provide for bankers to stay compliant with laws and regulations?", "docs": [{"id": "doc-aml-topic-98-2-1", "title": "AML Topic 98 Part 1", "text": "Bank, Des Plaines, Ill. Assumes All Deposits of Pulaski Savings\u2026\nPODCASTS / January 06, 2025\nSmall Business Lending\nResources\nToggle submenu\nResources\nThe FDIC provides a wealth of resources for consumers, bankers, analysts, and other stakeholders. Browse our collection of financial education materials, data tools, documentation of laws and regulations, information on important initiatives, and more.\nAdditional FDIC Resources\nConsumer Resource Center\nBanker Resource Center\nDeposit Insurance\nSupe", "score": 0.9, "summary": "Bank, Des Plaines, Ill. Assumes All Deposits of Pulaski Savings\u2026 PODCASTS / January 06, 2025 Small Business Lending Resources Toggle submenu Resources...", "extraction": "The FDIC provides a wealth of resources for consumers, bankers, analysts, and other stakeholders. Browse our collection of financial education materials, data tools, documentation of laws and regulations, information on important initiatives, and more."}], "answer": "The FDIC offers a Banker Resource Center that includes documentation of laws and regulations, along with other financial education materials, data tools, and information on important initiatives. The FDIC's Community Banking Research Program provides resources and research that help small banks understand industry trends and challenges, enabling them to make informed decisions. The FDIC offers a range of financial education materials to consumers through its Consumer Resource Center, which includes information on deposit insurance, supervision, examinations, and more.", "output": "The FDIC provides a wealth of resources for consumers, bankers, analysts, and other stakeholders [1].", "intermediate": ["[Retrieval]", "The FDIC provides a wealth of resources for consumers, bankers, analysts, and other stakeholders."]}, {"qa_pairs": [{"context": "No context provided", "question": "How does the FDIC provide updates on the latest banking issues and policy changes?", "short_answers": ["FDIC announcements", "Policy changes for banks"], "wikipage": null}, {"context": "No context provided", "question": "What kind of financial performance data does the FDIC report on?", "short_answers": ["Return on assets", "Net income reports"], "wikipage": null}, {"context": "No context provided", "question": "What resources does the FDIC provide for understanding banking performance and issues?", "short_answers": ["Quarterly Banking Profile", "Annual Risk Review"], "wikipage": null}], "wikipages": [{"title": "AML Topic 99", "url": "https://www.fdic.gov/about/open-government"}], "annotations": [{"knowledge": [], "long_answer": "The FDIC publishes regular updates on news and activities, including announcements, speeches, and testimonies on the latest banking issues. The FDIC reports on various financial performance data, including return on assets and net income of FDIC-insured institutions. The FDIC provides a variety of resources for understanding banking performance and issues, including the Quarterly Banking Profile, Annual Risk Review, and reports from the Center for Financial Research."}, {"knowledge": [{"content": "The FDIC publishes regular updates on news and activities. Keep up with FDIC announcements, read speeches and testimony on the latest banking issues, learn about policy changes for banks, and get the details on upcoming conferences and events.", "wikipage": "AML Topic 99"}, {"content": "FDIC-Insured Institutions Reported Return on Assets of 1.11 Percent and Net Inc\u2026 EVENT / December 12, 2024 FDIC-Insured Institutions Reported Net Income of $65.4 Billion EVENT / September 05, 2024 FDIC-Insured Institutions Reported Net Income of $71.5 Billion", "wikipage": "AML Topic 99"}, {"content": "Quarterly Banking Profile FDIC Academic Challenge FDIC Banking Issues in Focus Annual Risk Review", "wikipage": "AML Topic 99"}], "long_answer": "The FDIC publishes regular updates on news and activities, including announcements, speeches, and testimonies on the latest banking issues. They also provide details on policy changes for banks and information about upcoming conferences and events.\n\nThe FDIC reports on various financial performance data, including return on assets and net income of FDIC-insured institutions. For example, they reported a return on assets of 1.11 percent and net incomes of $65.4 billion and $71.5 billion in different periods.\n\nThe FDIC provides a variety of resources for understanding banking performance and issues, including the Quarterly Banking Profile, Annual Risk Review, and reports from the Center for Financial Research. They also conduct the FDIC Academic Challenge and publish the FDIC Banking Issues in Focus."}], "sample_id": "aml-topic-99-3", "question": "How does the FDIC provide updates on the latest banking issues and policy changes?", "docs": [{"id": "doc-aml-topic-99-3-2", "title": "AML Topic 99 Part 2", "text": "/ September 05, 2024\nFDIC-Insured Institutions Reported Net Income of $71.5 Billion\nEVENT / May 29, 2024\nQuarterly Banking Profile for First Quarter 2024\nNews\nToggle submenu\nNews\nThe FDIC publishes regular updates on news and activities. Keep up with FDIC announcements, read speeches and testimony on the latest banking issues, learn about policy changes for banks, and get the details on upcoming conferences and events.\nFind More FDIC News\nPress Releases\nFinancial Institution Letters\nConferences", "score": 0.85, "summary": "/ September 05, 2024 FDIC-Insured Institutions Reported Net Income of $71.5 Billion EVENT / May 29, 2024 Quarterly Banking Profile for First Quarter 2...", "extraction": "/ September 05, 2024\nFDIC-Insured Institutions Reported Net Income of $71.5 Billion\nEVENT / May 29, 2024\nQuarterly Banking Profile for First Quarter 2024\nNews\nToggle submenu\nNews\nThe FDIC publishes re"}], "answer": "The FDIC publishes regular updates on news and activities, including announcements, speeches, and testimonies on the latest banking issues. The FDIC reports on various financial performance data, including return on assets and net income of FDIC-insured institutions. The FDIC provides a variety of resources for understanding banking performance and issues, including the Quarterly Banking Profile, Annual Risk Review, and reports from the Center for Financial Research.", "output": "Answer: The FDIC publishes regular updates on news and activities [1].", "intermediate": ["[Retrieval]", "Answer: The FDIC publishes regular updates on news and activities."]}, {"qa_pairs": [{"context": "No context provided", "question": "What resources does the FDIC provide for bankers to enhance their compliance with laws and regulations?", "short_answers": ["Banker Resource Center", "Documentation of laws and regulations"], "wikipage": null}, {"context": "No context provided", "question": "How can stakeholders access information on FDIC's community banking research?", "short_answers": ["Community Banking Research Program", "FDIC resources"], "wikipage": null}, {"context": "No context provided", "question": "What kind of training opportunities does the FDIC offer internationally?", "short_answers": ["International seminars", "Training opportunities"], "wikipage": null}], "wikipages": [{"title": "AML Topic 104", "url": "https://www.fdic.gov/banker-resource-center/cra-regional-contacts-list"}], "annotations": [{"knowledge": [], "long_answer": "The FDIC offers a Banker Resource Center that includes documentation of laws and regulations, financial education materials, and other resources to help bankers comply with regulatory requirements. Stakeholders can access information on community banking research through the FDIC's Community Banking Research Program, which is part of the resources they provide. The FDIC offers international seminars and training as part of its resources for stakeholders."}, {"knowledge": [{"content": "The FDIC provides a wealth of resources for consumers, bankers, analysts, and other stakeholders. Browse our collection of financial education materials, data tools, documentation of laws and regulations, information on important initiatives, and more. Additional FDIC Resources: Consumer Resource Center, Banker Resource Center, Deposit Insurance, Supervision & Examinations, Laws & Regulations, Resolutions, Publications, Forms, Data Tools, Community Banking Research Program, International Seminars and Training.", "wikipage": "AML Topic 104"}, {"content": "The FDIC provides a wealth of resources for consumers, bankers, analysts, and other stakeholders. Browse our collection of financial education materials, data tools, documentation of laws and regulations, information on important initiatives, and more. Additional FDIC Resources: Consumer Resource Center, Banker Resource Center, Deposit Insurance, Supervision & Examinations, Laws & Regulations, Resolutions, Publications, Forms, Data Tools, Community Banking Research Program, International Seminars and Training.", "wikipage": "AML Topic 104"}, {"content": "The FDIC provides a wealth of resources for consumers, bankers, analysts, and other stakeholders. Browse our collection of financial education materials, data tools, documentation of laws and regulations, information on important initiatives, and more. Additional FDIC Resources: Consumer Resource Center, Banker Resource Center, Deposit Insurance, Supervision & Examinations, Laws & Regulations, Resolutions, Publications, Forms, Data Tools, Community Banking Research Program, International Seminars and Training.", "wikipage": "AML Topic 104"}], "long_answer": "The FDIC offers a Banker Resource Center that includes documentation of laws and regulations, financial education materials, and other resources to help bankers comply with regulatory requirements.\n\nStakeholders can access information on community banking research through the FDIC's Community Banking Research Program, which is part of the resources they provide.\n\nThe FDIC offers international seminars and training as part of its resources for stakeholders."}], "sample_id": "aml-topic-104-2", "question": "What resources does the FDIC provide for bankers to enhance their comp