ssion, leadership, history, career opportunities, and more.", "wikipage": "AML Topic 106"}], "long_answer": "The Federal Deposit Insurance Corporation (FDIC) is an independent agency created by Congress to maintain stability and public confidence in the nation\u2019s financial system.\n\nTo ensure you are accessing the official FDIC website securely, look for the 'https://' in the URL, which indicates that you are connecting to the official website and that any information you provide is encrypted and transmitted securely.\n\nUnder the 'About' section of the FDIC website, one can learn about the FDIC\u2019s mission, leadership, history, career opportunities, and more."}], "sample_id": "aml-topic-106-1", "question": "What is the purpose of the Federal Deposit Insurance Corporation (FDIC)?", "docs": [{"id": "doc-aml-topic-106-1-2", "title": "AML Topic 106 Part 2", "text": "ov\nSearch\nAbout\nToggle submenu\nAbout\nThe Federal Deposit Insurance Corporation (FDIC) is an independent agency created by the Congress to maintain stability and public confidence in the nation\u2019s financial system. Learn about the FDIC\u2019s mission, leadership, history, career opportunities, and more.\nLearn More About the FDIC\nWhat We Do\nLeadership\nCareers\nInitiatives\nStrategic Plans\nFinancial Reports\nHistory\nGovernance\nOmbudsman\nDoing Business with the FDIC\nPRESS RELEASE / February 25, 2025\nFDIC-Ins", "score": 0.85, "summary": "ov Search About Toggle submenu About The Federal Deposit Insurance Corporation (FDIC) is an independent agency created by the Congress to maintain sta...", "extraction": "ov\nSearch\nAbout\nToggle submenu\nAbout\nThe Federal Deposit Insurance Corporation (FDIC) is an independent agency created by the Congress to maintain stability and public confidence in the nation\u2019s finan"}], "answer": "The Federal Deposit Insurance Corporation (FDIC) is an independent agency created by Congress to maintain stability and public confidence in the nation\u2019s fi