_answers": ["Press releases", "Financial institution letters"], "wikipage": null}], "wikipages": [{"title": "AML Topic 116", "url": "https://www.fdic.gov/banker-resource-center/transaction-account-guarantee-program"}], "annotations": [{"knowledge": [], "long_answer": "Enterprises can access state banking performance data, FDIC National Survey of Unbanked and Underbanked Households, Quarterly Banking Profile, and Annual Risk Review among other resources. The FDIC provides updates on banking performance quarterly, as evidenced by the Quarterly Banking Profile releases. The FDIC communicates policy changes and other important information through press releases, financial institution letters, conferences and events, speeches, statements, testimonies, and policy fact sheets."}, {"knowledge": [{"content": "g papers, and state banking performance data. Browse our extensive research tools and reports. More FDIC Analysis Center for Financial Research Consumer Research FDIC National Survey of Unbanked and Underbanked Households Quarterly Banking Profile FDIC Academic Challenge FDIC Banking Issues in Focus Annual Risk Review", "wikipage": "AML Topic 116"}, {"content": "EVENT / May 29, 2024 Quarterly Banking Profile for First Quarter 2024", "wikipage": "AML Topic 116"}, {"content": "News The FDIC publishes regular updates on news and activities. Keep up with FDIC announcements, read speeches and testimony on the latest banking issues, learn about policy changes for banks, and get the details on upcoming conferences and events. Find More FDIC News Press Releases Financial Institution Letters Conferences & Events Speeches, Statements & Testimonies Policy Fact Sheets", "wikipage": "AML Topic 116"}], "long_answer": "Enterprises can access state banking performance data, FDIC National Survey of Unbanked and Underbanked Households, Quarterly Banking Profile, and Annual Risk Review among other resources.\n\nThe FDIC provides updates on banking performance quarterly, as evidenced by the Quarterly Banking Profile releases.\n\nThe FDIC communicates policy changes and other important information through press releases, financial institution letters, conferences and events, speeches, statements, testimonies, and policy fact sheets."}], "sample_id": "aml-topic-116-3", "question": "What kind of reports and data can enterprises access through the FDIC's research tools?", "docs": [{"id": "doc-aml-topic-116-3-1", "title": "AML Topic 116 Part 1", "text": "g papers, and state banking performance data. Browse our extensive research tools and reports.\nMore FDIC Analysis\nCenter for Financial Research\nConsumer Research\nFDIC National Survey of Unbanked and Underbanked Households\nQuarterly Banking Profile\nFDIC Academic Challenge\nFDIC Banking Issues in Focus\nAnnual Risk Review\nEVENT / February 25, 2025\nFDIC-Insured Institutions Reported Return on Assets of 1.11 Percent and Net Inc\u2026\nEVENT / December 12, 2024\nFDIC-Insured Institutions Reported Net Income o", "score": 0.9, "summary": "g papers, and state banking performance data. Browse our extensive research tools and reports. More FDIC Analysis Center for Financial Research Consum...", "extraction": "g papers, and state banking performance data. Browse our extensive research tools and reports. More FDIC Analysis Center for Financial Research Consumer Research FDIC National Survey of Unbanked and Underbanked Households Quarterly Banking Profile FDIC Academic Challenge FDIC Banking Issues in Focus Annual Risk Review"}], "answer": "Enterprises can access state banking performance data, FDIC National Survey of Unbanked and Underbanked Households, Quarterly Banking Profile, and Annual Risk Review among other resources. The FDIC provides updates on banking performance quarterly, as evidenced by the Quarterly Banking Profile releases. The FDIC communicates policy changes and other important information through press releases, financial institution letters, conferences and events, speeches, statements, testimonies, and policy fact sheets.", "output": "Answer: Enterprises can access reports and data on banking performance, consumer behavior, and economic trends through the FDIC's research tools [1].", "intermediate": ["[Retrieval]", "Answer: Enterprises can access reports and data on banking performance, consumer behavior, and economic trends through the FDIC's research tools."]}, {"qa_pairs": [{"context": "No context provided", "question": "What type of data does the FDIC's Quarterly Banking Profile provide?", "short_answers": ["State banking performance data", "Financial health metrics"], "wikipage": null}, {"context": "No context provided", "question": "How can I stay updated on the latest FDIC policy changes for banks?", "short_answers": ["FDIC news updates", "Speeches and testimony"], "wikipage": null}, {"context": "No context provided", "question": "What are some events where FDIC-insured institutions' financial performance is reported?", "short_answers": ["Quarterly Banking Profile", "Net income announcements"], "wikipage": null}], "wikipages": [{"title": "AML Topic 117", "url": "https://www.fdic.gov/banker-resource-center/chairmans-statement-temporary-liquidity-guarantee-program"}], "annotations": [{"knowledge": [], "long_answer": "The FDIC's Quarterly Banking Profile provides data on the performance of state banking institutions, including their financial health and other relevant metrics. You can stay updated on the latest FDIC policy changes for banks by following their regular news updates, which include announcements, speeches, testimony, and policy changes. FDIC-insured institutions' financial performance is reported during events such as the Quarterly Banking Profile releases and other specific announcements like the ones on December 12, 2024, and September 05, 2024, where net income figures were shared."}, {"knowledge": [{"content": "Quarterly Banking Profile for First Quarter 2024", "wikipage": "AML Topic 117"}, {"content": "The FDIC publishes regular updates on news and activities. Keep up with FDIC announcements, read speeches and testimony on the latest banking issues, learn about policy changes for banks...", "wikipage": "AML Topic 117"}, {"content": "EVENT / December 12, 2024 FDIC-Insured Institutions Reported Net Income of $65.4 Billion EVENT / September 05, 2024 FDIC-Insured Institutions Reported Net Income of $71.5 Billion", "wikipage": "AML Topic 117"}], "long_answer": "The FDIC's Quarterly Banking Profile provides data on the performance of state banking institutions, including their financial health and other relevant metrics.\n\nYou can stay updated on the latest FDIC policy changes for banks by following their regular news updates, which include announcements, speeches, testimony, and policy changes.\n\nFDIC-insured institutions' financial performance is reported during events such as the Quarterly Banking Profile releases and other specific announcements like the ones on December 12, 2024, and September 05, 2024, where net income figures were shared."}], "sample_id": "aml-topic-117-3", "question": "What type of data does the FDIC's Quarterly Banking Profile provide?", "docs": [{"id": "doc-aml-topic-117-3-1", "title": "AML Topic 117 Part 1", "text": "rly banking profiles, working papers, and state banking performance data. Browse our extensive research tools and reports.\nMore FDIC Analysis\nCenter for Financial Research\nConsumer Research\nFDIC National Survey of Unbanked and Underbanked Households\nQuarterly Banking Profile\nFDIC Academic Challenge\nFDIC Banking Issues in Focus\nAnnual Risk Review\nEVENT / February 25, 2025\nFDIC-Insured Institutions Reported Return on Assets of 1.11 Percent and Net Inc\u2026\nEVENT / December 12, 2024\nFDIC-Insured Instit", "score": 0.9, "summary": "rly banking profiles, working papers, and state banking performance data. Browse our extensive research tools and reports. More FDIC Analysis Center f...", "extraction": "Quarterly Banking Profile for First Quarter 2024"}], "answer": "The FDIC's Quarterly Banking Profile provides data on the performance of state banking institutions, including their financial health and other relevant metrics. You can stay updated on the latest FDIC policy changes for banks by following their regular news updates, which include announcements, speeches, testimony, and policy changes. FDIC-insured institutions' financial performance is reported during events such as the Quarterly Banking Profile releases and other specific announcements like the ones on December 12, 2024, and September 05, 2024, where net income figures were shared.", "output": "Answer: The FDIC's Quarterly Banking Profile provides data on the condition, performance, and profitability of insured U. S. commercial banks and thrift institutions [1].", "intermediate": ["[Retrieval]", "Answer: The FDIC's Quarterly Banking Profile provides data on the condition, performance, and profitability of insured U.S. commercial banks and thrift institutions."]}, {"qa_pairs": [{"context": "No context provided", "question": "What types of resources does the FDIC provide for financial education and support?", "short_answers": ["Financial education materials", "Data tools", "Laws and regulations documentation"], "wikipage": null}, {"context": "No context provided", "question": "Where can bankers find specific resources tailored to their needs provided by the FDIC?", "short_answers": ["Banker Resource Center"], "wikipage": null}, {"context": "No context provided", "question": "What is the FDIC's role in the realm of banking industry research?", "short_answers": ["Pre-eminent source of banking research", "Quarterly bank reports"], "wikipage": null}], "wikipages": [{"title": "AML Topic 119", "url": "https://www.fdic.gov/banker-resource-center/tlgp-debt-guarantee-program-issuer-reported-debt-details"}], "annotations": [{"knowledge": [], "long_answer": "The FDIC offers a range of resources including financial education materials, data tools, documentation of laws and regulations, and information on important initiatives. Bankers can find specific resources tailored to their needs in the Banker Resource Center provided by the FDIC. The FDIC is a pre-eminent source of U."}, {"knowledge": [{"content": "The FDIC provides a wealth of resources for consumers, bankers, analysts, and other stakeholders. Browse our collection of financial education materials, data tools, documentation of laws and regulations, information on important initiatives, and more.", "wikipage": "AML Topic 119"}, {"content": "Additional FDIC Resources\nConsumer Resource Center\nBanker Resource Center\nDeposit Insurance\nSupervision & Examinations\nLaws & Regulations\nResolutions\nPublications\nForms\nData Tools", "wikipage": "AML Topic 119"}, {"content": "The FDIC is proud to be a pre-eminent source of U.S. banking industry research, including quarterly bank", "wikipage": "AML Topic 119"}], "long_answer": "The FDIC offers a range of resources including financial education materials, data tools, documentation of laws and regulations, and information on important initiatives. These resources are available for consumers, bankers, analysts, and other stakeholders.\n\nBankers can find specific resources tailored to their needs in the Banker Resource Center provided by the FDIC.\n\nThe FDIC is a pre-eminent source of U.S. banking industry research, providing analysis including quarterly bank reports."}], "sample_id": "aml-topic-119-2", "question": "What types of resources does the FDIC provide for financial education and support?", "docs": [{"id": "doc-aml-topic-119-2-1", "title": "AML Topic 119 Part 1", "text": "January 17, 2025\nMillennium Bank, Des Plaines, Ill. Assumes All Deposits of Pulaski Savings\u2026\nPODCASTS / January 06, 2025\nSmall Business Lending\nResources\nToggle submenu\nResources\nThe FDIC provides a wealth of resources for consumers, bankers, analysts, and other stakeholders. Browse our collection of financial education materials, data tools, documentation of laws and regulations, information on important initiatives, and more.\nAdditional FDIC Resources\nConsumer Resource Center\nBanker Resource C", "score": 0.9, "summary": "January 17, 2025 Millennium Bank, Des Plaines, Ill. Assumes All Deposits of Pulaski Savings\u2026 PODCASTS / January 06, 2025 Small Business Lending Resour...", "extraction": "The FDIC provides a wealth of resources for consumers, bankers, analysts, and other stakeholders. Browse our collection of financial education materials, data tools, documentation of laws and regulations, information on important initiatives, and more."}], "answer": "The FDIC offers a range of resources including financial education materials, data tools, documentation of laws and regulations, and information on important initiatives. Bankers can find specific resources tailored to their needs in the Banker Resource Center provided by the FDIC. The FDIC is a pre-eminent source of U.", "output": "Answer: The FDIC provides a wealth of resources for consumers, bankers, analysts, and other stakeholders [1].", "intermediate": ["[Retrieval]", "Answer: The FDIC provides a wealth of resources for consumers, bankers, analysts, and other stakeholders."]}, {"qa_pairs": [{"context": "No context provided", "question": "What resources does the FDIC offer for understanding banking performance data?", "short_answers": ["banking profiles", "working papers", "state banking performance data"], "wikipage": null}, {"context": "No context provided", "question": "Where can one find information about the FDIC's recent financial performance reports?", "short_answers": ["Quarterly Banking Profile", "FDIC-insured institutions' net income reports"], "wikipage": null}, {"context": "No context provided", "question": "How does the FDIC communicate updates and policy changes to the public?", "short_answers": ["news updates", "press releases", "speeches and testimonies"], "wikipage": null}], "wikipages": [{"title": "AML Topic 119", "url": "https://www.fdic.gov/banker-resource-center/tlgp-debt-guarantee-program-issuer-reported-debt-details"}], "annotations": [{"knowledge": [], "long_answer": "The FDIC provides various resources such as banking profiles, working papers, and state banking performance data. Information about the FDIC's recent financial performance reports can be found in their announcements of quarterly and annual results, such as the Quarterly Banking Profile and reports on the return on assets and net income of FDIC-insured institutions. The FDIC communicates updates and policy changes through regular news updates, press releases, speeches, testimonies, and policy fact sheets."}, {"knowledge": [{"content": "ing profiles, working papers, and state banking performance data. Browse our extensive research tools and reports. More FDIC Analysis Center for Financial Research Quarterly Banking Profile", "wikipage": "AML Topic 119"}, {"content": "Quarterly Banking Profile FDIC-Insured Institutions Reported Return on Assets of 1.11 Percent and Net Inc\u2026 FDIC-Insured Institutions Reported Net Income of $65.4 Billion FDIC-Insured Institutions Reported Net Income of $71.5 Billion", "wikipage": "AML Topic 119"}, {"content": "The FDIC publishes regular updates on news and activities. Keep up with FDIC announcements, read speeches and testimony on the latest banking issues, learn about policy changes for banks, and get the details on upcoming conferences and events.", "wikipage": "AML Topic 119"}], "long_answer": "The FDIC provides various resources such as banking profiles, working papers, and state banking performance data. Additionally, they offer tools and reports through their Center for Financial Research and the Quarterly Banking Profile.\n\nInformation about the FDIC's recent financial performance reports can be found in their announcements of quarterly and annual results, such as the Quarterly Banking Profile and reports on the return on assets and net income of FDIC-insured institutions.\n\nThe FDIC communicates updates and policy changes through regular news updates, press releases, speeches, testimonies, and policy fact sheets. They also provide information through conferences, events, and various media campaigns."}], "sample_id": "aml-topic-119-3", "question": "What resources does the FDIC offer for understanding banking performance data?", "docs": [{"id": "doc-aml-topic-119-3-1", "title": "AML Topic 119 Part 1", "text": "ing profiles, working papers, and state banking performance data. Browse our extensive research tools and reports.\nMore FDIC Analysis\nCenter for Financial Research\nConsumer Research\nFDIC National Survey of Unbanked and Underbanked Households\nQuarterly Banking Profile\nFDIC Academic Challenge\nFDIC Banking Issues in Focus\nAnnual Risk Review\nEVENT / February 25, 2025\nFDIC-Insured Institutions Reported Return on Assets of 1.11 Percent and Net Inc\u2026\nEVENT / December 12, 2024\nFDIC-Insured Institutions R", "score": 0.9, "summary": "ing profiles, working papers, and state banking performance data. Browse our extensive research tools and reports. More FDIC Analysis Center for Finan...", "extraction": "ing profiles, working papers, and state banking performance data. Browse our extensive research tools and reports. More FDIC Analysis Center for Financial Research Quarterly Banking Profile"}], "answer": "The FDIC provides various resources such as banking profiles, working papers, and state banking performance data. Information about the FDIC's recent financial performance reports can be found in their announcements of quarterly and annual results, such as the Quarterly Banking Profile and reports on the return on assets and net income of FDIC-insured institutions. The FDIC communicates updates and policy changes through regular news updates, press releases, speeches, testimonies, and policy fact sheets.", "output": "Answer: The FDIC offers resources for understanding banking performance data, such as the FDIC's Quarterly Banking Profile, which provides key financial data for FDIC-insured institutions, and the FDIC's Banking Trends and Statistics, which provides historical data on banking performance and structure [1].", "intermediate": ["[Retrieval]", "Answer: The FDIC offers resources for understanding banking performance data, such as the FDIC's Quarterly Banking Profile, which provides key financial data for FDIC-insured institutions, and the FDIC's Banking Trends and Statistics, which provides historical data on banking performance and structure."]}, {"qa_pairs": [{"context": "No context provided", "question": "What is the main purpose of the Federal Deposit Insurance Corporation (FDIC)?", "short_answers": ["Maintain financial stability", "Public confidence"], "wikipage": null}, {"context": "No context provided", "question": "What should you ensure before sharing sensitive information on a federal government website?", "short_answers": [".gov or .mil domain", "HTTPS encryption"], "wikipage": null}, {"context": "No context provided", "question": "What recent press release topics has the FDIC covered in 2025?", "short_answers": ["Return on assets", "Withdrawal from network"], "wikipage": null}], "wikipages": [{"title": "AML Topic 120", "url": "https://www.fdic.gov/banker-resource-center/tlgp-debt-guarantee-program-disclaimer"}], "annotations": [{"knowledge": [], "long_answer": "The main purpose of the Federal Deposit Insurance Corporation (FDIC) is to maintain stability and public confidence in the nation\u2019s financial system. Before sharing sensitive information on a federal government website, you should ensure that you are on an official government site, which is indicated by a . In 2025, the FDIC has covered topics such as the return on assets reported by FDIC-insured institutions and its withdrawal from the Network of Central Banks and Supervisors for Greening the Financial System."}, {"knowledge": [{"content": "The Federal Deposit Insurance Corporation (FDIC) is an independent agency created by the Congress to maintain stability and public confidence in the nation\u2019s financial system.", "wikipage": "AML Topic 120"}, {"content": "Federal government websites often end in .gov or .mil. Before sharing sensitive information, make sure you\u2019re on a federal government site. The site is secure. The https:// ensures that you are connecting to the official website and that any information you provide is encrypted and transmitted securely.", "wikipage": "AML Topic 120"}, {"content": "PRESS RELEASE / February 25, 2025 FDIC-Insured Institutions Reported Return on Assets of 1.11 Percent and Ne\u2026 PRESS RELEASE / January 21, 2025 FDIC Withdraws from the Network of Central Banks and Supervisors for Green\u2026", "wikipage": "AML Topic 120"}], "long_answer": "The main purpose of the Federal Deposit Insurance Corporation (FDIC) is to maintain stability and public confidence in the nation\u2019s financial system.\n\nBefore sharing sensitive information on a federal government website, you should ensure that you are on an official government site, which is indicated by a .gov or .mil domain, and that the site uses HTTPS to encrypt and securely transmit information.\n\nIn 2025, the FDIC has covered topics such as the return on assets reported by FDIC-insured institutions and its withdrawal from the Network of Central Banks and Supervisors for Greening the Financial System."}], "sample_id": "aml-topic-120-1", "question": "What is the main purpose of the Federal Deposit Insurance Corporation (FDIC)?", "docs": [{"id": "doc-aml-topic-120-1-2", "title": "AML Topic 120 Part 2", "text": "About\nToggle submenu\nAbout\nThe Federal Deposit Insurance Corporation (FDIC) is an independent agency created by the Congress to maintain stability and public confidence in the nation\u2019s financial system. Learn about the FDIC\u2019s mission, leadership, history, career opportunities, and more.\nLearn More About the FDIC\nWhat We Do\nLeadership\nCareers\nInitiatives\nStrategic Plans\nFinancial Reports\nHistory\nGovernance\nOmbudsman\nDoing Business with the FDIC\nPRESS RELEASE / February 25, 2025\nFDIC-Insured Insti", "score": 0.85, "summary": "About Toggle submenu About The Federal Deposit Insurance Corporation (FDIC) is an independent agency created by the Congress to maintain stability and...", "extraction": "About\nToggle submenu\nAbout\nThe Federal Deposit Insurance Corporation (FDIC) is an independent agency created by the Congress to maintain stability and public confidence in the nation\u2019s financial syste"}], "answer": "The main purpose of the Federal Deposit Insurance Corporation (FDIC) is to maintain stability and public confidence in the nation\u2019s financial system. Before sharing sensitive information on a federal government website, you should ensure that you are on an official government site, which is indicated by a . In 2025, the FDIC has covered topics such as the return on assets reported by FDIC-insured institutions and its withdrawal from the Network of Central Banks and Supervisors for Greening the Financial System.", "output": "The main purpose of the Federal Deposit Insurance Corporation (FDIC) is to maintain stability and public confidence in the U. S. financial system [1].", "intermediate": ["[Retrieval]", "The main purpose of the Federal Deposit Insurance Corporation (FDIC) is to maintain stability and public confidence in the U.S. financial system."]}, {"qa_pairs": [{"context": "No context provided", "question": "What resources does the FDIC provide for compliance officers to stay informed about laws and regulations?", "short_answers": ["Documentation of laws and regulations", "Banker Resource Center"], "wikipage": null}, {"context": "No context provided", "question": "How can bankers access FDIC resources for better understanding deposit insurance?", "short_answers": ["Banker Resource Center", "Deposit Insurance"], "wikipage": null}, {"context": "No context provided", "question": "What type of educational materials does the FDIC offer to stakeholders?", "short_answers": ["Financial education materials", "Data tools"], "wikipage": null}], "wikipages": [{"title": "AML Topic 121", "url": "https://www.fdic.gov/banker-resource-center/temporary-liquidity-guarantee-program-archive"}], "annotations": [{"knowledge": [], "long_answer": "The FDIC provides a variety of resources including documentation of laws and regulations, a Consumer Resource Center, a Banker Resource Center, and more to help compliance officers stay informed. Bankers can access FDIC resources such as the Banker Resource Center and specific sections on Deposit Insurance to better understand the topic. The FDIC offers financial education materials, data tools, and information on important initiatives among other resources to stakeholders."}, {"knowledge": [{"content": "The FDIC provides a wealth of resources for consumers, bankers, analysts, and other stakeholders. Browse our collection of financial education materials, data tools, documentation of laws and regulations, information on important initiatives, and more.", "wikipage": "AML Topic 121"}, {"content": "Additional FDIC Resources Consumer Resource Center Banker Resource Center Deposit Insurance Supervision & Examinations Laws & Regulations Resolutions Publications Forms Data Tools", "wikipage": "AML Topic 121"}, {"content": "The FDIC provides a wealth of resources for consumers, bankers, analysts, and other stakeholders. Browse our collection of financial education materials, data tools, documentation of laws and regulations, information on important initiatives, and more.", "wikipage": "AML Topic 121"}], "long_answer": "The FDIC provides a variety of resources including documentation of laws and regulations, a Consumer Resource Center, a Banker Resource Center, and more to help compliance officers stay informed.\n\nBankers can access FDIC resources such as the Banker Resource Center and specific sections on Deposit Insurance to better understand the topic.\n\nThe FDIC offers financial education materials, data tools, and information on important initiatives among other resources to stakeholders."}], "sample_id": "aml-topic-121-2", "question": "What resources does the FDIC provide for compliance officers to stay informed about laws and regulations?", "docs": [{"id": "doc-aml-topic-121-2-1", "title": "AML Topic 121 Part 1", "text": "7, 2025\nMillennium Bank, Des Plaines, Ill. Assumes All Deposits of Pulaski Savings\u2026\nPODCASTS / January 06, 2025\nSmall Business Lending\nResources\nToggle submenu\nResources\nThe FDIC provides a wealth of resources for consumers, bankers, analysts, and other stakeholders. Browse our collection of financial education materials, data tools, documentation of laws and regulations, information on important initiatives, and more.\nAdditional FDIC Resources\nConsumer Resource Center\nBanker Resource Center\nDep", "score": 0.9, "summary": "7, 2025 Millennium Bank, Des Plaines, Ill. Assumes All Deposits of Pulaski Savings\u2026 PODCASTS / January 06, 2025 Small Business Lending Resources Toggl...", "extraction": "The FDIC provides a wealth of resources for consumers, bankers, analysts, and other stakeholders. Browse our collection of financial education materials, data tools, documentation of laws and regulations, information on important initiatives, and more."}], "answer": "The FDIC provides a variety of resources including documentation of laws and regulations, a Consumer Resource Center, a Banker Resource Center, and more to help compliance officers stay informed. Bankers can access FDIC resources such as the Banker Resource Center and specific sections on Deposit Insurance to better understand the topic. The FDIC offers financial education materials, data tools, and information on important initiatives among other resources to stakeholders.", "output": "The FDIC provides a wealth of resources for consumers, bankers, analysts, and other stakeholders [1].", "in