"}, {"content": "Additional FDIC Resources Consumer Resource Center Banker Resource Center Deposit Insurance Supervision & Examinations Laws & Regulations Resolutions Publications Forms Data Tools Community Banking Research Program International Seminars and Training", "wikipage": "AML Topic 126"}, {"content": "Additional FDIC Resources Consumer Resource Center Banker Resource Center Deposit Insurance Supervision & Examinations Laws & Regulations Resolutions Publications Forms Data Tools Community Banking Research Program International Seminars and Training", "wikipage": "AML Topic 126"}], "long_answer": "The FDIC provides a collection of financial education materials, data tools, documentation of laws and regulations, information on important initiatives, and more.\n\nBankers can find resources specific to their needs in the Banker Resource Center provided by the FDIC.\n\nThe FDIC offers International Seminars and Training as part of its resources."}], "sample_id": "aml-topic-126-2", "question": "What type of resources does the FDIC offer for financial education?", "docs": [{"id": "doc-aml-topic-126-2-1", "title": "AML Topic 126 Part 1", "text": "lennium Bank, Des Plaines, Ill. Assumes All Deposits of Pulaski Savings\u2026\nPODCASTS / January 06, 2025\nSmall Business Lending\nResources\nToggle submenu\nResources\nThe FDIC provides a wealth of resources for consumers, bankers, analysts, and other stakeholders. Browse our collection of financial education materials, data tools, documentation of laws and regulations, information on important initiatives, and more.\nAdditional FDIC Resources\nConsumer Resource Center\nBanker Resource Center\nDeposit Insura", "score": 0.9, "summary": "lennium Bank, Des Plaines, Ill. Assumes All Deposits of Pulaski Savings\u2026 PODCASTS / January 06, 2025 Small Business Lending Resources Toggle submenu R...", "extraction": "The FDIC provides a wealth of resources for consumers, bankers, analysts, and other stakeholders. Browse our collection of financial education materials, data tools, documentation of laws and regulations, information on important initiatives, and more."}], "answer": "The FDIC provides a collection of financial education materials, data tools, documentation of laws and regulations, information on important initiatives, and more. Bankers can find resources specific to their needs in the Banker Resource Center provided by the FDIC. The FDIC offers International Seminars and Training as part of its resources.", "output": "Answer: The FDIC provides a wealth of resources for consumers, bankers, analysts, and other stakeholders [1].", "intermediate": ["[Retrieval]", "Answer: The FDIC provides a wealth of resources for consumers, bankers, analysts, and other stakeholders."]}, {"qa_pairs": [{"context": "No context provided", "question": "What types of resources does the FDIC provide for stakeholders such as consumers and bankers?", "short_answers": ["Financial education materials", "Data tools", "Documentation of laws and regulations"], "wikipage": null}, {"context": "No context provided", "question": "Where can bankers find specific resources related to deposit insurance and supervision?", "short_answers": ["Banker Resource Center", "Deposit Insurance", "Supervision & Examinations"], "wikipage": null}, {"context": "No context provided", "question": "What programs does the FDIC offer to support community banking research?", "short_answers": ["Community Banking Research Program"], "wikipage": null}], "wikipages": [{"title": "AML Topic 128", "url": "https://www.fdic.gov/banker-resource-center/information-technology-it-and-cybersecurity"}], "annotations": [{"knowledge": [], "long_answer": "The FDIC provides a variety of resources for stakeholders including financial education materials, data tools, documentation of laws and regulations, and information on important initiatives. Bankers can find specific resources related to deposit insurance and supervision in the Banker Resource Center provided by the FDIC. The FDIC offers the Community Banking Research Program as part of its resources to support community banking research."}, {"knowledge": [{"content": "The FDIC provides a wealth of resources for consumers, bankers, analysts, and other stakeholders. Browse our collection of financial education materials, data tools, documentation of laws and regulations, information on important initiatives, and more.", "wikipage": "AML Topic 128"}, {"content": "Additional FDIC Resources Consumer Resource Center Banker Resource Center Deposit Insurance Supervision & Examinations", "wikipage": "AML Topic 128"}, {"content": "Resources The FDIC provides a wealth of resources for consumers, bankers, analysts, and other stakeholders... Community Banking Research Program", "wikipage": "AML Topic 128"}], "long_answer": "The FDIC provides a variety of resources for stakeholders including financial education materials, data tools, documentation of laws and regulations, and information on important initiatives.\n\nBankers can find specific resources related to deposit insurance and supervision in the Banker Resource Center provided by the FDIC.\n\nThe FDIC offers the Community Banking Research Program as part of its resources to support community banking research."}], "sample_id": "aml-topic-128-2", "question": "What types of resources does the FDIC provide for stakeholders such as consumers and bankers?", "docs": [{"id": "doc-aml-topic-128-2-1", "title": "AML Topic 128 Part 1", "text": "2025\nMillennium Bank, Des Plaines, Ill. Assumes All Deposits of Pulaski Savings\u2026\nPODCASTS / January 06, 2025\nSmall Business Lending\nResources\nToggle submenu\nResources\nThe FDIC provides a wealth of resources for consumers, bankers, analysts, and other stakeholders. Browse our collection of financial education materials, data tools, documentation of laws and regulations, information on important initiatives, and more.\nAdditional FDIC Resources\nConsumer Resource Center\nBanker Resource Center\nDeposi", "score": 0.9, "summary": "2025 Millennium Bank, Des Plaines, Ill. Assumes All Deposits of Pulaski Savings\u2026 PODCASTS / January 06, 2025 Small Business Lending Resources Toggle s...", "extraction": "The FDIC provides a wealth of resources for consumers, bankers, analysts, and other stakeholders. Browse our collection of financial education materials, data tools, documentation of laws and regulations, information on important initiatives, and more."}], "answer": "The FDIC provides a variety of resources for stakeholders including financial education materials, data tools, documentation of laws and regulations, and information on important initiatives. Bankers can find specific resources related to deposit insurance and supervision in the Banker Resource Center provided by the FDIC. The FDIC offers the Community Banking Research Program as part of its resources to support community banking research.", "output": "Answer: The FDIC provides a wealth of resources for consumers, bankers, analysts, and other stakeholders [1].", "intermediate": ["[Retrieval]", "Answer: The FDIC provides a wealth of resources for consumers, bankers, analysts, and other stakeholders."]}, {"qa_pairs": [{"context": "No context provided", "question": "What kind of research tools and reports does the FDIC provide?", "short_answers": ["Center for Financial Research", "FDIC National Survey of Unbanked and Underbanked Households"], "wikipage": null}, {"context": "No context provided", "question": "What are some of the events where FDIC-insured institutions' financial performance was reported?", "short_answers": ["February 25, 2025", "Net Income of $65.4 Billion"], "wikipage": null}, {"context": "No context provided", "question": "How can one stay updated with the latest FDIC news and activities?", "short_answers": ["FDIC announcements", "Policy changes for banks"], "wikipage": null}], "wikipages": [{"title": "AML Topic 128", "url": "https://www.fdic.gov/banker-resource-center/information-technology-it-and-cybersecurity"}], "annotations": [{"knowledge": [], "long_answer": "The FDIC provides research tools and reports such as the Center for Financial Research, Consumer Research, FDIC National Survey of Unbanked and Underbanked Households, Quarterly Banking Profile, FDIC Academic Challenge, FDIC Banking Issues in Focus, and the Annual Risk Review. The financial performance of FDIC-insured institutions was reported at events on February 25, 2025, December 12, 2024, and September 05, 2024, where metrics such as return on assets and net income were discussed. To stay updated with the latest FDIC news and activities, one can follow FDIC announcements, read speeches and testimony on banking issues, learn about policy changes for banks, and get details on conferences and events."}, {"knowledge": [{"content": "More FDIC Analysis Center for Financial Research Consumer Research FDIC National Survey of Unbanked and Underbanked Households Quarterly Banking Profile FDIC Academic Challenge FDIC Banking Issues in Focus Annual Risk Review", "wikipage": "AML Topic 128"}, {"content": "EVENT / February 25, 2025 FDIC-Insured Institutions Reported Return on Assets of 1.11 Percent and Net Inc\u2026 EVENT / December 12, 2024 FDIC-Insured Institutions Reported Net Income of $65.4 Billion EVENT / September 05, 2024 FDIC-Insured Institutions Reported Net Income of $71.5 Billion", "wikipage": "AML Topic 128"}, {"content": "The FDIC publishes regular updates on news and activities. Keep up with FDIC announcements, read speeches and testimony on the latest banking issues, learn about policy changes for banks, and get the details on upcoming conferences and events.", "wikipage": "AML Topic 128"}], "long_answer": "The FDIC provides research tools and reports such as the Center for Financial Research, Consumer Research, FDIC National Survey of Unbanked and Underbanked Households, Quarterly Banking Profile, FDIC Academic Challenge, FDIC Banking Issues in Focus, and the 