etters, and various media campaigns.\n\nIn February 2025, FDIC-insured institutions reported a return on assets of 1.11 percent."}], "sample_id": "aml-topic-137-3", "question": "What type of research tools and reports does the FDIC provide for financial analysis?", "docs": [{"id": "doc-aml-topic-137-3-1", "title": "AML Topic 137 Part 1", "text": "formance data. Browse our extensive research tools and reports.\nMore FDIC Analysis\nCenter for Financial Research\nConsumer Research\nFDIC National Survey of Unbanked and Underbanked Households\nQuarterly Banking Profile\nFDIC Academic Challenge\nFDIC Banking Issues in Focus\nAnnual Risk Review\nEVENT / February 25, 2025\nFDIC-Insured Institutions Reported Return on Assets of 1.11 Percent and Net Inc\u2026\nEVENT / December 12, 2024\nFDIC-Insured Institutions Reported Net Income of $65.4 Billion\nEVENT / Septemb", "score": 0.9, "summary": "formance data. Browse our extensive research tools and reports. More FDIC Analysis Center for Financial Research Consumer Research FDIC National Surve...", "extraction": "formance data. Browse our extensive research tools and reports. More FDIC Analysis Center for Financial Research Consumer Research FDIC National Survey of Unbanked and Underbanked Households Quarterly Banking Profile FDIC Academic Challenge FDIC Banking Issues in Focus Annual Risk Review"}], "answer": "The FDIC provides extensive research tools and reports including the Center for Financial Research, Consumer Research, the FDIC National Survey of Unbanked and Underbanked Households, the Quarterly Banking Profile, the FDIC Academic Challenge, FDIC Banking Issues in Focus, and the Annual Risk Review. The FDIC publishes regular updates on news and activities through various channels including announcements, speeches, testimony, policy changes, conferences, and events. In February 2025, FDIC-insured institutions reported a return on assets of 1.", "output": "Answer: The FDIC provides a variety of research tools and reports 